{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls","id":1479169,"title":"Have you guys ever made a deviant the Renegades character based on magical girls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-20T07:20:57-07:00","id":1479169,"title":"Have you guys ever made a deviant the Renegades character based on magical girls?","content":"You may share your other crazy character concepts if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27338-dragonhunter5684","name":"Dragonhunter5684","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T07:28:02-07:00","id":1479170,"title":"","content":"Magical Girls. That\u2026sounds unnervingly plausible as a character concept lol<br /> <br /> But my system mastery for Deviant is weak ATM, so I\u2019ll sadly have to pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T10:12:38-07:00","id":1479176,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a great idea! But no I haven\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T11:22:59-07:00","id":1479179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1479170#post1479170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magical Girls. That\u2026sounds unnervingly plausible as a character concept lol<br /> <br /> But my system mastery for Deviant is weak ATM, so I\u2019ll sadly have to pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>EIther in the announcement or the kickstarter, I've got a post that actually dug into how a lot of the genre pieces line up really well with Deviant, in particularly a whole bunch of the subversive stuff that came post-codification, along with a list of things just off the top of my head that proved the point. It's hilariously compatible.<br /> <br /> (of course, part of that is how a lot of Deviant's sources are also superhero adjacent, and Magical Girls have a lot of adjacency to that- a cynical and incomplete take of the genre is Superheroes with the feminine-as-merchandising and maybe some actual feminism if you're lucky, but we're getting side tracked here.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337213#post1337213\">scratching of the surface</a> I mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-12-2023, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T19:22:29-08:00","id":1502804,"title":"","content":"I've only seen the manga in Books a Million, I haven't read it but isn't the premise of &quot;Magical Girl Apocalypse&quot; that magical girls are created by the military industrial complex? Doesn't that story line fit well in the Chronicles of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:51:35-08:00","id":1502876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1502804#post1502804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only seen the manga in Books a Million, I haven't read it but isn't the premise of &quot;Magical Girl Apocalypse&quot; that magical girls are created by the military industrial complex? Doesn't that story line fit well in the Chronicles of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more directly it's antecedent Magical Girl Site, but yeah-but there's a long history of dark subversion of the genre coming at it from angles pretty well adjacent to that starting location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:16:32-08:00","id":1502889,"title":"","content":"Puella Magi Madoka Magica might work as a Deviant magical girl game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T07:55:44-08:00","id":1503030,"title":"","content":"It is disturbingly easy to subvert the Magical Girls genre for use in a Deviants game; the <i>real </i>challenge is to play them as straight as possible while still fitting the game's themes and mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T05:42:55-07:00","id":1550587,"title":"","content":"I think the magical girl concept can work only if the whole chronicle is based on it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise if your character in the only &quot;magical girl&quot; in the party, I think it may result a bit out of contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T14:41:19-07:00","id":1550916,"title":"","content":"One of my Deviant Character Ideas is a Cyborg inspired by Urgot from League of Legends, the Talos Pain &amp; Chronos Parasite Engines from WH40K, Warren from The Surge, Serial Designations N, J &amp; V from Murder Drones, and other such individuals across media.<br /> <br /> The basic idea being that the conspiracy that put them through the Divergence did so in an attempt to create a new sort of industrial worker-drone, utilising the dynamic fuzzy-logic problem solving of organic wetware, the brute-force computational solutions of available software, the physical improvements of technological hardware and a bevy of subliminally hypnotic indoctrination firmware to allow for a loyal workforce that could, and would, work for however long was necessary on whatever tasks were required of them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the control system wasn't as perfect as they thought it was, allowing my character to go through a Lancer NHP style 'Cascade' of thinking their way out of the restraints on their mind, and subsequently demonstrating that their custom-made industrial equipment was equally viable as effective, if occasionally unwieldy, weaponry. Cue them breaking out of the conspiracy's facility and making like a roadrunner for the hills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T20:39:06-07:00","id":1554635,"title":"","content":"something something <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/PrincessTheHopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: The Hopeful</a>.<br /> <br /> There is a surprising amount of compatibility between Magical Girls and CoD if you take a lot of Magical Girl tropes and look at them critically or examine implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T22:29:12-07:00","id":1554636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1550587#post1550587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the magical girl concept can work only if the whole chronicle is based on it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise if your character in the only &quot;magical girl&quot; in the party, I think it may result a bit out of contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> There's something to it as, as a genre, Magical Girls are related to Sentai, so a bunch of their native tropes work better in a group of similar warriors. But just as in this genre, you can play a lot with what the group is about and how it is built, and &quot;similarity&quot; doesn't have to mean everyone is a Magical Girl.<br /> <br /> But sure, it won't work in any group. They must have some common ground and reason to work together, and most MGs will be more idealistic/committed to a higher calling than just opportunists. But again, you can have that in a variety of groups.<br /> <br /> In fact you can play straight a Magical Girl in any CoD splat with some effort and alongside other types of characters, although I do agree Deviant eases the process a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554635#post1554635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something something <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/PrincessTheHopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: The Hopeful</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think most people here knows or even played Princess. It doesn't really engages with the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T14:37:28-07:00","id":1554670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554636#post1554636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact you can play straight a Magical Girl in any CoD splat with some effort and alongside other types of characters, although I do agree Deviant eases the process a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, for example, a fan-made Hunter Conspiracy that serves the dual role of being a &quot;crossover splat&quot; with Changeling and being a a Magical Girl splat.<br /> <br /> I could also see a Mage Legacy or a Changeling Entitlement based on Magical Girl tropes.<br /> <br /> Geist's focus on Death would make for a particularly morbid take on the Magical Girl genre; but the Sin-Eater aspect of the game makes it almost as suitable for handling Magical Girl themes as Mage and Changeling.<br /> <br /> Werewolf would be a bit more of a stretch; though if you lean into the &quot;lycanthropy as an analogy to the physical and emotional chaos of teenagers&quot; option, I could see that working as well.<br /> <br /> The next one I'd look at would be Demon, with its &quot;techgnostic espionage against the amoral God-Machine&quot; angle. Think Penny from RWBY as inspiration.<br /> <br /> That leaves Vampire, Promethean, Mummy, and Beast as the ones that would be hardest to make work. Beast would probably be the hardest, as it's very nearly the &quot;anti-Magical Girl&quot; gameline: its whole premise is about subverting the sorts of tropes and themes that a played-straight a Magical Girl would likely feature. Of the other three\u2026 I'm not sure how I'd rank them.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm awaiting the release of Black Vans, which introduces a set of Greater and Lesser Forms allowing you to simulate the other denizens of the CoD, as well as rules for things like Emergent Superheroes. With those tools in hand, one could use Deviant to do all of the above, and even a &quot;genuine&quot; Inner Light infused Princess. But that's kind of cheating.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Fixed Minor typo 01-11-2026, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T19:32:41-07:00","id":1554677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554670#post1554670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves Vampire, Promethean, Mummy, and Beast as the ones that would be hardest to make work. Beast would probably be the hardest, as it's very nearly the &quot;anti-Magical Girl&quot; gameline: its while premise is about subverting the sorts of tropes and themes that a played-straight a Magical Girl would likely feature. Of the other three\u2026 I'm not sure how I'd rank them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire would be rather context-specific, but since they're still born-human I think it wouldn't be particularly hard. It would be closer to some Magical Girls in the sense that their status as such has less to do with the nature of their powers and more with their personal proclivities. That said, you can always have a Magical Girl Bloodline, shouldn't be hard to do.<br /> <br /> Promethean and Mummy would in fact be trickier. It's relatively easy to make a Promethean Role or a few work for this, it would be harder to make a whole Pilgrimage. But still not unfeasible. The greatest challenge would maybe be to figure out how to either build a Promethean to be a Magical Girl or to recruit them for this.<br /> <br /> Mummy shouldn't be particularly hard now that I think about it. You may have a group that already worked similar to Magical Girls back in Irem, or since the First Sothic Turn after it. As long as the Judges &quot;approve&quot; enough of their approach, or even demand it, a chronicle should run just fine. In fact, it may be said that Sailor Moon were already very Mummy-adjacent.<br /> <br /> But I agree about Beast. I still think it can be worked with, but that would be a rather particular Beast to work as a played-straight MG. But since it also works well with other splats, such a unique Beast could work within a mixed-splat or other-splat group of Magical Girls. Making an all-Beast Magical Girls group would be probably the most contrived here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T22:14:06-07:00","id":1554714,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it some more, I wonder about the possibility of something Salubri-like as the basis for Vampiric Magical Girls? As far as I know, VtR doesn't have anything like the Salubri; but perhaps something like a new Bloodline or mini-Covenant could be invented for the purpose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typo 01-11-2026, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T22:30:47-07:00","id":1554717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554714#post1554714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it some more, I wonder about the possibility of something Salubri-like as the basis for Vampiric Magical Girls? As far as I know, VtR doesn't have anything like there Salubri; but perhaps something like a new Bloodline or mini-Covenant could be invented for the purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would work, yes. The Salubri do hit a lot of points for a Magical Girl story, and while most people like to twist the Salubri, straight-played Salubri is pretty much straight-played Magical Girl.<br /> <br /> Both Covenant, Bloodline or a combination would be an interesting option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T05:24:04-07:00","id":1554720,"title":"","content":"After some research, I found the Septemi, a Daeva Bloodline that's addicted to their higher selves, to the point that they're compelled to fulfill their Virtue. They're Christians of the &quot;love your neighbor as yourself&quot; variety, directly opposed to the Lancea Sanctum and its &quot;God's terrorists&quot; philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T12:30:10-07:00","id":1554739,"title":"","content":"And you're right about Prometheans and Mummies: a &quot;played straight magical girl&quot; could be achieved by leaning into the Pilgrimage or Apotheosis, respectively. <br /> <br /> For the Promethean, look at each of the Refinements through the lens of what would be appropriate for a Magical Girl: for instance, the Refinement of Aurum deals with social interactions; a Promethean Magical Girl on that Refinement would lean into the &quot;friendship is magic&quot; tropes. Ferrum deals with the body; and a Promethean Magical Girl on that Refinement would seek to develop her own physical capabilities so as to better be able to help people. On the Refinement of Aes, she'd seek ways to build a team of Magical Girls; on the Refinement of Argentum, she'd seek to learn about the monsters that she's defending humanity against. The Refinement of Mercurius lets her determine what it is that empowers her. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T04:51:24-08:00","id":1557413,"title":"","content":"Isn't the premise of Deviant supposed to be that the experiment went wrong somehow, or left the subject deeply traumatized?<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I've got few ideas you could draw inspiration from:<br /> <br /> <b>Magical Girl Raising Project - </b>A series in which 17 candidates are given magical girl powers, and forced to compete in a free for all battle to the death. The winner is allowed to keep their powers, while the losers die horribly at the hands of their fellow contestants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Madoka Magica</b> - A mysterious entity finds young girls to grant magical powers to, so that they can protect the world from evil witches. But unbeknownst to them, the plan is to have them get killed on the job, as part of a ritual sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Magical Girl</b> - A two page comic made by e254e, in which a mad scientist creates a wand that is supposed to grant the wielder the powers of the 'celestial rabbit.' After leaving it out for some innocent girl to find as part of a test run, it's revealed that the wand may not be able to differentiate between clothing and flesh. So during the transformation sequence, when the girl's undergoes the common trope of having her clothes explode off her body, she also finds herself being skinned alive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T07:35:18-08:00","id":1557417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1557413#post1557413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the premise of Deviant supposed to be that the experiment went wrong somehow, or left the subject deeply traumatized?</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of Deviant is that the powers of the transformed come with metaphysical damage to the soul that messes with their ability to maintain normal relationships and supernaturally reinforces various issues (at best giving them drawbacks to any powers that manifest at the same time).<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking they're the bleeding edge of various supernatural development methods, such that they're not &quot;perfected&quot; versions of whatever made them what they are, but conspiracies make deviants on purpose to largely predictable outcomes with some regularity (albeit finding successful candidates without a lot of horrific failures or a long span of careful testing is a rarity) and supplements have made it clear that it is nevertheless quite possible for a deviant to acclimate to their state to such a degree that they have powerful Variations entangled with minor Scars and a number of methods of mitigating Instability even if they haven't become Guardians or Furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to finish a parenthetical clause. 01-09-2026, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T08:39:28-08:00","id":1557944,"title":"","content":"I created a DtR character that was basically She-Ra. Not exactly &quot;magical girl&quot; in the strict Japanese trope sense, but close. Never got to play her though. It's hard to find people to game DtR with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T09:11:33-07:00","id":1562226,"title":"","content":"Trying to build something here. A cross-splat Magical Girl group and Chronicle with included guidelines for participation of every splat. It may work as a Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo alternative to the Contagion Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Rules:<br /> - Genre played straight, not parody/subversion;<br /> - CofD played straight, this is not an adaptation;<br /> - Stretching genre into darker themes is valid;<br /> - Breaking genre against darker themes, is not;<br /> - Empowerment fantasy core;<br /> - Main struggle: dual life vs emotional sincerity;<br /> - Upbeat not mandatory, but compatibility is.<br /> <br /> Classic References:<br /> Mah\u014d no Princess Mink\u012b Momo<br /> Bish\u014djo Senshi Sailor Moon<br /> Cardcaptor Sakura<br /> Pretty Cure Series<br /> <br /> Genre Testers (they may look like mockery or parody, but are played straight):<br /> Princess Tutu<br /> Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo Lyrical Nanoha<br /> Senki Zessh\u014d Symphogear<br /> Flip Flappers<br /> Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo ni Akogarete<br /> <br /> Litmus Tests (they legitimately straddle the line and are partly genre breakers, but reaffirm the genre's values in the end and through contrast with a full deconstruction -&gt; reconstruction cycle):<br /> Y\u016bki Y\u016bna wa Y\u016bsha de Aru<br /> Puella Magi Madoka Magica<br /> <br /> Counter References (those works misrepresent the genre):<br /> Magical Girl Raising Project<br /> Magical Girl Site<br /> Magical Girl Spec-Ops Asuka<br /> Any isekai of Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo in a Grimdark world<br /> <br /> Genre staples checklist:<br /> 1\ufe0f\u20e3 Weaponized Femininity<br /> - [ ] Accessories as itens of power<br /> - [ ] Vanity legitimated without &quot;glory/honor&quot;<br /> - [ ] Cute, Feminine and Romantic motifs<br /> - [ ] Emotional engagement<br /> 2\ufe0f\u20e3 Coming of Age<br /> - [ ] 10 - 14 years old protagonists<br /> - [ ] Oni-like adult villains (preferably women)<br /> - [ ] Mature-adjacent Alter-Ego<br /> - [ ] Mundane life milestones discussed (school, work, marriage)<br /> 3\ufe0f\u20e3 Empowerment<br /> - [ ] Scepter as soft symbol of authority<br /> - [ ] Rebellion against imposed roles<br /> - [ ] Transformation granting autonomy<br /> - [ ] Idealism validated<br /> 4\ufe0f\u20e3 Relationships and Emotion<br /> - [ ] Bonds and friendship between women<br /> - [ ] Hope and dreams can prevail and heal<br /> - [ ] Magic is positive personal expression<br /> - [ ] Emotional sincerity as source of Strength<br /> 5\ufe0f\u20e3 Superhero Core<br /> - [ ] Compact of \u5909\u8eab\u30d2\u30ed\u30a4\u30f3 and superpowers<br /> - [ ] Secret Identity - Dual Life tension<br /> - [ ] Extraordinary duty to protect Humanity<br /> - [ ] Otherworldly Cute Mascot<br /> <br /> Observation: male characters have gender roles and expectations challenged in the genre. For important NPCs they must be few, but as PCs the arc of finding validation of &quot;feminine&quot; virtues or interests is valid.<br /> <br /> For now I'm structuring the basics as per above, some ideas I have already:<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udffaMummies: possibly the original group, it was formed in Irem before the ritual. Members may have split or joined through the ages.<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udf16 Werewolf: build an example totem, maybe a Lodge.<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udf77 Vampire: a MG Covenant, in its center there may be a MG Bloodline.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\uddff Mage: Rotes galore, maybe a Legacy.<br /> <br /> \u26d3\ufe0f\u200d\ud83d\udca5 Changeling: new Court Systems, maybe?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udddd\ufe0f Geist: what this Krewe would look like?<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udfad Demon: an Agency with strict rules on Pact, but also a system in place to help with Covers.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udca4 Beast: Horrors themed around monstrous femininity.<br /> <br /> \u2623\ufe0f Deviant: at least one Conspiracy is making Magical Girls on purpose.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Promethean: how this Pilgrimage can look like? How to settle a mundane life without causing a Wasteland?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udeab Hunter: a Hunter Conspiracy, Endowments, support for supernaturals struggling to do well rather than focus on destruction.<br /> <br /> What is the Transformation? How's the item that induces it? Is it common for all, specific by Splat, or are there numerous ways?<br /> <br /> Who are the villains? Who's the ultimate villainess? How each splat contributes evil doers?<br /> <br /> How some greater powers and factions react to the whole idea? Covenants, Orders, True Fae, Chthonic Gods, Judges of Du'at, God-Machine, Heroes, Conspiracies, Qashmalin? Exploring the possible reactions of known entities and new ones.<br /> <br /> I can't really devote much to this project right now, but am throwing seeds anyone can discuss or use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T22:04:35-07:00","id":1563209,"title":"","content":"I intend to get around to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>' proposal a bit later. But first, since this is the <b>aa</b> forum:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Princesses among the Deviants</b></span><br /> Princesses, known among themselves as the Hopeful, are individuals whose intense passions and empathy have caused them to Blossom, unlocking magical powers fueled by the Light. They fight a desperate, largely unseen war against the All-Consuming Darkness\u2014an omnipresent metaphysical force that feeds on human fear, spawning monsters and corrupting souls. Divided into the Radiant and Twilight Courts, the Hopeful must balance their mundane lives with their supernatural duties, donning magical Regalia to battle the creatures of the dark.<br /> <b>Threat Level:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Themes</b></span><br /> <i>Princess: The Hopeful</i> explores what it means to hold onto empathy and hope in a world ruled by fear and isolation. Like Renegades, the Hopeful are transformed individuals who must carefully navigate their mundane lives alongside their supernatural reality, relying heavily on Touchstones to keep their volatile souls intact. The tragic slide of a Deviant into End Stage Instability perfectly mirrors a Princess whose Belief drops to zero, transforming her into a horrific, irredeemable monster known as a Dethroned.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Allies</b></span><br /> Radiant Princesses are naturally empathetic and driven to help victims of abuse, exploitation, and despair. They make staunch allies for Renegades, often viewing the Broken as wounded souls in need of healing and protection from the conspiracies that abused them. A cohort might find a Princess to be a tireless (if occasionally naive) defender against their mutual enemies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Enemies</b></span><br /> A cohort whose pursuit of vengeance causes massive collateral damage, or who preys on innocents to survive, will quickly draw the ire of Radiant Guardians. Meanwhile, Twilight Nemeses might target Deviants whose chaotic powers or monstrous Scars trigger their Victim Profiles, viewing the Broken as tainted aberrations of the Darkness that must be violently purged.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Web of Pain</b></span><br /> The Twilight Courts operate seamlessly as conspiracies within the Web of Pain. The Court of Tears runs authoritarian, bureaucratic Enclaves to tax hope and resources from the populace; the Court of Storms fields ruthless paramilitary cults to annihilate any perceived taint of the Darkness; and the Court of Mirrors builds narcissistic mystery cults around their True Heirs. They readily create, recruit, or exploit the Remade to serve as foot soldiers, lab rats, or weapons, seeing them as expendable tools in their cosmic wars.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Greater Form: Princess</b></span><br /> The creature is one of the Hopeful, a magical being driven by intense passions. Anchored entirely by extremes of love and hate, she exists in a volatile spiritual state, locked into either the Radiant or Twilight Courts.<ul><li><b>Supernatural Potency (Inner Light):</b> Dictates maximum Attribute ratings, caps Wisp capacity, and serves as Supernatural Tolerance. <b>Sensitivity Drawback:</b> Witnessing suffering, cruelty, or Pure Darkness triggers a mental or physical attack. The Princess must roll Inner Light; failure generates <b>Shadows</b> (Instability), which erode her magic and well-being.</li> <li><b>Fuel Trait (Wisps):</b> Motes of positive emotion and magical energy. Maximum capacity equals Inner Light. Spend 1 Wisp to reflexively fuel <b>Defiance (Holy Shield)</b> to downgrade or negate incoming damage. She may spend unlimited Wisps per turn. <i>Regain Wisps via:</i> <b>Call of Duty</b> (meaningfully furthering Calling duties), <b>Inner Strength</b> (spending Willpower in immediate danger, or reflexively converting unspent Willpower), or <b>Circle of Light</b> (socializing with friends and family).</li> <li><b>Integrity Trait (Belief):</b> Starting at 7 (or 8 for a Onceborn), Belief is a three-tiered track measuring moral conviction: <b>Paragon (10-8)</b>, <b>Idealist (7-4)</b>, and <b>Pragmatist (3-1)</b>. Faltering against Touchstones triggers a Belief Compromise, risking Belief damage, Shadows, and negative Conditions. Failing to further a Touchstone in a chapter inflicts a minor Instability.</li> <li><b>Virtue and Vice (Drive and Dread):</b> Due to her inherently empathetic and driven nature, a Princess retains a Baseline's Virtue and Vice, often reframed as Drive and Dread. <b>These supplement her Loyalty and Conviction rather than replacing them.</b> Indulging Vice/Dread restores 1 Willpower and heals a minor Instability. Meaningfully upholding Virtue/Drive despite danger restores all Willpower and heals a minor or medium Instability.</li> <li><b>End Stage (The Dethroned):</b> If Belief reaches 0, Inner Light gutters out into a cold, silent absence. The Princess reverts to her mundane identity, loses all powers, and sheds one Willpower dot per hour as her soul disintegrates. Reaching 0 Willpower triggers a final, horrific transformation into an irredeemable monster of the Darkness known as the Dethroned.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Courts</b></span><br /> Princesses must align with the Radiant or Twilight Courts, functioning as Guardians or Nemeses. In this state of spiritual equilibrium, she regains one extra Willpower per day (even without restful sleep), ignores automatic minor Instabilities at story start, and automatically heals one minor Instability at chapter start.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Radiant Guardians</b></span><br /> Function in a state of <b>Catharsis</b>; Loyalty outweighs Conviction.<ul><li><b>Touchstones:</b> Begins with more Loyalty than Conviction.</li> <li><b>The Fall:</b> If Conviction ever equals or exceeds active Loyalty, she loses Catharsis and Falters on her Loyalty Touchstones. She spirals toward becoming Feral (The Dethroned) unless she seeks refuge in a Twilight conspiracy.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Twilight Nemeses</b></span><br /> Function in a state of <b>Fury</b>; Conviction outweighs Loyalty.<ul><li><b>Touchstones:</b> Begins with more Conviction than Loyalty. Purging targets heals her soul; showing mercy inflicts Instability.</li> <li><b>The Redemption:</b> If active Loyalty ever equals or exceeds Conviction, she loses Fury and Falters on her Conviction Touchstones. As toxic hatreds break, new bonds of Loyalty catch her, allowing a safe transition back to Radiant Catharsis.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Lesser Forms</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Calling</b></span><br /> Defines her approach to fighting the Darkness. With the Charms Form, grants an affinity for three Charm families. With the Transformation Lesser Form, she gains a free Transformed Attribute dot. By itself, the Form grants Sacred Code if Radiant or Victim Profile if Twilight.<ul><li><b>Champion:</b> +1 Strength or Resolve. <i>Affinities:</i> Bless, Fight, Perfect.<ul><li><i>Radiant Code:</i> Defend the weak, shun violence for personal gain, never back down.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Tears):</i> Operates outside Alhambra's law, hoards hope/resources, actively resists Tithe collection.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Storms):</i> Operates outside Twilight authority, bears Darkness taint, harmed an innocent.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Mirrors):</i> Rival for leadership, criticized the Princess's combat prowess, refuses to submit to her &quot;protection.&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Grace:</b> +1 Presence or Composure. <i>Affinities:</i> Bless, Connect, Govern.<ul><li><i>Radiant Code:</i> Take responsibility, uplift others, never magically manipulate.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Tears):</i> Mundane authority figure, resisted the Princess, refuses emotional tribute to Alhambra.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Storms):</i> Preaches peace or compromise, associated with a target of the Princess's wrath, obstructs the crusade.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Mirrors):</i> Social influencer, ignored the Princess, refuses to acknowledge her as the True Heir.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Mender:</b> +1 Intelligence or Dexterity. <i>Affinities:</i> Perfect, Restore, Shape.<ul><li><i>Radiant Code:</i> Provide requested aid, mitigate suffering, never harm a patient.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Tears):</i> Member of a rival Court, wastes magical resources, threatens Alhambra's infrastructure.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Storms):</i> Cultist, corrupted physiology, inflicted structural damage.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Mirrors):</i> Offers aid to others instead of the Princess, refused the Princess's &quot;healing&quot;, shows independence.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Seeker:</b> +1 Intelligence or Wits. <i>Affinities:</i> Appear, Govern, Learn.<ul><li><i>Radiant Code:</i> Seek truth, never cover up wrongdoing, accept no unsolvable mystery.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Tears):</i> Conceals forbidden truths, rebel cell member, lies to the Princess.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Storms):</i> Hides creatures of Darkness, uses stealth/deception to avoid the crusade, bears a Dark taint.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Mirrors):</i> Uncovered the Princess's flaws, refuses to believe the Princess's narrative, spreads &quot;lies&quot; about the True Heir.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Troubadour:</b> +1 Presence or Dexterity. <i>Affinities:</i> Appear, Inspire, Shape.<ul><li><i>Radiant Code:</i> Awaken audiences, eschew ego-driven art, never cease creating.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Tears):</i> Inspires hope in the Rebellious Provinces, refuses to surrender Wisps to Alhambra, openly joyful.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Storms):</i> Creates art depicting peace/mercy, distracts the Sworn Guard, associated with the Darkness.</li> <li><i>Victim Profile (Mirrors):</i> Mocked the Princess, rival agent, steals the spotlight.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Charms</b></span><br /> This Form grants access to four Charms (Scar-free Magnitude 2 Variations). If the character possesses the Calling Lesser Form, her four free Charms must be chosen from among her Calling's Affinities, and improving them or purchasing new Affinity Charms costs only 2 Experiences per Magnitude. Without a Calling, her free Charms can be chosen without restriction, but all Charms cost the standard 3 Experiences per Magnitude to improve or purchase.<ul><li><b>Appear (Illusions &amp; Stealth):</b> Camouflage, Face Thief, Holographic Projection, Shadow Selves.</li> <li><b>Bless (Enhancements &amp; Luck):</b> Blessing, Hyper-Competence, Superhuman Attribute.</li> <li><b>Connect (Social bonds &amp; Manipulation):</b> Fate-Bind, Pheromones, Psycho-Onomastics, Telepathy.</li> <li><b>Fight (Combat prowess):</b> Carapace, Lash, Kiai (Buster/Deadly Ichor).</li> <li><b>Govern (Supernatural control &amp; Wards):</b> Fate's Agent, Occult Singularity, Otherworldly Connection, Soul Seer.</li> <li><b>Inspire (Crowd control &amp; Emotion):</b> Delude, Emotion Amplification, Vocalization.</li> <li><b>Learn (Senses &amp; Knowledge):</b> Clairvoyance, Internet Acuity, Precognition, Shadows of the Past, Specialized Sense.</li> <li><b>Perfect (Movement &amp; Self-defense):</b> Aquatic, Brachiation, Enhanced Speed, Environmental Adaptation, Flight, Immunity.</li> <li><b>Restore (Healing &amp; Purging):</b> Absorb Instability, Healer, Rapid Healing.</li> <li><b>Shape (Elements &amp; Matter):</b> Aerokinesis, Conjuration, Cryokinesis, Electrokinesis, Hydrokinesis, Matter Control, Matter Emulation, Mechanical Transformation, Plant Control, Pyrokinesis, Terrakinesis.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Transformation &amp; Secret Identity</b></span><br /> The Princess possesses a Phylactery, a physical representation of her Belief.<ul><li><b>The Transformation:</b> Instant action once per scene (or reflexive with 1 Wisp/exceptional success). Grants Transformed Traits and Regalia. Bypasses the risk to her Secret Identity when using Charms.</li> <li><b>Transformed Traits:</b> Adds Transformed dots to Baseline Attributes/Skills, recalculating Advantages. Transformed Health damage doesn't wrap to mundane Health; Transformed Willpower can only be spent while Transformed. <b>Transformed Traits cost one Experience less than normal.</b> If the character lacks the Greater Form's Inner Light to cap these traits, her maximum Transformed dots across all traits cannot exceed the Magnitude of her Transformation Variation.</li> <li><b>Regalia (Preparation &amp; Catalyst):</b> Magical gear modeled as Variations entangled with the Preparation Scar and Catalyst Deviation. Because Regalia is personalized, it functions as a +2 or +3 Magnitude Catalyst. Catalysts manifest upon Transformation, and <b>can be dismissed and resummoned at will.</b></li> <li><b>Secret Identity:</b> Grants the Secret Identity Merit free. Enemies cannot magically link her personas. Using an Overt Charm or a Subtle Charm (Magnitude 3+) untransformed suppresses this Merit for the chapter.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Invocations</b></span><br /> Once per scene, reflexively apply an Invocation to add its dots to a Charm's activation pool. Applying an Invocation requires the Princess to meet a specific philosophical condition.<ul><li><b>The Radiant Queens:</b><ul><li><i>Acqua (Currents/Diamonds):</i> Requires clear and careful thought.</li> <li><i>Aria (Spades):</i> Requires joy, freedom, or unconventional methods.</li> <li><i>Fuoco (Swords):</i> Requires love and unbridled passion.</li> <li><i>Legno (Flowers/Clubs):</i> Requires harmony, resilience, and finding balance.</li> <li><i>Terra (Jewels/Hearts):</i> Requires building relationships, trust, and society.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Twilight Queens (Conspiracies):</b> Because the Twilight Queens operate as vast conspiracies within the Web of Pain, learning their Invocations also grants (or requires) the <b>Devoted Form (Advanced)</b>.<ul><li><i>Lacrima (Tears):</i> Requires sacrificing others to preserve what is left (Devoted to Alhambra).</li> <li><i>Tempesta (Storms):</i> Requires caustic hatred and merciless destruction of the Darkness (Devoted to the Sworn Guard).</li> <li><i>Specchio (Mirrors):</i> Requires vanity and exalting oneself above all others (Devoted to the Cult of the True Heir).</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Philosophies as Touchstones:</b> Each Invocation acts as a Touchstone; upholding its ideals restores Willpower and heals Shadows. Violating its Ban triggers a Belief Compromise. <b>Without the Transformation Form, Invocation Touchstones take up regular Touchstone slots.</b> If she does possess the Transformation Form, Invocation Touchstones are considered part of the Transformed state and are only accessible while Transformed.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Crawlspace</b></span><br /> Physically enter the Dreamlands through a localized threshold (like a closet) via an extended Inner Light + Empathy + Shadows roll.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Light-Touched</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>New Form Variant: Dedicated (Light-Touched)</b><br /> Used by Beacons and Sworn. The character remains a Baseline and does not Diverge through Instability.<ul><li><b>The Blossoming Trigger:</b> The character only Diverges into a full Princess narratively: by facing a severe crisis, taking personal responsibility, and finding the inner strength to act.</li> <li><b>Crushed Hope:</b> Accumulating too much Instability (dropping to 0 Integrity) crushes their spirit. They lose the Dedicated Form and all magical benefits, reverting to a normal, traumatized Baseline.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>THE BEACONS (Threat 1-2)</b><br /> Everyday humans with a tiny, unconscious spark of the Light.<ul><li><b>Base Form:</b> Dedicated (Light-Touched Variant).</li> <li><b>Adaptation (The Spark of Hope):</b> Once per chapter, when the Beacon spends Willpower in immediate danger or fulfills her Virtue/Drive, she may reset one per-scene/chapter ability.</li> <li><b>Drawback (Sensitivity):</b> Rolls Integrity to resist accumulating Shadows when witnessing cruelty.</li> <li><b>The Quiet Echo:</b> Allies in her immediate presence gain +1 to breaking point rolls caused by fear or despair.</li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Charms (The Spark):</b> Possesses exactly <b>one Charm</b> (Magnitude 1 or 2 Variation) locked into a single, highly specific application. Activates <b>once per scene</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>THE SWORN (Threat 2-3)</b><br /> Mortals formally initiated into the Light to serve the Nobility.<ul><li><b>Base Forms:</b> Dedicated (Light-Touched Variant). Pledging to an authoritarian or highly organized faction grants the <b>Devoted Form</b>.</li> <li><b>Adaptation (Oathbound Magic):</b> Cannot easily fuel his own magic. A Princess may spend her Wisps or use her Adaptation to reset the Sworn's per-scene/chapter features (requires 1 minute of physical contact to confirm his oath). Bequests may have independent reset conditions.</li> <li><b>Drawback (Sensitivity):</b> Rolls Integrity to resist Shadows.</li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Invocations:</b> Gains 1 free dot in his Queen's Invocation, acting as a Touchstone (restores Willpower/risks Integrity). Can be reflexively applied to Charms.</li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Charms (Bequests):</b> Gains 2-4 Charms. <i>Every</i> Charm must use the Preparation (Catalyst) Scar, representing physical magical items. Losing the Bequest removes access to the Charm. Activates <b>once per scene</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>THE SHIKIGAMI (Threat 2-3)</b><br /> Dreamlands spirits bound to physical vessels to mentor Princesses.<ul><li><b>Base Forms (The Vessel):</b> <b>Outsider</b> (Root: Dreamlander), suffering the <i>Awkward</i> trait. Combined with either <b>Automaton</b> (toys/dolls) or <b>Uplift</b> (animals), maintaining Size 1-3 and the physical limitations/Scars of their shell.</li> <li><b>Greater Form: Shikigami (Familiar Spirit)</b><ul><li><i>Supernatural Potency (Reflected Light):</i> Magical limits (Max Charm rating, Transformed traits) are capped by the highest Inner Light among all bonded Princesses.</li> <li><i>Adaptation (Symbiotic Familiar):</i> <b>Once per scene</b>, when a bonded Princess gains a Beat from an Aspiration/Dream, the Shikigami may reset an ability. A Princess may also spend Wisps/use her Adaptation to reset the Shikigami's abilities via 1 minute of physical contact.</li> <li><i>Integrity &amp; Sensitivity:</i> Uses <b>Belief</b> (starts at 8). Suffers Sensitivity with a base pool of 1 die.</li> <li><i>Anchors:</i> One Anchor is focused on the Nakama (an ideal to embody or pitfall to avoid); the second is a personal quirk tied to their vessel.</li> <li><i>Lesser Form: The Bond (Magical Relay):</i> Turns the bonded Nakama into a Dedicated Commonalty for the purposes of targeting Charms.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Shikigami Transformation (Variant):</b> Activates <b>once per scene</b> to gain Transformed Attributes/Skills. <i>Differences:</i> No Phylactery (suffers Stunned Tilt on a dramatic failure instead of losing an item); can purchase Transformed Size dots (1 Merit dot per Size) to scale its tiny vessel up to Size 8.</li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Shikigami Charms (Variant):</b> Activates each Charm <b>once per scene</b>. <i>Differences:</i> Max Charm rating is capped by Reflected Light. A bonded Princess can channel her own Skills and Charms through the familiar by spending Wisps/using her Adaptation to reset the Shikigami's ability for the roll.</li> <li><b>Lesser Form: Crawlspace Guide (Variant):</b> Automatically finds physical thresholds into the Dreamlands. Adds a flat +3 bonus as a secondary actor on teamwork actions when aiding a Princess using her Crawlspace Lesser Form.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T22:23:55-07:00","id":1563210,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Mystery Cult Initiation: Embassies and Protectorates</b></span><br /> Specialized diplomatic or authoritarian cults that alter the character's magic, modeled via the 1-to-5 dot <b>Mystery Cult Initiation</b> Merit.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants basic cult knowledge (a Skill Specialty) and a 1- or 2-dot Merit.</li> <li><b>Consul / Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Recognized authority. Grants Skill dots and 3-dot Merits.</li> <li><b>Ambassador / Regent (Dot 5):</b> The cult's apex. Fundamentally shifts the Princess's magic to command the chosen concept, granting a major advantage not reflected in game traits (encapsulating narrative-altering Privileges).</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Embassies of the Radiant Courts</b></span><br /> Embassies are diplomatic missions to the strange, alien, or mundane concepts of the World of Darkness. Princesses join an Embassy to humanize or redeem its purview, incorporating its magic into themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to the Arcane (The Spooks)</b><br /> A cult of occult investigators, witch-finders, and scholars who monitor the sorcerous and arcane forces of the world.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Occult Specialty in <i>Ritual Magic</i> and the Unseen Sense (Arcane) Merit. The Secretary gains <b>Arcane Shield</b>; she can pinpoint the source of ritual magic and inherently penalizes any arcane rituals targeting her by an amount equal to her Inner Light.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Occult and a 3-dot Library Merit. The Consul can sense lingering magical effects and empowered items, divining their purpose with study. She may also spend 1 Wisp to share her Arcane Shield with an ally.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>The Magic Within Man</b>. By witnessing an Arcane ritual (such as Blood Sorcery or Awakened magic), she can replicate it using her own Wisps and Inner Light in place of the original caster's supernatural fuel and traits.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Childhood (The Governesses)</b><br /> A compassionate cult of teachers and caretakers who nurture and protect the next generation, believing children are the key to a better future.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Empathy Specialty in <i>Children</i> and the True Friend Merit. The Secretary gains a perfect first impression with any child, and can reflexively spend 1 Wisp to upgrade any action taken to protect a child from physical or psychological harm into a Rote action.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Empathy and a 3-dot Allies Merit. The Consul can teach a child a magic word; if the child speaks it, the Consul receives a vision of their location and may spend 1 Wisp to instantly teleport to them.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious</b>. With a touch, the Ambassador may temporarily transfer dots of her own Inner Light and Charms to a child, granting the child the Princess template (using Integrity instead of Belief) so they can defend themselves.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Death (The Reapers)</b><br /> A solemn order that walks the line between the living and the dead, seeking to soothe the grief of mortality and protect the lost souls of the Underworld.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Occult Specialty in <i>Ghosts</i> and the Unseen Sense (Ghosts) Merit. The Secretary can see, hear, and physically interact with ephemeral entities in Twilight. In the face of death or lethal violence, she gains a phantom dot of Composure to keep her cool.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Occult and a 3-dot Contacts (Underworld) Merit. The Consul can touch an Avernian Gate and spend 2 Wisps to open it without a key. She may also spend 1 Wisp to banish all physical pain from a target for a scene.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Flesh without Substance</b>. As a reflexive action, the Ambassador may spend 2 Wisps to shift her physical body into Twilight, becoming completely incorporeal and treating the ephemeral world as solid.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to the Dreamlands (The Daydreamers)</b><br /> A society of lucid dreamers and astral explorers who seek to bridge the gap between the waking world and the collective unconscious.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Survival Specialty in <i>The Dreamlands</i> and the Dream Travel Merit. The Secretary can easily locate Crawlspace entrances and may split her consciousness, sending her Transformed self into the Dreamlands while her Baseline self remains awake (though she suffers a -2 Initiative penalty while divided).</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Survival and a 3-dot Meditative Mind Merit. The Consul can reach into the Dreamlands to pull out physical tools (granting equipment bonuses), and completely ignores the mind-warping effects of the Astral Gales.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Wendy's Boys</b>. The Ambassador overlays the Dreamlands onto reality in a wide radius. Mortals in this &quot;daydreaming zone&quot; gain +1 to Belief/Integrity rolls, and Dreamlanders can materialize for free without suffering Essence bleed.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to the Economy (The Accountants)</b><br /> A cadre of financial investigators and corporate watchdogs who view the flow of money as the lifeblood of human civilization.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Academics Specialty in <i>Finance</i> and the 2-dot Contacts (Corporate) Merit. The Secretary can magically tag a financial transaction; 24 hours later, she divines the Aspirations, Virtues, and structural secrets of the organization that processed the money.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Academics and a 3-dot Resources Merit. The Consul may spend 2 Wisps to divine the exact location of the paper trail, evidence, or whistleblower needed to expose a specific corporate secret to the public.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Shaking Hands with the Invisible Hand</b>. By tagging an organization's funds, the Ambassador can ask the Storyteller direct, specific questions about that organization's future plans and actions, receiving perfectly accurate answers.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Ephemera (The Shamans)</b><br /> A spiritualist circle that acts as diplomats, guardians, and peacekeepers between humanity and the animistic spirits of the Shadow.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Persuasion Specialty in <i>Spirits</i> and the Unseen Sense (Spirits) Merit. The Secretary can see and interact with Twilight spirits, perfectly understands the First Tongue, and perceives local Resonance and Manifestation Conditions automatically.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Persuasion and a 3-dot Allies (Spirits) Merit. The Consul may spend 2 Wisps to impose, alter, or suppress Resonant Conditions in an area, manipulating the local spirit ecology. She may also grant her spiritual sight to others.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Queen of the Spirit World</b>. The Ambassador achieves an honorary Spirit Rank of 3 (or 4 at Inner Light 9). She may declare her Rank to automatically subtract it from the dice pools of any spirit or werewolf attempting to affect her.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Fortune (The Dancers)</b><br /> A whimsical, acrobatic order patronized by a literal cosmic Cat, dedicating themselves to redistributing luck and loading the cosmic dice.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Athletics Specialty in <i>Acrobatics</i> and the Danger Sense Merit. The Secretary senses when destiny or luck is being magically altered. She may spend 1 Wisp to generate minor strokes of highly improbable good luck (finding exactly \\$50 in a trash can, the villain tripping on a shoelace).</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Athletics and the Fast Reflexes 3 Merit. The Consul's Initiative modifier is doubled, and she never takes damage from falling. She may roll twice on any action, saving the discarded result to magically force that exact result onto a future roll.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>It Must Be</b>. The Ambassador can spend 3 Wisps to make every action she takes for the rest of the scene a Rote action. However, cosmic balance demands a toll; for every failure she successfully rerolls, the Storyteller gets to enforce an automatic dramatic failure on her in a future scene.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Lilith (The Dusks)</b><br /> A clandestine network of therapists, blood-sorcery experts, and rehabilitation counselors seeking to save vampires from their Beasts and free their mortal victims.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Empathy Specialty in <i>Addicts</i> and the Unseen Sense (Blood Magic) Merit. The Secretary can track Vitae and identify vampiric Disciplines. Her blood burns vampires, destroying Vitae rather than granting it, and she adds her Inner Light to rolls to resist blood bonds and mind control.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Empathy and the Iron Stamina 3 Merit. The Consul can spend 2 Wisps to chain a frenzying vampire's Beast, imposing severe dice penalties and forcing a strict behavioral Ban on the monster for the duration of the frenzy.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>The Light's Forgotten Kiss</b>. The Ambassador may spend 3 Wisps to grant a vampire a temporary dot of Humanity, reminding them of their mortal soul. However, the Ambassador gains Blood Sympathy to the vampire for the duration.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Machines (The Machinists)</b><br /> A guild of engineers and transhumanists who see the clockwork universe as a thing of awe, blending technology and the Light of Hope.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Crafts Specialty in <i>Electronics</i> and the Interdisciplinary Specialty Merit. The Secretary intuitively understands any complex system, suffering no penalties for using unfamiliar technology, and may lend her Crafts or Science dots to allies for a scene.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Crafts and the Professional Training 3 Merit. By spending 1 Wisp and taking a turn to calibrate a machine, the Consul adds half her Inner Light to its equipment bonus for the rest of the scene.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Magnum Opus</b>. The Ambassador learns to encode the Light of Hope into technology, allowing her to forge permanent Bequests (magical devices) that can be operated by completely mundane Baselines without a Phylactery.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Night (The Night Witches)</b><br /> A secretive, cloaked order that operates under the cover of darkness to dismantle fear, ensuring the night remains a time of peace and rest.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Stealth Specialty in <i>Shadows</i> and the Direction Sense Merit. Under the night sky, the Secretary sees perfectly in pitch darkness and can spend 1 Wisp to veil herself, penalizing all attempts to spot her by an amount equal to her Composure.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Stealth and a 3-dot Anonymity Merit. The Consul adds her Stealth dots to her dice pool whenever she attempts to uncover hidden things or pierce someone else's subterfuge. She may also grant her night vision and veiling to allies.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Midnight Noon</b>. The Ambassador commands the conceptual weight of the sky. For a scene, she dictates how supernatural powers interact with the time of day\u2014making a vampire burn under starlight, or allowing sun-powered magic to function at midnight.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to the Ocean (The Explorers)</b><br /> A vanguard of fearless divers and survivalists pushing the boundaries of the known world, exploring the deepest trenches and harshest environments.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Survival Specialty in <i>Navigation</i> and the Direction Sense Merit. The Secretary can never get lost. In water, she can transform her legs into a mermaid tail, quadrupling her swim speed and gaining underwater echolocation.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Survival and the Multilingual 3 Merit. The Consul's voice becomes a siren song; she may roll to entrance targets, inflicting the Swooning Condition. She may also spend Wisps to grant her mermaid transformation to an ally.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Mermaid's Crown</b>. The Ambassador achieves total immunity to environmental hazards, surviving the Mariana Trench or the vacuum of space with equal ease. She also gains a focused echolocation pulse capable of mapping the molecular density of solid objects or living tissue.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Embassy to Stories (The Godmothers)</b><br /> A theatrical society of bards and reality-hackers who understand that the universe runs on narrative tropes, and seek to weave &quot;happily ever after&quot; into reality.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Expression Specialty in <i>Storytelling</i> and the Unseen Sense (Wyrd) Merit. The Secretary can sense Fae magic. She may also &quot;Enter the Tale&quot;, magically inserting herself into an unfulfilled role in a social structure or narrative to trick reality into accepting her as that role.</li> <li><b>Consul (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Expression and the Alternate Identity 3 Merit. The Consul may &quot;Become the Tale&quot;, shaping dreamstuff into a literal new body that perfectly matches her narrative role, rendering her immune to DNA tests and protecting her from the Thorns of the Hedge.</li> <li><b>Ambassador (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Editing the Tale</b>. The Ambassador may perform Talecrafting once per session, twisting fate, probability, and reality to suit narrative tropes (such as invoking &quot;The Power of Friendship&quot; to defeat an otherwise mathematically superior foe).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Protectorates of the Twilight Courts</b></span><br /> Protectorates are authoritarian extensions of the Queen of Tears' will, maintaining the survival of Alhambra by taxing, manipulating, and policing the Rebellious Provinces (Earth).<br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Amethyst (The Grave Tenders)</b><br /> A somber priesthood that manages Alhambra's dead, officiating funerals and exploiting ghosts to protect the Queen's interests.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Expression Specialty in <i>Funerals</i> and the Medium Merit. The Secretary can invite a ghost to safely possess her body, allowing it to interact with the world, and can generate Essence to feed local ghosts by performing funeral rites.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Expression and a 3-dot Status (Alhambra) Merit. The Governor can consecrate ground to pacify restless spirits, and may magically dissolve physical Bequests to transform them into permanent Numina for a ghost.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Bearing the Burdens of the Dead</b>. The Regent can touch Ghost Princesses (or living allies) to peel away their accumulated Shadows (Instability), storing the corruption inside her own soul to keep them pure, which she can later expel as hostile Darkspawn wraiths.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Blue Topaz (The Playwrights)</b><br /> A clandestine ministry of propaganda and psychological warfare that shapes art, theater, and dreams to enforce absolute loyalty to Alhambra.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Empathy Specialty in <i>Dreams</i> and a 2-dot Retainer (Irim) Merit. The Secretary shapes a piece of her soul into an ephemeral dream-bird (an Irim). She can send the bird into a target's dreams to divine their Virtues, Vices, Aspirations, and mental Conditions.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Empathy and a 3-dot Status (Blue Topaz) Merit. The Governor can send her Irim to lay a &quot;Cuckoo's Egg&quot; in a target's dream, imposing a persistent mental Condition (like Phobia or Obsession) that alters the victim's behavior in the waking world.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Birdhouse in Your Soul</b>. The Regent's Irim can physically possess a dreaming target, overriding their consciousness and turning them into a biological meat-puppet that perfectly acts out the Regent's script.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Fused Quartz (The Sibyls)</b><br /> A terrifying sect of oracles and timeline-manipulators who gaze into the future to ensure Alhambra's survival.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Occult Specialty in <i>Omens</i> and the Danger Sense Merit. The Secretary can enter a trance to ask the Storyteller direct yes/no questions about the future. She may also magically trigger improbable butterfly-effect events to swap the outcomes of two unrelated actions.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Occult and a 3-dot Status (Fused Quartz) Merit. The Governor can accelerate her perception of time during stressful moments; she may treat any mundane instant action as an advanced action, rolling twice and taking the better result.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>So Let It Be Written</b>. The Regent may pronounce a horrifying, unavoidable Doom upon a target. However, achieving this rank curses the Regent herself with an inescapable, fatal Doom that no magic can permanently avert.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Garnet (The Questers)</b><br /> The secret police and internal affairs division of Alhambra, tasked with rooting out treason, inspecting outposts, and ensuring bureaucratic obedience.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants an Intimidation Specialty in <i>Interrogation</i> and a 2-dot Status (Alhambra) Merit. The Secretary may force a target to believe she is their immediate superior, compelling them to answer her questions. She also projects an aura that causes mortals to ignore her trespassing in restricted areas.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Intimidation and a 3-dot Status (Garnet) Merit. The Governor can issue a scathing critique of an official's competence, magically draining their Willpower and forcing them to adopt an Aspiration to fix their mistakes. She may also create magical spies tied to her senses.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Royal Appointment</b>. By defeating a target in a Clash of Wills, the Regent permanently strips the target of their Status dots and claims them for herself, magically brainwashing the entire organization into believing the Regent is their newly appointed boss.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Heliotrope (The Night Audit)</b><br /> A lethal inquisition specializing in the extermination of vampires, hijacking their blood magic, and seizing their mortal thralls to serve Alhambra instead.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Politics Specialty in <i>Vampires</i> and the Unseen Sense (Blood Magic) Merit. The Secretary can track Vitae by scent, and her blood destroys a vampire's Vitae if they attempt to feed on her. She may also hijack existing Blood Bonds or Dominate effects, turning the thrall's loyalty to herself.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Politics and a 3-dot Status (Heliotrope) Merit. The Governor can completely shatter Blood Bonds and Ghouling addictions, reverting Ghouls to normal mortals or converting them directly into Sworn servants of the Queen of Tears.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Queen of the Night</b>. The Regent can impose &quot;Midnight Noon&quot; on an area, forcing supernatural creatures to suffer their daytime weaknesses (such as sunlight lethality) under the night sky. She may also spend her own blood to sustain a Ghoul indefinitely without the need for Vitae.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Malachite (The Redemptionists)</b><br /> A sinister psychological division that functions as Alhambra's confessors, using memory alteration and mind control to &quot;cure&quot; rebellious thoughts.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Persuasion Specialty in <i>Counseling</i> and the Sympathetic Merit. The Secretary can instantly diagnose a target's mental Conditions and Trauma. By offering &quot;confession,&quot; she can magically suppress or cure their psychological conditions, or crush them under the Guilty Condition.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Persuasion and a 3-dot Status (Malachite) Merit. The Governor can sever a target's ties to their past, imposing false memories to replace their old loyalties with absolute devotion to Alhambra. She can also download massive amounts of information directly into a target's brain.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Conversion</b>. The Regent can literally rewrite a person's soul. She may permanently delete one of a target's Aspirations or Touchstones and replace it with a goal of her own choosing. However, doing so magically curses one of the Regent's own Aspirations to constantly fail.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Novaculite (The Drafters)</b><br /> The drill sergeants and military commanders of Alhambra's armies, turning conscripts into fearless, unified killing machines.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Weaponry Specialty in <i>Drill/Training</i> and the Inspiring Merit. The Secretary can magically upload Weaponry, Brawl, or language Skills directly into a recruit's mind for a day. She may also assist allies in resisting Breaking Points via a supernatural teamwork action.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Weaponry and a 3-dot Status (Novaculite) Merit. The Governor can instantly convert entire squads of mortals into Sworn soldiers. She may also bind an organization together, magically increasing their cohesion and Commonalty to the highest possible tier.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Favor of the Last Empress</b>. The Regent can pronounce a royal blessing over an entire army, granting every soldier a massive pool of banked dice to ensure absolute victory in their assigned mission.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Protectorate of Pyrite (The Liaisons)</b><br /> Alhambra's public face, deploying diplomats and negotiators to the outside world to secure resources, establish enclaves, and enforce the Queen's authority.<ul><li><b>Secretary (Dots 1-2):</b> Grants a Socialize Specialty in <i>Etiquette</i> and a floating 2-dot Contacts Merit. The Secretary projects an aura of unquestioned authority that grants her bonuses to social maneuvering, while simultaneously rendering her completely anonymous to those she interacts with.</li> <li><b>Consul/Governor (Dots 3-4):</b> Grants +1 Socialize and a 3-dot Status (Pyrite) Merit. The Governor can spend Wisps to automatically open Doors in social maneuvering without rolling. She may also extend her aura of anonymity and diplomatic immunity to her subordinates and staff.</li> <li><b>Regent (Dot 5):</b> Grants <b>Ask And You Shall Receive</b>. The Regent carries the absolute authority of the Last Empress. With a successful roll, she can command the total obedience of an organization, instantly generating phantom Allies dots that represent her absolute control over their resources.\u200b</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Alhambra, The Last Kingdom</b></span><br /> Alhambra exists in a pocket dimension deep within the Dark World, the only surviving remnant of the fallen Kingdom. To its inhabitants, it is the last bastion of light and civilization, surrounded by an All-Consuming Darkness. Because the city requires an immense amount of magical energy simply to keep its wards active and its streetlamps burning, Alhambra survives as a parasite. Its agents routinely venture into the &quot;Rebellious Provinces&quot; (Earth) to enact the Bleak Harvest\u2014stealing joy, hope, and magical energy from humanity to funnel back to the Last Empress.<br /> <br /> As an <b>Otherworldly Conspiracy (Standing 10)</b>, Alhambra is immune to mundane Baseline interventions. No amount of police raids or journalistic whistleblowing can reach a city hidden in another dimension. Worse, they are inextricably woven into the Web of Pain; Alhambra uses its vast network of Embassies, Protectorates, and mortal cults to manipulate Earth's societies, pit rival conspiracies against one another, and funnel resources back to the Dark World.<br /> <br /> They function primarily as an <b>Acquisitive/Progenitor Conspiracy</b>. They eagerly recruit grieving, lonely individuals, offering them a safe haven from a terrifying world in exchange for absolute loyalty. For those who refuse, Alhambra has no qualms about using force, utilizing mind-altering magic, or deploying their elite Devoted (the Ravens and Sworn Guard) to eliminate threats.<br /> <br /> <b>Conspiracy Traits</b><ul><li><b>Standing:</b> 10 (Otherworldly)</li> <li><b>Principles:</b> Alhambra must survive; there is no price too high; subdue the Rebellious Provinces.</li> <li><b>Virtue:</b> Dedicated (The citizens of Alhambra will endure any hardship to protect the Last City).</li> <li><b>Vice:</b> Mournful (The conspiracy is paralyzed by grief, demanding adherence to ancient, depressive traditions).</li> <li><b>Attributes:</b> Power 9, Finesse 8, Resistance 9 (Total: 26)</li> <li><b>Conspiracy Actions:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Association:</b> 12</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Nodes</b><ul><li><b>The Order of the Parrot (Hierarchical):</b> The monastic record-keepers, ritualists, and educators of Alhambra. They dictate the proper time and manner for all actions, ensuring the city's traditions never change. They also run the schools that indoctrinate Alhambran youth into the necessity of the Bleak Harvest.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Focused Action</i> conspiracy action.</li> <li><b>Protectorate of Garnet (Hierarchical):</b> The Queen\u2019s Questers and secret police. Operating outside the jurisdiction of the other Orders, they root out treason, police the Nobility, and ensure absolute obedience to the Last Empress.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Silence Enemy</i> and <i>Turn Traitor</i> effects of <i>Manufacture Complication</i>.</li> <li><b>The Order of the Spotted Hyena (Temporal):</b> Alhambra\u2019s standing army and police force. They specialize in urban skirmishing, establishing defensive perimeters during the Wisp harvests on Earth, and hunting down dangerous Ferals and Renegades. Due to a royal writ of conscription, they draft the best and brightest youth from the city.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Shock Troops</i> and <i>Armory</i> effects of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>Protectorate of Heliotrope (Temporal):</b> Also known as the Night Audit. They are tasked with traveling to Earth, seizing infrastructure from rival conspiracies (particularly vampires and blood-sorcerers), and repurposing it to establish outposts for the Bleak Harvest.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>False Front</i> effect of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>The Order of the Vulture (Exploitative):</b> The tax collectors of Alhambra. They operate the refineries that distill raw, stolen hope into the taffy and lamp-fuel that powers the city. On Earth, they sit at the top of every Alhambran Enclave, calculating exactly how much misery must be inflicted to meet the city's quotas.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Resource Denial</i> effect of <i>Manufacture Complication</i>.</li> <li><b>Protectorate of Blue Topaz (Exploitative):</b> A clandestine ministry of propaganda and psychological warfare. They shape art, theater, and dreams in the Rebellious Provinces to slowly normalize Alhambran virtues: absolute dedication to the group, the willingness to commit atrocities without regret, and contempt for individualism.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Make Viral</i> effect of <i>Manufacture Complication</i>.</li> <li><b>The Order of the Beaver (Structural):</b> The Serene Architects. They manufacture the raw materials the city is built from using charmed furnaces, and they maintain the sprawling, rain-slicked architecture of Alhambra.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +1 to <i>Accelerate Project</i>.</li> <li><b>The Order of the Tortoise (Structural):</b> Blending the roles of librarians and castellans, the Tortoises protect the city's archives and its armories. They stockpile ancient Bequests (magical weapons/tools) dating back to the fallen Kingdom, heavily arming their fortress against intruders.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Experimental Equipment</i> effect of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Icons</b><ul><li><b>The Luminous Refineries (Organizational/Association):</b> The conspiracy extracts energy directly from human suffering. Once per chapter, Alhambra can heal/downgrade damage to its Association using 1, 3, or 5 conspiracy actions, instead of requiring a Project, by violently harvesting Wisps from the populace.</li> <li><b>Bequests of the Lost Kingdom (Agent/Variations):</b> The Order of the Tortoise stockpiles magical artifacts. All witting agents of Alhambra (including Baseline Sworn) have access to equipment that grants them Scar-free Magnitude 2 or 3 Variations (such as <i>Flight</i>, <i>Carapace</i>, or <i>Lash</i>) while operating on official business.</li> <li><b>The Queen's Shilling (Agent/Variations):</b> Alhambra can produce Devoted with terrifying efficiency. As a Complexity 1 Project, they can execute a <i>Launch Devoted Line</i> or <i>Expand Line</i> Project, instantly transforming Baseline agents into fully empowered Sworn bound by loyalty to the Last Empress.</li> <li><b>Dark Gates (Agent/Transportation):</b> Alhambra exists outside of reality. The conspiracy ignores all penalties from the <i>Improbable Escape</i> action (allowing its agents to vanish into shadows and mirrors to return to the Dark World). Furthermore, their facilities on Earth can be collapsed and relocated overnight.</li> <li><b>The Courtesy of Our Lady (Organizational/Resistance):</b> Alhambra extends diplomatic immunity and safe haven to its enemies, providing them with housing, medical care, and secure meeting places inside the Last City. By doing so, they monitor the actions of rogue Deviants. Attempts to investigate Alhambra from the outside suffer a -5 penalty, and the conspiracy's next surveillance roll against those investigators enjoys a +5 bonus.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Using Alhambra in a Chronicle</b><ul><li><b>The Gilded Cage:</b> Alhambra makes a brilliant &quot;acquisitive conspiracy&quot;. They do not view themselves as villains; they believe they are making the hard, necessary choices to preserve the last light in the universe. When the cohort is battered, bleeding, and running from more brutal conspiracies, Alhambra's Liaisons will appear, offering them shelter, hot food, and an arsenal of magical weapons. The only catch is that the cohort must swear fealty and help collect the &quot;hope tax&quot; from the mundane world. This sets up a profound psychological horror: the characters are safe, but only by becoming part of the system that parasitizes humanity.</li> <li><b>Sabotaging the Resistance:</b> Alhambra does not want Renegades and Radiant Princesses to successfully unite. The Order of the Ghost Owl actively floods supernatural communication channels with junk data, intercepts messengers, and sabotages alliances between other Remade. If the players' cohort attempts to build a massive network or coalition to fight the Web of Pain, Alhambra will use its Exploitative Nodes to fracture that alliance, preferring to keep rogue Deviants isolated and ineffective &quot;for their own good&quot; so they don't draw the ire of the Darkness.</li> <li><b>A War on Two Fronts:</b> Alhambra despises the other Twilight Courts just as much as they despise the Darkness. A chronicle could easily feature the cohort caught in a brutal shadow war between Alhambra and the <b>Queen of Storms</b> (a rival otherworldly conspiracy utilizing the <i>Tempesta</i> Invocation to relentlessly annihilate anything tainted by the dark). Renegades might find themselves temporarily allying with Alhambran strike teams to put down a rampaging Storms cult, only to have the Ravens turn on them the moment the immediate threat is dealt with.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Army of the Seraphic General (The Queen of Storms)</b></span><br /> The Queen of Storms was once a mortal monarch of the Fearless Kingdoms, an impartial judge who loved her people. When the Kingdom fell and was betrayed from within, she transcended her mortal flesh, burning alive in a crucible of rage to become a living natural disaster. Today, she is the Seraphic General, an entity of screaming winds, green fire, and caustic hatred waging an eternal, suicidal war in the Dark World against the All-Consuming Darkness and the Traitors of Alhambra.<br /> <br /> As an <b>Otherworldly Conspiracy (Standing 10)</b>, the Army of the Seraphic General operates globally across Earth and the Dark World. They are a <b>Destructive Conspiracy</b> of the highest order. The Queen of Storms' followers\u2014the Seraphim, the Furies, the Stormwracked, and the ephemeral Goalenu\u2014care nothing for subtlety, infiltration, or collateral damage. They do not compromise, they do not negotiate, and they view anyone who stands in their way (or shows mercy to the wicked) as enemies of the Light who must be purged.<br /> <br /> <b>Conspiracy Traits</b><ul><li><b>Standing:</b> 10 (Otherworldly)</li> <li><b>Principles:</b> Death to the Darkness; burn the world to save the world; show absolutely no mercy.</li> <li><b>Virtue:</b> Fearless (The Seraphim will gladly die if it means taking their enemies with them).</li> <li><b>Vice:</b> Wrathful (The conspiracy is utterly blind to collateral damage and refuses to compromise).</li> <li><b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 6, Resistance 10 (Total: 28)</li> <li><b>Conspiracy Actions:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Association:</b> 13</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Nodes</b><ul><li><b>The Heart of the Storm (Hierarchical):</b> The epicenter of the Queen's eternal crusade within the Dark World. It is not a place, but the roaring vortex of the Queen of Storms herself. To approach her is to step into a hurricane of screaming souls and acid. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Focused Action</i> conspiracy action.</li> <li><b>The Sworn Guard (Hierarchical):</b> The Goalenu Barons. Ephemeral knights of Tempesta, born from the souls of the Queen's original fallen army. They possess terrifying combat prowess and command the lesser forces on Earth. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Shock Troops</i> effect of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>Stormwracked Cells (Temporal):</b> The Queen's mortal soldiers. Broken survivors, bereaved victims, and furious vigilantes who have sworn their lives to vengeance. They organize in heavily armed, decentralized paramilitary cells. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Armory</i> and <i>Weight of Numbers</i> effects of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>The Furies (Temporal):</b> Princesses of Storms. The magical vanguard of the conspiracy, channeling the Invocation of Tempesta to melt their enemies with acid and fire, unbothered by the damage their magic inflicts on their own bodies. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Execute</i> effect of <i>Send Agents</i> (if using lethal variations).</li> <li><b>Vengeful Hunters (Exploitative):</b> The conspiracy readily co-opts mundane monster hunters, radicalized law enforcement, and heavily armed militias, turning their righteous anger into a weapon for the Seraphic General. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Resource Denial</i> effect of <i>Manufacture Complication</i> (usually via arson or explosives).</li> <li><b>Potter's Forges (Structural):</b> Secret sanctuaries and basements where Stormwracked cultists ritually mix freshly dug clay with their own blood. This produces the raw vessels necessary to summon and house Goalenu spirits on Earth. <i>Privilege:</i> +1 to <i>Accelerate Project</i>.</li> <li><b>The Front Lines (Structural):</b> Tainted Places and Nightscapes that the conspiracy has purposefully invaded. Instead of sealing them, they use these bleeding wounds in reality as beachheads to funnel troops directly into the Dark World. <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Improbable Escape</i> action.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Icons</b><ul><li><b>Royal Favors (Agent/Variations):</b> The Queen channels her raw, acidic hatred directly through her followers. All Devoted and agents of Storms can unleash devastating, Scar-free Magnitude 4 or 5 Variations (such as <i>Lash</i>, <i>Storm-Caller</i>, or <i>Flight</i>), but doing so inflicts resistant lethal or aggravated damage on the agent themselves.</li> <li><b>Stormwracked Dreams (Organizational/Surveillance):</b> The Queen whispers in the nightmares of her followers, showing them battlefields and the faces of monsters. The conspiracy enjoys a +5 bonus to Surveillance rolls to locate creatures of Darkness, Alhambran agents, or heavily Tainted locations.</li> <li><b>Purgation's Fire (Organizational/Resistance):</b> The conspiracy leaves nothing for its enemies to salvage. The Army of Storms ignores bashing damage to its Association. Furthermore, whenever a Node is destroyed, it triggers a catastrophic explosion of green fire and acid, inflicting massive damage on whoever destroyed it.</li> <li><b>The Chimerical Barons (Agent/Variations):</b> The conspiracy can deploy Goalenu. As a Complexity 3 Project, they can execute a <i>Launch Devoted Line</i>, animating clay and flesh vessels with the spirits of the Sworn Guard to act as elite assassins and tacticians.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Using the Queen of Storms in a Chronicle</b><ul><li><b>The Nuclear Option:</b> The Queen of Storms is the ultimate Destructive Conspiracy. They do not scheme, blackmail, or gaslight; they annihilate. If a Renegade cohort needs an insurmountable target destroyed, pointing a Stormwracked cell at it is highly effective\u2014but the Furies will burn down the whole neighborhood, and everyone in it, to make sure the target is dead.</li> <li><b>Enemy of My Enemy:</b> A cohort might find themselves temporarily allied with a cell of Furies to take down a massive Progenitor conspiracy. However, the tension remains palpable: the Furies will gladly sacrifice the Renegades to achieve the objective, and the moment the cohort hesitates, shows mercy, or refuses to cross a moral line, the Seraphim will classify them as traitors and turn their weapons on the players.</li> <li><b>The Trail of Ash:</b> Sometimes the cohort isn't fighting the conspiracy directly, but dealing with the horrific aftermath. The Seraphic General's forces regularly leave behind burning buildings, innocent casualties, and massive property damage. The Renegades might have to play damage control, saving trapped civilians and navigating the mundane police response caused by a Fury's fanatical crusade against a monster hiding in the city.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:28px\">\u200b\u200b<b>The Court of the True Heir (The Queen of Mirrors)</b></span><br /> Trapped in the shattered remnants of the Crystal Tower of Heril, unmoored in nothingness, the Queen of Mirrors watches the world through reflective surfaces. Unable to cope with the tragedy of the Kingdom's fall, she retreated into absolute denial. She seeks the &quot;True Heir&quot;\u2014a prophesied, perfect savior who will effortlessly fix the world without compromise or sacrifice. She whispers to young, inexperienced, or isolated Princesses through mirrors, convincing each of them that <i>they</i>, and they alone, are this destined savior.<br /> <br /> As an <b>Otherworldly Conspiracy (Standing 10)</b>, the Court of Mirrors is less a unified organization and more a global web of malignant narcissists, sycophants, and magical pop-stars. The Queen's followers (the Lightbearers or Heirs) believe they possess the divine right to rule. They are an <b>Acquisitive/Subversive Conspiracy</b>. While they rarely commit the blatant atrocities of Tears or Storms, their absolute solipsism makes them incredibly dangerous. To an Heir, everyone else is a secondary character in her story. When an Heir's refusal to make hard choices inevitably leads to disaster, she simply uses her magic to erase her own memories of the failure, leaving others to suffer the consequences of her vanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Conspiracy Traits</b><ul><li><b>Standing:</b> 10 (Otherworldly)</li> <li><b>Principles:</b> Exalt yourself above all others; modesty is a false virtue; never accept compromise or sacrifice.</li> <li><b>Virtue:</b> Radiant (The Heirs genuinely believe they are shining beacons of hope and can inspire absolute, cult-like devotion).</li> <li><b>Vice:</b> Solipsistic (The conspiracy refuses to acknowledge reality when it conflicts with their narrative of perfection, leading to madness and catastrophic negligence).</li> <li><b>Attributes:</b> Power 10, Finesse 11, Resistance 7 (Total: 28)</li> <li><b>Conspiracy Actions:</b> 5</li> <li><b>Association:</b> 10</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Nodes</b><ul><li><b>The Crystal Tower (Hierarchical):</b> The Queen's seat in the Dreamlands. It is utterly inaccessible, but from it, she watches through every mirror on Earth. She grants her Heirs prophetic visions (that conveniently omit any of their own flaws or failures) and whispers advice.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Focused Action</i> conspiracy action.</li> <li><b>The True Heirs (Hierarchical):</b> The Princesses of Mirrors themselves. They operate as independent warlords of vanity, each believing she is the sole leader of the Light. They command immense magical power, specializing in illusions, self-enhancement, and light manipulation.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Execute</i> or <i>Shock Troops</i> effects of <i>Send Agents</i> (when an Heir personally takes the field to show off).</li> <li><b>Cults of Personality (Exploitative):</b> Sycophantic Sworn, desperate Beacons, paparazzi, and mortal fan clubs who adore the Heirs. The Heirs use their <i>One Perfect Woman</i> Charms to brainwash organizations into viewing them as flawless paragons.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Make Viral</i> effect of <i>Manufacture Complication</i>.</li> <li><b>Astral Droplets (Temporal):</b> The Heirs rarely want to do boring, mundane work. They use the <i>Goccia Astrale</i> Charm to pull living clones of themselves out of mirrors. These &quot;Droplets&quot; have their own twisted sentience and perform the conspiracy's grunt work, though they are prone to developing their own megalomaniacal agendas.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>False Front</i> effect of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>Enduring Beauty Clinics (Structural):</b> Hidden salons and plastic surgery clinics where the Heirs literally peel the beauty away from sleeping or captive victims to forge metaphysically potent gems.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +1 to <i>Accelerate Project</i>.</li> <li><b>Hidey-Holes (Structural):</b> Pocket dimensions carved into the infinite glass behind mirrors. The conspiracy uses these extradimensional vaults to store weapons, kidnapped rivals, and stolen artifacts.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Improbable Escape</i> action.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Icons</b><ul><li><b>Through the Looking Glass (Organizational/Transportation):</b> The Court of Mirrors bypasses physical security with ease. Conspiracy agents can use <i>Mirror Walk</i> to step into any reflective surface large enough to hold them and emerge from another. The conspiracy ignores all penalties for the <i>Improbable Escape</i> action as long as a mirror or large pane of glass is nearby.</li> <li><b>Enduring Beauty Gems (Agent/Variations):</b> The conspiracy hoards gems forged from stolen human beauty. Agents carrying these gems gain access to Scar-free Magnitude 3 or 4 Variations (such as <i>Awe</i>, <i>Illusions</i>, or <i>Telekinesis</i>). A gem can also be crushed to automatically grant an exceptional success on a crucial roll.</li> <li><b>Somebody Else's Problem (Organizational/Resistance):</b> The Heirs magically erase their own memories of failure, shielding their egos from reality. The conspiracy ignores bashing damage to its Association. Furthermore, if a Node is subverted or exposed, the conspiracy can automatically sever the Node and erase all memory of its existence from the remaining members, preventing the damage from spreading.</li> <li><b>Specchio's Madness (Organizational/Association):</b> The magic of Mirrors is fundamentally unhinged. Anyone attempting to investigate the conspiracy's deep lore, or any Renegade who attempts to forcefully extract information from an Heir via telepathy, risks their own sanity. Investigators suffer a -3 penalty to all rolls to uncover the conspiracy's true motives, and dramatic failures inflict the <i>Madness</i> or <i>Unbalanced</i> Conditions.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Using the Queen of Mirrors in a Chronicle</b><ul><li><b>The &quot;Helpful&quot; Patron:</b> An Heir of Mirrors might introduce herself to a cohort of Renegades not as an enemy, but as their rightful leader. She will offer them shelter, immense wealth, and magical support, expecting them to act as her adoring sidekicks. The horror here is entirely social: the Renegades must navigate the fragile, explosive ego of a demigod who will instantly turn on them if they refuse to validate her delusions or if they try to share in the spotlight.</li> <li><b>Lethal Negligence:</b> The cohort is forced to deal with the catastrophic fallout of an Heir's actions. Because Heirs refuse to make hard choices or accept necessary sacrifices, they often try to save everyone in impossible situations\u2014and end up getting everyone killed. Worse, because of the <i>Somebody Else's Problem</i> Charm, the Heir has literally erased her own memory of the failure. The Renegades must clean up a horrific mess (like a rampaging monster the Heir &quot;spared&quot;) while dealing with a conspiracy leader who genuinely believes she did a perfect job.</li> <li><b>The Hall of Mirrors:</b> Engaging the Court of Mirrors in combat is a surreal nightmare. The cohort will find themselves fighting endless, fragile mirror-clones (<i>Astral Droplets</i>), chasing enemies through portals in storefront windows, and dealing with massive, disorienting illusions that flip gravity and light. It requires clever tactics and destroying the reflective surfaces in an environment just to pin an Heir down.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T22:36:33-07:00","id":1563212,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>DETHRONED</b></span><br /> Dethroned are former Princesses who despaired of their calling, lost all their Touchstones, and went completely <b>Feral</b>. Having shed their mortal forms and lost their Belief, they have succumbed permanently to <b>End Stage Instability</b>. They are twisted and empowered by a blasphemous transformation that fills the void in their souls with pure Taint. They are horrific, corrupted reflections of the Hopeful who project their unending grief and bitterness onto the world around them, reshaping reality into twisted reflections of their own nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Threat Level:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Themes</b></span><br /> The Dethroned represent the themes of hopelessness, tragedy, and the destructive cycle of abuse. They are the Hopeful equivalent of a Feral Deviant in End Stage\u2014a creature utterly devoid of the Loyalty and Conviction Touchstones required to anchor a shattered soul. Because they lack these bonds, they have no way to heal their Instability. Their Scars and Variations run rampant, mutating them beyond all recognition into unrecognizable caricatures of their former selves. Rather than being driven by the focused vengeance of a Renegade or the obedience of a Devoted, the Dethroned act entirely on terror, agony, and instinct. Their existence is a constant, surreal loop of their own failures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Allies</b></span><br /> Dethroned have no true friends, only thralls. Any Dark being that enters their presence has its will twisted to become a willing supporter of the Dethroned's despair, making even intelligent monsters extremely wary of them. The most degenerate cults of the Darkness may worship them as fallen gods, but the Dethroned view them only as props in their eternal tragedies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Enemies</b></span><br /> Radiant Princesses hunt the Dethroned in hopes of defeating their physical forms so they can bear the terrible burden of redeeming their souls. Normal Renegades and Devoted despise them for their ability to violently subjugate the minds of others and warp victims into mindless extensions of their own twisted psyches.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Web of Pain</b></span><br /> Conspiracies treat Dethroned the same way they treat any powerful Feral: as apocalyptic errors that must be euthanized, scrubbed from records, and destroyed, or as disposable throw-away weapons of mass destruction to unleash upon their rivals. Occasionally, a conspiracy's cruel experiments on a captive Princess will inadvertently strip away her final Touchstone, triggering her horrific transformation into a Feral Dethroned and unleashing a localized apocalypse upon the conspirators' own facility.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Greater Form: Dethroned</b></span><br /> The creature is a fallen Noble. She has a Supernatural Potency trait called Inner Darkness, Anchors in the form of horrific Obsessions, and a Fuel trait called Clouds (or Shadows). This Greater Form completely replaces the Princess Greater Form and grants access to two exclusive Lesser Forms: Chains and Hexes.<ul><li><b>Supernatural Potency (Inner Darkness):</b> When a Princess falls, her Inner Light inverts into Inner Darkness. This trait acts as her Supernatural Tolerance, dictates the maximum number of Clouds she can hold, and limits the amount of fuel she can spend in a single turn.</li> <li><b>Anchors (Zero Touchstones &amp; The Fall):</b> A Dethroned is Feral; she possesses zero Touchstones. Instead, she is anchored entirely by the circumstances of her fall. She interprets all current events as a recapitulation of her personal tragedy, using her powers to forcefully assign roles to her victims so they can reenact her failures.</li> <li><b>Fuel Trait: Clouds (Shadows):</b> Where the Hopeful use Wisps, the Dethroned fuel their dark magic with Clouds (also known as Shadows)\u2014fragments of misery and despair. A Dethroned regains Clouds in the following ways:<ul><li><i>Endless Angst:</i> Merely by existing in a state of eternal torment, she regains 1 Cloud each night at midnight.</li> <li><i>Sadism:</i> The Dethroned replaces a Princess's Sensitivity with Sadism. Whenever she witnesses or causes the suffering of others, it confirms her dark choices; she rolls her Inner Darkness and regains 1 Cloud for each success.</li> <li><i>Misery Gluttony:</i> If she possesses the Misery Glutton Hex, she regains Willpower when a victim loses their last Willpower point, and fully restores all Clouds and Willpower if a victim commits suicide in her presence.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Chains</b></span><br /> Chains represent the Dethroned's innate authority over the Dark World and its creatures.<ul><li><b>Fortress of Regrets:</b> The Dethroned projects a Lament (a personal Nightscape) into the Dark World that continuously broadcasts the agonizing allegories of her fall.</li> <li><b>Companions in Misery:</b> She forcefully overwrites the loyalties of Dark beings and mortals, inflicting the Dethroned Follower Condition to make them subservient actors in her tragedy.</li> <li><b>Spawn Darkchild:</b> She can spend Willpower to spontaneously generate bespoke Darkspawn from the substance of the Dark World to serve as foot soldiers.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Lesser Form: Hexes</b></span><br /> Hexes are corrupted black magics formed of solid misery that replace the Charms she wielded in life.<ul><li><b>Destructive Magic:</b> Hexes allow the Dethroned to project devastating energy (<i>Blast</i>), infect victims with supernatural despair (<i>Infectious Madness</i>), or bind her own Shadows into mortals to corrupt them (<i>Kiss of a Princess</i>).</li> <li><b>Monstrous Mutations:</b> Hexes also warp her physical form into an uncontrollable End Stage monstrosity, granting her the ability to swell to gigantic proportions (<i>Monstrous Size</i>), dissolve into a swarm of horrors (<i>Swarming Horror</i>), or rapidly heal her injuries by oozing void from her wounds (<i>Regeneration</i>).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Redemption (Curing the Incurable)</b></span><br /> For a normal Deviant, going Feral and reaching End Stage Instability is an inescapable, incurable condition. The Dethroned are the sole exception to this cosmic rule. After a Dethroned's physical form is defeated, a Radiant Princess can reach out to its soul through her Sensitivity. By voluntarily taking on the Dethroned's accumulated Shadows into her own soul, the Princess can ultimately redeem the fallen Noble, returning her to the Light and the cycle of reincarnation.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Archetypes</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Tragic Cleaner (Controlled):</b> In life, Maria was driven to suicide by the overwhelming stress of a rigged system. Now, the monster that wears her memories obsessively orders her Darkspawn minions to &quot;clean&quot; houses in the real world. Because the inhuman monsters understand nothing of sanitation, these cleanings are horrific, violent ransackings.<br /> <br /> <b>The Witch in the Woods (Feral):</b> Cast out by her village for her magic, she struggled to raise her children alone in the forest until the isolation broke her. Now, she dwells deep in the Dark World within a watercolor-painted log cabin. She kidnaps living children to play the role of her family, only to inevitably devour them alive to &quot;keep them safe&quot; inside her own tainted body.<br /> <br /> <b>The Catfish (Exploitative):</b> As one of the rare &quot;Enthroned&quot; who rules a Nightscape on Earth instead of the Dark World, she maintains a deceptive presence on the internet. She infiltrates online support groups for young Princesses and Renegades, earning their trust only to lure them to physical meetups where she slaughters them, finding sick solace in making others suffer worse than she does.\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Fortress of Regrets (Dethroned Nightscape)</b></span><br /> When a Princess falls to 0 Belief and embraces the All-Consuming Darkness, she transforms into a Dethroned\u2014a horrific monster of pure Taint. Her domain in the Dark World is known as a Fortress of Regrets or a Lament. This Nightscape acts as a self-contained, otherworldly conspiracy that projects its unending grief onto the world, drawing in victims to reenact the fallen Noble's tragedy.<br /> <br /> A Dethroned's Nightscape is best modeled as a <b>Standing 6 (Metamorphosis)</b> conspiracy. Although its influence is usually localized to a specific Tainted Place on Earth, its otherworldly nature, endless supply of monsters, and reality-warping power make it an apocalyptic threat.<br /> <br /> <b>Conspiracy Traits</b><ul><li><b>Standing:</b> 6</li> <li><b>Principles:</b> Reenact the tragedy; extinguish the Light of Hope; punish the guilty and the innocent alike.</li> <li><b>Virtue:</b> Relentless (The Nightscape compulsively repeats its narrative and never stops hunting intruders).</li> <li><b>Vice:</b> Despairing (The conspiracy is paralyzed by grief, preferring to wallow in misery rather than adapt to threats).</li> <li><b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 3, Resistance 7 (Total: 18)</li> <li><b>Conspiracy Actions:</b> 3</li> <li><b>Association:</b> 10</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Hierarchical Node:</b> The Lair<br /> <b>Temporal Nodes:</b> Cataphractoi Enforcers, Darkspawn Packs, Nightmare Swarms<br /> <b>Exploitative Nodes:</b> Dark Cultists, Broken Touchstones, Tainted Places<br /> <b>Structural Nodes:</b> The Caricature, The Lock, The Psychodrama<br /> <b>Icons:</b> Spawn Darkchild, The Labyrinth, Welcome to My Personal Hell<br /> <br /> <b>Nodes</b><ul><li><b>The Lair (Hierarchical):</b> The black heart of the Nightscape where the Dethroned resides. It is a surreal, twisted reflection of the place where her soul finally broke. The Dethroned herself serves as the Linchpin. Because she is a Feral End-Stage Deviant, she rarely leaves the Lair, instead forcing her victims and thralls to come to her.<br /> <i>Privilege:</i> +2 to the <i>Shock Troops</i> and <i>Weight of Numbers</i> effects of <i>Send Agents</i>.</li> <li><b>Nightmare Swarms (Temporal):</b> The Nightscape is populated by Nightmares\u2014ephemeral manifestations of the Dethroned's fears and memories. They are the foot soldiers of the conspiracy, sent to terrorize victims and harvest Essence/Wisps to sustain the Nightscape.<br /> <i>Linchpin:</i> A Jailer Nightmare\u2014an unreasoning, relentless super-monster that carries out its torments with absolute zeal.</li> <li><b>Tainted Places (Exploitative):</b> The Nightscape bleeds into the real world through Tainted Places. The conspiracy uses these physical locations to subtly influence the mundane world, exploiting the resulting misery to feed the Dark World.<br /> <i>Linchpin:</i> A Defiler or Mnemosyne who maintains the Tainted Place on Earth, luring victims inside.</li> <li><b>The Psychodrama (Structural):</b> The core narrative loop the Nightscape exists to reenact. The Dethroned uses the environment and her minions to force intruders into the roles of her abusers or victims.<br /> <i>Linchpin:</i> The Caricature. A twisted, powerless copy of the Dethroned's former human self, eternally trapped in the Nightscape's worst moments. Subverting this Node is key to discovering the Dethroned's true identity and the trauma that broke her.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Icons</b><ul><li><b>Spawn Darkchild (Agent/Variations):</b> A Dethroned molds the stuff of the Dark World to spontaneously generate bespoke Darkspawn to serve her. Once per chapter, the conspiracy may take the <i>Send Agents</i> action with a +4 bonus to the <i>Weight of Numbers</i> effect without it counting against its maximum number of conspiracy actions. These agents are manifestations of Pure Darkness and never suffer breaking points.</li> <li><b>Welcome to My Personal Hell (Organizational/Transportation):</b> The Dethroned can forcibly drag targets from the material world into her Dark World Lament. As a conspiracy action, the Nightscape may use Power to abduct a target who is currently within a Tainted Place. If successful, the target is instantly transported into the Nightscape, bypassing normal physical boundaries.</li> <li><b>The Lock (Organizational/Resistance):</b> A Nightscape is anchored by a specific puzzle, unacknowledged truth, or insurmountable psychological barrier. Until the cohort understands and unravels this mystery (by gathering Clues to damage the Nightscape's &quot;Enigma&quot; and &quot;Psyche&quot;), the Dethroned is nearly invincible. The conspiracy ignores all lethal damage to its Association unless the cohort has successfully subverted <i>The Psychodrama</i> Structural Node by uncovering the circumstances of the Dethroned's fall.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Using the Nightscape in a Chronicle</b><br /> <br /> <b>Mapping Princess Rules to Deviant Mechanics</b><br /> In <i>Princess: The Hopeful</i>, defeating a Nightscape requires depleting three tracks: Corpus (physical destruction of monsters), Enigma (solving the mystery of the trauma), and Psyche (convincing the prisoner to let go). In a <i>Deviant</i> chronicle, this naturally maps to destroying a Conspiracy:<ul><li><b>Corpus:</b> Engaging the Temporal Nodes (fighting Nightmares and Darkspawn).</li> <li><b>Enigma:</b> Investigating the Structural and Exploitative Nodes to gather Clues about the Dethroned's identity and the <i>Psychodrama</i>.</li> <li><b>Psyche:</b> Subverting the Structural Nodes (interacting with the <i>Caricature</i> or solving <i>The Lock</i>) to deal lethal or aggravated damage to the conspiracy's Association.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>The Dungeon Crawl</b><br /> Unlike corporate or government conspiracies, a Nightscape functions like a horrific, surreal dungeon. The cohort is physically trapped inside a shifting, hostile dimension. Conspiracy Actions taken by the Nightscape represent the environment turning against the Renegades: shifting hallways, sudden floods of toxic memories, or the Dethroned using her <i>Recalled Torment</i> Hex to overwrite the cohort's perceptions.<br /> <br /> <b>Redemption as Subversion</b><br /> If the Renegades simply fight their way to the center and kill the Dethroned, the Nightscape is destroyed, but the Dethroned's soul is lost to the Darkness. If a Radiant Princess (or a highly empathetic Renegade) wishes to <i>redeem</i> the Dethroned, they must fully subvert the <i>Lair</i> Hierarchical Node. This requires taking on the Dethroned's Shadows/Instability to cure her End-Stage condition\u2014a monumental, self-sacrificing act that dismantles the conspiracy peacefully from within.\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T09:39:00-07:00","id":1563249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1562226#post1562226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to build something here. A cross-splat Magical Girl group and Chronicle with included guidelines for participation of every splat. It may work as a Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo alternative to the Contagion Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Rules:<br /> - Genre played straight, not parody/subversion;<br /> - CofD played straight, this is not an adaptation;<br /> - Stretching genre into darker themes is valid;<br /> - Breaking genre against darker themes, is not;<br /> - Empowerment fantasy core;<br /> - Main struggle: dual life vs emotional sincerity;<br /> - Upbeat not mandatory, but compatibility is.<br /> <br /> Classic References:<br /> Mah\u014d no Princess Mink\u012b Momo<br /> Bish\u014djo Senshi Sailor Moon<br /> Cardcaptor Sakura<br /> Pretty Cure Series<br /> <br /> Genre Testers (they may look like mockery or parody, but are played straight):<br /> Princess Tutu<br /> Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo Lyrical Nanoha<br /> Senki Zessh\u014d Symphogear<br /> Flip Flappers<br /> Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo ni Akogarete<br /> <br /> Litmus Tests (they legitimately straddle the line and are partly genre breakers, but reaffirm the genre's values in the end and through contrast with a full deconstruction -&gt; reconstruction cycle):<br /> Y\u016bki Y\u016bna wa Y\u016bsha de Aru<br /> Puella Magi Madoka Magica<br /> <br /> Counter References (those works misrepresent the genre):<br /> Magical Girl Raising Project<br /> Magical Girl Site<br /> Magical Girl Spec-Ops Asuka<br /> Any isekai of Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo in a Grimdark world<br /> <br /> Genre staples checklist:<br /> 1\ufe0f\u20e3 Weaponized Femininity<br /> - [ ] Accessories as itens of power<br /> - [ ] Vanity legitimated without &quot;glory/honor&quot;<br /> - [ ] Cute, Feminine and Romantic motifs<br /> - [ ] Emotional engagement<br /> 2\ufe0f\u20e3 Coming of Age<br /> - [ ] 10 - 14 years old protagonists<br /> - [ ] Oni-like adult villains (preferably women)<br /> - [ ] Mature-adjacent Alter-Ego<br /> - [ ] Mundane life milestones discussed (school, work, marriage)<br /> 3\ufe0f\u20e3 Empowerment<br /> - [ ] Scepter as soft symbol of authority<br /> - [ ] Rebellion against imposed roles<br /> - [ ] Transformation granting autonomy<br /> - [ ] Idealism validated<br /> 4\ufe0f\u20e3 Relationships and Emotion<br /> - [ ] Bonds and friendship between women<br /> - [ ] Hope and dreams can prevail and heal<br /> - [ ] Magic is positive personal expression<br /> - [ ] Emotional sincerity as source of Strength<br /> 5\ufe0f\u20e3 Superhero Core<br /> - [ ] Compact of \u5909\u8eab\u30d2\u30ed\u30a4\u30f3 and superpowers<br /> - [ ] Secret Identity - Dual Life tension<br /> - [ ] Extraordinary duty to protect Humanity<br /> - [ ] Otherworldly Cute Mascot<br /> <br /> Observation: male characters have gender roles and expectations challenged in the genre. For important NPCs they must be few, but as PCs the arc of finding validation of &quot;feminine&quot; virtues or interests is valid.<br /> <br /> For now I'm structuring the basics as per above, some ideas I have already:<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udffaMummies: possibly the original group, it was formed in Irem before the ritual. Members may have split or joined through the ages.<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udf16 Werewolf: build an example totem, maybe a Lodge.<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udf77 Vampire: a MG Covenant, in its center there may be a MG Bloodline.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\uddff Mage: Rotes galore, maybe a Legacy.<br /> <br /> \u26d3\ufe0f\u200d\ud83d\udca5 Changeling: new Court Systems, maybe?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udddd\ufe0f Geist: what this Krewe would look like?<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udfad Demon: an Agency with strict rules on Pact, but also a system in place to help with Covers.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udca4 Beast: Horrors themed around monstrous femininity.<br /> <br /> \u2623\ufe0f Deviant: at least one Conspiracy is making Magical Girls on purpose.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Promethean: how this Pilgrimage can look like? How to settle a mundane life without causing a Wasteland?<br /> <br /> \ud83d\udeab Hunter: a Hunter Conspiracy, Endowments, support for supernaturals struggling to do well rather than focus on destruction.<br /> <br /> What is the Transformation? How's the item that induces it? Is it common for all, specific by Splat, or are there numerous ways?<br /> <br /> Who are the villains? Who's the ultimate villainess? How each splat contributes evil doers?<br /> <br /> How some greater powers and factions react to the whole idea? Covenants, Orders, True Fae, Chthonic Gods, Judges of Du'at, God-Machine, Heroes, Conspiracies, Qashmalin? Exploring the possible reactions of known entities and new ones.<br /> <br /> I can't really devote much to this project right now, but am throwing seeds anyone can discuss or use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 I tried moving the discussion of this to the general CofD forum, as this isn't specific to just Deviant anymore. But my post there got Unapproved; so let me try again here. <br /> <br /> What I'd use as the core of this would be a Magical Girl Merit-based Template (see Hurt Locker). The core Transformation Merit would be built around not just changing appearance, but also in providing you with a customized loadout of gear whenever you transform, reflavored as raiments and regalia: in its simplest version, a Magical Girl gets to swap out her \u201ccivilian clothes\u201d for a number of dots worth of Equipment. Said equipment is magical in the sense that its form doesn't necessarily follow its function: the Magical Girl might transform and find herself equipped with the equivalent of a rifle, complete with all the game stats of a rifle; but its form is a highly decorated wand that fires bursts of magical energy. <br /> <br /> This Transformation Merit would be available to anyone with an appropriate justification, mortal or supernatural. Mortals would have the ability to supplement this with additional Merits making it easier for them to deal with the supernatural elements of the Chronicles of Darkness; for this, I intend to borrow from the Bystander Merits from WoD's Hunter Player's Guide: things like an ability to see through illusions/identify monsters for what they are, or a resistance to supernatural mental control/monstrous auras like Lunacy or Disquiet, etc. Basically, mortals with the Magical Girl Merit-based Template would be much like WoD's Imbued, but reflavored with Magical Girl tropes. It maybe it might be thought of as the MG equivalent of WoD's Faith \u2014 just made more generic rather than Christian-themed. <br /> <br /> But the Transformation Merit itself, being solely about changing appearance and loadout, would be available to <i>anyone</i>, not just mortals. <br /> <br /> Another implication of the reframing of the Imbued into Magical Girl terms is that there's something out there in the Chronicles of Darkness that's roughly analogous to the Messengers: a supernatural faction of Light that opposes the Darkness. But it's not as\u2026 hands-off or narrow-minded? as HtR's Messengers were, and are willing to empower <i>anyone</i> who's willing to fight the Darkness, not just mortals. Most of the supernatural girls they empower already have a large toolkit in terms of supernatural benefits and only get the Transformation Merit; only mortals get access to the additional Merits inspired by the Imbued. In terms of not being as hands-off, I'd have the MG-flavored version of the Messengers take the form of Mascot allies. This too would be available as an optional Merit that most Magical Girls would have regardless of origin; the only reason to lack it would be if the character concept involves the Magical Girl becoming estranged from the Messengers. I'm still working out the details; but I'm thinking in terms of the Messenger also serving as the unifying factor for a team of Magical Girls and as a nexus for \u201cthe magic of friendship\u201d capabilities that such a team might have. <br /> <br /> Both the Transformation and the Mascot would be potentially available to anyone. With that in place, we can start moving through the existing supernatural factions and creating MG-themed allegiances for each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T10:36:12-07:00","id":1563251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563212#post1563212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Redemption as Subversion</b><br /> If the Renegades simply fight their way to the center and kill the Dethroned, the Nightscape is destroyed, but the Dethroned's soul is lost to the Darkness. If a Radiant Princess (or a highly empathetic Renegade) wishes to <i>redeem</i> the Dethroned, they must fully subvert the <i>Lair</i> Hierarchical Node. This requires taking on the Dethroned's Shadows/Instability to cure her End-Stage condition\u2014a monumental, self-sacrificing act that dismantles the conspiracy peacefully from within.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a member of another splat be able to redeem the Dethroned? Would it be valid for any character to take in her Instability?<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar enough with Princess, how does it work to cleanse yourself from those after you redeem (or starts redemption of) the Dethroned?<br /> <br /> What happens to a soul lost to the Darkness? Is it merely a sad end, or does it comes back to bite you later?<br /> <br /> By the way: would you say those Deviant-based versions are working well as a means to translate the fansplats while ensuring some mechanical quality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T02:41:41-07:00","id":1563981,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Woops, I already mentioned the darker magical girl series I was thinking of!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-11-2026, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T17:59:13-07:00","id":1563987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563249#post1563249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd use as the core of this would be a Magical Girl Merit-based Template (see Hurt Locker). The core Transformation Merit would be built around not just changing appearance, but also in providing you with a customized loadout of gear whenever you transform, reflavored as raiments and regalia: in its simplest version, a Magical Girl gets to swap out her \u201ccivilian clothes\u201d for a number of dots worth of Equipment. Said equipment is magical in the sense that its form doesn't necessarily follow its function: the Magical Girl might transform and find herself equipped with the equivalent of a rifle, complete with all the game stats of a rifle; but its form is a highly decorated wand that fires bursts of magical energy.<br /> <br /> This Transformation Merit would be available to anyone with an appropriate justification, mortal or supernatural. Mortals would have the ability to supplement this with additional Merits making it easier for them to deal with the supernatural elements of the Chronicles of Darkness; for this, I intend to borrow from the Bystander Merits from WoD's Hunter Player's Guide: things like an ability to see through illusions/identify monsters for what they are, or a resistance to supernatural mental control/monstrous auras like Lunacy or Disquiet, etc. Basically, mortals with the Magical Girl Merit-based Template would be much like WoD's Imbued, but reflavored with Magical Girl tropes. It maybe it might be thought of as the MG equivalent of WoD's Faith \u2014 just made more generic rather than Christian-themed.<br /> <br /> But the Transformation Merit itself, being solely about changing appearance and loadout, would be available to <i>anyone</i>, not just mortals.<br /> <br /> Another implication of the reframing of the Imbued into Magical Girl terms is that there's something out there in the Chronicles of Darkness that's roughly analogous to the Messengers: a supernatural faction of Light that opposes the Darkness. But it's not as\u2026 hands-off or narrow-minded? as HtR's Messengers were, and are willing to empower <i>anyone</i> who's willing to fight the Darkness, not just mortals. Most of the supernatural girls they empower already have a large toolkit in terms of supernatural benefits and only get the Transformation Merit; only mortals get access to the additional Merits inspired by the Imbued. In terms of not being as hands-off, I'd have the MG-flavored version of the Messengers take the form of Mascot allies. This too would be available as an optional Merit that most Magical Girls would have regardless of origin; the only reason to lack it would be if the character concept involves the Magical Girl becoming estranged from the Messengers. I'm still working out the details; but I'm thinking in terms of the Messenger also serving as the unifying factor for a team of Magical Girls and as a nexus for \u201cthe magic of friendship\u201d capabilities that such a team might have.<br /> <br /> Both the Transformation and the Mascot would be potentially available to anyone. With that in place, we can start moving through the existing supernatural factions and creating MG-themed allegiances for each.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here are the detailed mechanics for the Transformation and Mascot Merits:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Transformation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None (Open to mortals and all supernatural splats alike)<br /> <br /> <b>Core Mechanics:</b><br /> <b>Magical Persona &amp; Identity Shield:</b> Allows a character to instantly rewrite their civilian form into a high-utility, stylized magical persona. A supernatural perception filter prevents onlookers from linking the magical persona to the civilian identity, even if the character's face remains exposed. Forcing a recognition check requires a contested Wits + Composure vs. Presence + Subterfuge (or Supernatural Tolerance) roll at a -3 penalty (waived only with concrete proof). Digital recordings, cameras, and facial recognition software automatically register the persona as a separate, unidentifiable individual.<br /> <b>Transformed Inventory:</b> Upon transforming, civilian gear vanishes and is replaced by a predetermined magical loadout. Form does not follow function\u2014visual appearance is flavor (e.g., a star-tipped wand firing starlight beams), while game statistics use standard item templates. If gear leaves the character's person, it dissolves into light and resets to the character's transformation inventory.<br /> <b>Equipment Point Budget:</b> The character receives an Equipment Point Budget equal to 3 + dots in Transformation, allocating these points into a fixed inventory of manifested gear during narrative downtime:<ul><li><b>\u2022 Dot:</b> 4 Equipment Points</li> <li><b>\u2022\u2022 Dots:</b> 5 Equipment Points</li> <li><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots:</b> 6 Equipment Points</li> <li><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots:</b> 7 Equipment Points</li> <li><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots:</b> 8 Equipment Points</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Follow-Up Transformation Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Shared Grace (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Transformation (\u2022)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> <b>Persistent Manifestation:</b> Manifested gear no longer dissolves when separated from your character's person. It remains fully physical, retaining all of its statistics and visual aesthetics, as long as your Transformation remains active.<br /> <b>Loaning Gear:</b> You can manifest an item, loan it to a teammate or NPC, and then manifest completely separate gear for yourself from your remaining Equipment Point Budget.<br /> <b>Reflexive Recall:</b> You can reflexively dissolve loaned gear into light at any distance, immediately reclaiming those Equipment Budget points.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Cosmic Essence (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Transformation (\u2022)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> <b>Infinite Mundane Supply:</b> Transformed gear never runs out of mundane ammunition, battery life, charges, or internal fuel blocks.<br /> <b>No Reload Actions:</b> This overrides the Reload or Battery Capacity traits of underlying item templates, meaning your character never spends actions to reload in combat.<br /> <b>Supernatural Exclusions:</b> This benefit waives only mundane logistical costs; abilities requiring supernatural resources (such as Pure Spark abilities costing Spark) must still be paid normally.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Sample Transformation Equipment Loadouts</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loadout 1: The Starlight Marksman</b></span><br /> <b>Transformation Rating:</b> \u2022 (4 Equipment Points)<br /> <b>Concept:</b> A long-range attacker whose magical outfit resembles an astronomical sailor uniform.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Magical Weapon</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A polished, crystal-tipped wand shaped like a shooting star that fires concentrated bursts of blinding pink starlight.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Heavy Pistol</b> (2 Points) \u2014 Damage 2, Range 20/40/80, Size 1. <i>(Note: Cosmic Essence keeps ammunition infinite without reloads).</i></li> </ul><b>2. Defensive Attire</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A high-collared velvet vest with embroidered golden ribbons that magically deflects incoming impacts.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Kevlar Vest</b> (2 Points) \u2014 Armor 1/2 (General 1 / Ballistic 2).</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loadout 2: The Floral Vanguard</b></span><br /> <b>Transformation Rating:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022 (6 Equipment Points)<br /> <b>Concept:</b> A frontline brawler and defender themed around roses and thorned vines.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Primary Weapon</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> An elegant lace parasol lined with razor-sharp metallic rose petals that spins to slice through enemies.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Medium Melee Weapon / Longsword</b> (2 Points) \u2014 Damage 2, Size 2, Lethal.</li> </ul><b>2. Barrier Armor</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A glowing, translucent rose-gold tiara that projects a hard-light barrier around the wearer's body during combat.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Tactical Vest</b> (3 Points) \u2014 Armor 3/2 (General 3 / Ballistic 2).</li> </ul><b>3. Utility Item</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A floating compact mirror that emits a harsh, dazzling beam of sunlight when snapped open.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Tactical Searchlight</b> (1 Point) \u2014 Eliminates darkness penalties in a 20-yard cone and can inflict vision penalties on enemies.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loadout 3: The Cyber-Idol Berserker</b></span><br /> <b>Transformation Rating:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (8 Equipment Points)<br /> <b>Concept:</b> A futuristic magical warrior whose form radiates hard-light holograms and neon energy.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Heavy Weapon</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A pair of oversized, neon-pink robotic gauntlets decorated with kitten ears that strike with concussive shockwaves.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Heavy Melee Weapon / Greatsword</b> (3 Points) \u2014 Damage 3, Size 3, Lethal, Two-Handed.</li> </ul><b>2. Battle Suit</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A sleek, holographic seifuku armored dress woven from shifting digital patterns that absorbs heavy gunfire and slashes.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Riot Armor</b> (3 Points) \u2014 Armor 3/4 (General 3 / Ballistic 4).</li> </ul><b>3. Sensory Gear</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> Wing-shaped hair barrettes that pulse with a soft blue light, translating heat signatures and movement through walls into the user's mind.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Thermal / Night-Vision Goggles</b> (2 Points) \u2014 Completely ignores concealment penalties from darkness, fog, or heavy smoke.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Loadout 4: The Seraphic Sovereign</b></span><br /> <b>Transformation Rating:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (8 Equipment Points Budget)<br /> <b>Concept:</b> A high-flying, heavy-hitting battlefield controller adorned in six glowing hard-light wings and celestial plate mail.<br /> <b>1. Flight System (3 Equipment Points)</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> Six sweeping, translucent seraph wings composed of crystalline starlight and floating solar embers. They flare outwards upon transformation, allowing supersonic ascents, pinpoint aerial hovering, and instantaneous banking maneuvers.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Military Glider Rig / Flight System</b> (3 Points) \u2014 Grants full 3D aerial locomotion, hover capability, and high-altitude flight, completely ignoring ground hazards and terrain restrictions.</li> </ul><b>2. Primary Heavy Weapon (3 Equipment Points)</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> A massive, two-handed lance-bow forged from solid starlight that can impale armored foes at close range or strum solar shockwaves across the battlefield.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Heavy Melee Weapon / Greatsword</b> or <b>Assault Rifle</b> (3 Points) \u2014 Damage 3, Size 3, Lethal, Two-Handed. <i>(Combined with Cosmic Essence, ranged attacks never require reloads).</i></li> </ul><b>3. Seraphic Aegis Armor (2 Equipment Points)</b><ul><li><b>Form:</b> Shimmering, silver valkyrie plate mail adorned with star-sapphire filigree that projects a kinetic deflection barrier to turn away blades and gunfire.</li> <li><b>Function:</b> <b>Kevlar / Tactical Vest</b> (2 Points) \u2014 Armor 2/1 (General 2 / Ballistic 1).</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Mascot (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Social Merit<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <i>Special (The Shared Mascot): Multiple characters can buy into the same Mascot, pooling their bond to elevate their natural social ties into Metaphysical Sympathetic Links. Merit benefits do not require line of sight or physical proximity, functioning globally across the sympathetic network.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>I. Dual-Function Utility: Mentor &amp; Ephemeral Entity</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>1. The Mentor Connection</b><br /> In narrative downtime and off-screen support, the Mascot doubles directly as a <b>Mentor Merit</b> with a rating equal to your Mascot Merit dots:<br /> <br /> <b>Mentor Expertise:</b> Upon creating the Mascot, designate <b>three Skills</b> matching its narrative role and esoteric origin (e.g., <i>Occult, Empathy, Investigation</i>). One Skill may be substituted for <i>Resources</i> if the Mascot manages mystical stockpiles or pocket-dimension gear.<br /> <br /> <b>Mentor Favors:</b> Once per session, any character sharing the Mascot Merit can ask it for a favor or guidance within its fields of expertise. If a test is required to secure the favor, the Mascot automatically achieves <b>successes equal to its Mascot rating</b> without rolling.<br /> <br /> <b>Unseen Action:</b> The Storyteller may have the Mascot act independently in the background on behalf of the team (such as researching an enemy's Ban/Bane or scouting Twilight).<br /> <br /> <b>2. On-Screen Ephemeral Presence (Rank = Mascot Rating)</b><br /> When stepping into an active scene, the Mascot manifests as a full <b>Ephemeral Entity</b> whose <b>Rank</b> equals the Mascot Merit rating (Rank 1 to Rank 5):<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 1 Mascot (\u2022):</b> 5\u20138 Attribute dots (Power, Finesse, Resistance); Max Essence 10; 1\u20133 Numina; Influence \u2022 (e.g., <i>Hope</i> or <i>Friendship</i>); Twilight Form + 1 Manifestation Effect (typically <i>Fettered</i> to an animal/toy disguise or <i>Materialized</i>).<br /> <b>Rank 2 Mascot (\u2022\u2022):</b> 9\u201314 Attribute dots; Max Essence 15; 3\u20135 Numina; Influence \u2022\u2022; Twilight Form + 2 Manifestation Effects.<br /> <b>Rank 3 Mascot (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> 15\u201325 Attribute dots; Max Essence 20; 5\u20137 Numina; Influence \u2022\u2022\u2022; Twilight Form + 3 Manifestation Effects.<br /> <b>Rank 4 Mascot (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> 26\u201335 Attribute dots; Max Essence 25; 7\u20139 Numina; Influence \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Twilight Form + 4 Manifestation Effects.<br /> <b>Rank 5 Mascot (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> 36\u201345 Attribute dots; Max Essence 50; 9\u201311 Numina; Influence \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Twilight Form + 5 Manifestation Effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>II. Progressive Bond Abilities</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Spark of Companionship):</b> The group gains an extra, shared <b>Team Aspiration</b> slot. Fulfilling this goal awards a full Experience Beat to every player connected to the Mascot, regardless of location. The Mascot updates this goal at the start of each story chapter based on the circle's emotional state.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Unconditional Support):</b> Characters become completely immune to the negative passive supernatural auras of teammates sharing the same Mascot (such as Werewolf Lunacy, Promethean Disquiet, or Vampiric predatory tension). Unlocks <b>Sympathetic Shielding</b>: once per session, when a remote ally resolves a relationship Condition by sacrificing for the team, you can reflexively spend 1 Willpower to flash the bond across space, causing both characters to instantly regain all spent Willpower.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Shared Destiny / Harmonized Fate):</b> At the start of any scene where the split or unified team works toward a common goal, all members gain the <b>Harmonized Fate</b> Condition for free. Under this Condition, characters perform Teamwork actions remotely through the sympathetic network (+2 bonus per secondary actor success). Additionally, the Mascot can act as an independent secondary actor rolling a static pool of 4 dice to assist.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Esoteric Conduit / Sympathetic Transmutation):</b> Once per scene as an instant action, a character can transfer their native Resource points (such as Mana, Vitae, Essence, or Plasm) directly to any remote teammate sharing the Mascot. The Mascot converts the fuel type into the native energy required by the receiver at a 1:1 ratio. Transfers cannot exceed the receiver's standard per-turn expenditure limits; mortals without a supernatural fuel track send or receive Willpower.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Ultimate Unity):</b> Unlocks the <b>Overdrive</b> Condition for peak group synchronization, granting the entire team peak combat coordination and resource sharing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>III. Core Rules &amp; Systemic Constraints</b></span><br /> <b>Integrity of Friendship:</b> The network is fueled exclusively by genuine attachment. Infighting, betrayal, or mutual resentment fractures the sympathetic link, disabling all Mascot benefits between those specific characters until they reconcile. Widespread group fragmentation completely suppresses the Merit for all members.<br /> <b>Essence Sustenance &amp; Bleed Protection:</b> As long as the Mascot remains in proximity to its bonded team, it does not suffer standard Essence bleed. It regains 1 Essence per day automatically while near its circle, and can harvest additional Essence whenever a team member fulfills a Virtue, Vice, or the shared Team Aspiration.<br /> <b>Bans &amp; Banes:</b> Every Mascot possesses a behavioral <b>Ban</b> (e.g., <i>&quot;Must never ignore a crying child&quot;</i>) and a physical <b>Bane</b> (commonly <i>Cold Iron, Chalk,</i> or <i>True Starlight</i>).<br /> <b>Combat Discorporation:</b> If a Mascot's Corpus is reduced to 0, it discorporates into raw Ephemera and reverts to its anchor point. It cannot manifest on-screen or grant Mentor favors until its Essence refills to at least 1 point.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Sample Mascot Ephemeral Entities</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Pip, the Starlight Lop (Mascot \u2022 / Rank 1 Ephemeral Entity)</b></span><br /> <b>Concept:</b> A tiny, winged rabbit-moth hybrid with plush fur and star-shaped eyes that acts as an encouraging companion for a fledgling magical protector.<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1<br /> <b>Mascot Mentor Rating:</b> \u2022 (1 auto-success on Mentor favor rolls)<br /> <b>Mentor Skills:</b> Empathy, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 2, Finesse 3, Resistance 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 4 | <b>Size:</b> 2 | <b>Corpus:</b> 4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5 | <b>Defense:</b> 2 | <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Max Essence:</b> 10 (Max spend per turn: 1)<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Influence: Hope \u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Innocuous, Pathfinder, Sign<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Fettered (bound to a glowing star-ribbon keychain)<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Pip cannot refuse a sweet floral blossom or sugar cube offered with genuine affection.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Cold Iron.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Professor Barnaby (Mascot \u2022\u2022 / Rank 2 Ephemeral Entity)</b></span><br /> <b>Concept:</b> A miniature, brass clockwork owl with glowing quartz lenses that perches on shoulders to analyze occult anomalies and offer tactical advice.<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Mascot Mentor Rating:</b> \u2022\u2022 (2 auto-successes on Mentor favor rolls)<br /> <b>Mentor Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Science<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 5, Resistance 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8 | <b>Size:</b> 3 | <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9 | <b>Defense:</b> 4 | <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Max Essence:</b> 15 (Max spend per turn: 2)<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Influence: Clarity \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Innocuous<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Fettered (bound to an antique brass pocket watch)<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must pause and tilt its head to listen whenever a mechanical clock chimes within earshot.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Strong magnetic fields (which disrupt its internal gearwork).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Kitsu-Sama (Mascot \u2022\u2022\u2022 / Rank 3 Ephemeral Entity)</b></span><br /> <b>Concept:</b> A nine-tailed fox entity with silk-white fur and starlight-tipped tails, serving as a seasoned spiritual strategist and mystic conduit for a veteran circle.<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <b>Mascot Mentor Rating:</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022 (3 auto-successes on Mentor favor rolls)<br /> <b>Mentor Skills:</b> Investigation, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 12 | <b>Size:</b> 4 | <b>Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14 | <b>Defense:</b> 6 | <b>Speed:</b> 19<br /> <b>Max Essence:</b> 20 (Max spend per turn: 3)<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Influence: Valor \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (starlight foxfire), Emotional Aura, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Seek<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Reaching, Fettered (bound to an embroidered fox mask)<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot turn its back or dematerialize while an innocent is crying or pleading for help in its line of sight.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Holy salt water or a shrine bell melted down by dragon-fire. <hr />The idea here is that Magical Girls of all types would get these two Merits: the Mascot provides mechanics bridging different metaphysics and allowing a team of Magical Girls to coordinate their efforts to an extent that most in the Chronicles of Darkness can't manage; and the Transformation gives them the costume and\u200b a set of tools that's immensely useful but n not inherently overpowered: since it's all just reskinned \u201cordinary technology\u201d, it doesn't give the Magical Girl anything that cont be acquired through ordinary Resources. Though as some of the sample loadouts indicate, there's a lot you can do with \u201cordinary\u201d equipment. <br /> <br /> The next step is to go through the various supernaturals in the Chronicles of Darkness and develop for each of them a z-splat or equivalent tailored to recast that supernatural type as a Magical Girl. To start it off, here's a Merit-based Template (**Hurt Locker** style) designed to give you a \u201cblue book Magical Girl\u201d: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Pure Spark (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Mental Merit<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal Only (No supernatural templates), Transformation (\u2022) Merit.<br /> <i>Note: All benefits are dormant in civilian form and only apply while Transformed.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Core Mechanics:</b><br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Unyielding Resolve):</b> Grants complete immunity to passive supernatural auras generated by external threats (such as enemy Lunacy or Disquiet). Additionally, add your full Composure rating as a defense modifier against any active mind-control, coercion, or memory-altering supernatural powers.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (The Blindfold of Hope):</b> Grants complete immunity to Breaking Points resulting from witnessing supernatural phenomena, cosmic anomalies, or horrific monsters. Standard breaking points still apply if you personally commit acts of violence or violate your own moral code.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Spark of Conviction):</b> Unlocks the Conviction power stat at rating 1 (raised independently of Merits using standard Experiences at a cost of 5 Experiences per dot). You gain an energy pool called Spark, equal to 10 + Conviction. You can spend Spark per turn up to your Conviction limit to add +2 dice per point to any physical attribute action or combat roll. You regenerate Spark completely upon fulfilling your civilian Virtue or shielding a teammate from harm.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Empowered Aegis):</b> You use your Conviction rating as a permanent Clash of Wills modifier. Whenever an external power targets you with an effect that allows a supernatural resistance stat, you substitute your Conviction stat instead.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Sovereign Identity):</b> Grants complete immunity to any supernatural powers that command your actions, force physical possession of your body, or actively manipulate your emotional state (such as high-tier Vampiric Dominate or Majesty). Powers that would rob you of your turn or agency simply fail against you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Spark-Fueled Styles</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Pure Spark Merit.<br /> <i>Note: Purchased as separate, progressive Styles. Fueled by the Pure Spark Merit's energy pool and only available while transformed.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Retribution</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Strike the Wicked):</b> Spend 1 Spark to grant your transformed attacks the 9-Again rule for the turn (8-Again against known supernatural targets).<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Brand of Justice):</b> Spend 2 Spark upon successfully damaging a supernatural target to leave a burning brand on their soul; for the rest of the scene, they cannot use stealth/invisibility powers, and your allies gain +1 to all attack rolls against them.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Burden of Guilt):</b> Spend 3 Spark and roll Presence + Intimidation + Conviction vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. On a success, the target is filled with sudden remorse, losing their next Action.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Sanctuary</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Warding Light):</b> Spend 1 Spark as a reflexive action to add your Conviction rating to your Defense against a single incoming attack.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Aegis Circle):</b> Spend 2 Spark as an instant action to project a protective dome with a radius equal to your Conviction in yards. For a number of turns equal to your Composure, anyone inside the circle gains General Armor equal to your Conviction against external attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Cleanse the Taint):</b> Spend 3 Spark and touch a cursed, debuffed, or mind-controlled teammate. Roll Conviction + Medicine vs. the original caster's activation pool; success immediately breaks the magical affliction.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Radiance</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Piercing Gaze):</b> Spend 1 Spark to see through all mundane illusions, magical glamours, or physical disguises in your line of sight for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Blinding Beacon):</b> Spend 2 Spark as an instant action to flare your outfit. Enemies within 10 yards must roll Wits + Stamina or suffer the Blind Tilt for turns equal to your Conviction. Linked allies are immune and gain +1 to their next roll.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Restorative Grace):</b> Spend 3 Spark and roll Presence + Empathy + Conviction. Each success instantly heals 1 point of Bashing or Lethal damage on a teammate within eyesight, or removes a negative mental Condition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Wrath</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Relentless Force):</b> Spend 1 Spark to allow your physical attacks to ignore a target's Armor rating up to an amount equal to your Conviction for the rest of the turn.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Monster Slayer):</b> Spend 2 Spark when attacking a supernatural creature to convert your transformed weapon's damage profile into Aggravated damage for that single strike.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Overwhelming Tide):</b> Spend 3 Spark upon making a successful attack to inflict an automatic knockdown, which throws the target back yards equal to your Conviction and inflicts the Knocked Down Tilt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Devotion</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Share the Burden):</b> Spend 1 Spark as a reflexive action to transfer up to 2 points of damage dealt to a visible ally directly to your own health track as Bashing damage instead.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Sacrificial Surge):</b> Spend 2 Spark when your health enters your rightmost three boxes to completely ignore all wound penalties for the rest of the scene and gain a +2 bonus to all rolls while in this critical state.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Ultimate Offering):</b> Spend 3 Spark and accept 1 point of un-absorbable Lethal damage to grant all allies within your line of sight 1 instantly regained spent Resource point and a +2 bonus to their next roll.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Epiphany</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Cosmic Intuition):</b> Spend 1 Spark to ensure that for the rest of the scene, you cannot be ambushed or surprised, and your Defense is never reduced to 0 from unseen attackers or traps.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Thread Tracker):</b> Spend 2 Spark on a target and roll Wits + Occult + Conviction. Success reveals a glowing spiritual thread linking them to their master, haven, or absolute vulnerability, granting a +3 tracking and research bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Prescient Dodge):</b> Spend 3 Spark as a reflexive action when targeted by an attack to displace yourself up to your Speed rating in yards away, causing the incoming attack to automatically miss.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Style: Salvation</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Dot (Calming Presence):</b> Spend 1 Spark to emit a soothing aura requiring all supernatural targets within 5 yards actively in a frenzy or rage state to roll their respective resistance stat minus your Conviction or have their frenzy instantly suppressed for the turn.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Dots (Sever the Beast):</b> Spend 2 Spark upon executing a successful Brawl or Weapon attack to inflict no physical damage and completely block the target from spending their native fuel stat for a number of turns equal to your Conviction.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dots (Human Guise):</b> Spend 3 Spark, lock eyes with a transformed or monstrous creature, and roll Presence + Persuasion + Conviction vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. Success forcefully reverts them to their mundane, civilian human appearance for the rest of the scene. <hr />As mentioned before, this is basically an adaptation of WoD's Imbued Hunters into the Chronicles of Darkness setting, but reframed in the context of Magical Girls. \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T19:40:34-07:00","id":1563988,"title":"","content":"On <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>' checklist:<br /> <br /> <b><u>1. Weaponized Femininity</u></b><br /> - [ ] Accessories as items of power<br /> Check. The Transformation Merit allowing you to reskin functional gear as magical accessories covers this. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Vanity legitimated without &quot;glory/honor&quot;<br /> Please elaborate on what you're referring to here. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Cute, Feminine and Romantic motifs<br /> Needs work. The fact that the sample equipment reskins are cute and feminine works for this; but I'm not sure where else to go with this. Maybe something could be done with Striking Looks? <br /> <br /> - [ ] Emotional engagement<br /> Under the Mascot Merit, I made a point to have the various team synergy capabilities be dependent on <br /> <br /> <u><b>2. Coming of Age</b></u><br /> - [ ] 10 - 14 years old protagonists<br /> There's a Storyteller's Vault supplement called Fragile Innocence which serves as a 2e update of World of Darkness: Innocents. Apply that to a MG character, and you get your 10\u201314 year old protagonists. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Oni-like adult villains (preferably women)<br /> I haven't gotten to the villains side of this yet. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Mature-adjacent Alter-Ego<br /> This would involve building on the Transformation Merit. Maybe add another Merit for those protagonists that are built according to Fragile Innocence that results in the Transformed MG being effectively 15\u201318 \u2014 that is, what the young, still-maturing girl will be like in a few more years, after she's done growing up. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Mundane life milestones discussed (school, work, marriage)<br /> The trick here is to come up with a way of doing this that's compatible with 11 different gamelines (12, if you count blue book protagonists as their own gameline). <br /> <br /> <u><b>3. Empowerment</b></u><br /> - [ ] Scepter as soft symbol of authority<br /> - [ ] Rebellion against imposed roles<br /> Not sure what you have in mind for these. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Transformation granting autonomy<br /> Since Transformation serves as a perfect disguise, what the MG does while transformed has almost no impact on her civilian life. Add a \u201cfully mature\u201d supplemental Merit to that, and her activities as a MG are free from the social consequences of being underage. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Idealism validated<br /> Maybe under the Pure Spark Merit, Conviction should be recast as Idealism. This wouldn't help with any of the other MGs; but the Imbued MG would literally be empowered by her idealism. <br /> <br /> Maybe tie a mechanic to the MG's Virtue-equivalent? <br /> <br /> <u><b>4. Relationships and Emotion</b></u><br /> - [ ] Bonds and friendship between women<br /> The Mascot Merit is built around this. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Hope and dreams can prevail and heal<br /> - [ ] Magic is positive personal expression<br /> - [ ] Emotional sincerity as source of Strength<br /> Not sure what game engine support is needed here. <br /> <br /> <u><b>5. Superhero Core</b></u><br /> - [ ] Compact of \u5909\u8eab\u30d2\u30ed\u30a4\u30f3 and superpowers<br /> - [ ] Secret Identity - Dual Life tension<br /> Transformation Merit is built with these in mind. <br /> I should probably tie the Transformation Merit to an item. <br /> <br /> - [ ] Extraordinary duty to protect Humanity<br /> - [ ] Otherworldly Cute Mascot<br /> Covered by the Mascot Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T21:51:50-07:00","id":1563989,"title":"","content":"Loved the work, first of all it's excellent as basis. We can get a lot out of this simple 2 merits structure. Worst case scenario a game of Magical Girls start with a free dot in each, so it's an easy and low power setup to get running the baseline.<br /> <br /> Considerations:<br /> <br /> Transformation brings more than common equipment to the game: it smuggles it. You can get those items anywhere, past any inspection, it can't be tracked and you're given a &quot;burn ID&quot; of sorts that use it in the open then drop out of sight taking the offending material with it.<br /> <br /> My question is just if the benefits and equip dots are balanced for this. The answer may be yes.<br /> <br /> A more pressing matter: can a Transformation include other Merit-based magic objects? The various splats also introduce various Merits to represent objects produced or modified by the supernatural that may fit, actually pretty well, the genre.<br /> <br /> But adding the smuggling benefits to those items may, or may not, be too much. Tentative take: Transformation also unlocks access to any other Merit that gives access to equipment of any kind. Merits acquired like that become part of the Transformation load out rather than existing independently.<br /> <br /> Subsuming found items into a Transformation may be possible, but as default the items are developments of the Transformation from the start.<br /> <br /> What this adds: Magical Girls can access item merits across splats. Not only does it increase tools to customize their equipment (a genre staple), also facilitate a frequently overlooked means of integrating splats or crossing over key capabilities.<br /> <br /> Mortal MGs in particular get a solid avenue to invest XP in powerful effects without loosing characterization as mortals. They get more out of being Magical Girls instead, as more magic.<br /> <br /> Note: Identity Shield may be only Presence + Supernatural Tolerance, making the acquisition of Conviction even more relevant and MGs with low pools have reason to not try their luck. If it is meant to be too hard, it may be Presence + Subterfuge + Supernatural Tolerance always. Both work for me and confirm Superman as a Magical Girl.<br /> <br /> Shared Grace and Cosmic Essence could be mortal only. Alternatively, they could be cheaper to splats but cost splat-specific fuel to make happen. Also just occurred to me how close Transformation can become of a Lantern Ring or a Utility Belt, and I think those are good to lean on for possible new Merits.<br /> <br /> Hardest for me is to evaluate the Mascot for now, but I think it is a bit too powerful and anyway needs some key conceptual revisions.<br /> <br /> 1. Mascots need physicality. Even when they're truly abnormal beings, they're also estranged from their reality/people to remain with their charges. I think Ephemeral rules are not the best to capture them.<br /> <br /> 2. Power imbalance is also a staple: even the most powerful mascots are rarely able to help with the main action. Their expertise is support to the main magic itself and the basics on the villains, otherwise have mundane abilities and civilian skill levels at them.<br /> <br /> 3. We must be careful to not make a shared Mascot too powerful, especially not to shadow the splat-specific equivalents like a Totem. The result should also preferably equally support groups with multiple or single Mascots.<br /> <br /> I'm really weary of Esoteric Conduit. It doesn't just makes for a weird description of what's going on, but can severely impact the regular themes of the original lines as each splat has it expressed above all in their farming methods.<br /> <br /> Friendship is magic, but should this magic be strong enough that a Vampire never feeds or a Demon never needs venture into Infrastructure to refuel?<br /> <br /> On Pure Spark I'd switch Unyielding Resolve and The Blindfold of Hope. Witnessing magic without going bananas is the earliest must have, while immunity to auras from the get go is a bit too much. A Magical Girl still in the stage where exposure scares simply doesn't has this Merit yet.<br /> <br /> Spark of Conviction maybe should be 5th dot? Also Empowered Aegis should be something it brings with the stat, already.<br /> <br /> Didn't analyze the Style Merits yet, just noticed they look a lot like effective splat powers since they combine variety of powers with use of a supernatural fuel. Maybe use Willpower instead and then make something to convert Spark into Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T02:01:42-07:00","id":1563990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loved the work, first of all it's excellent as basis. We can get a lot out of this simple 2 merits structure. Worst case scenario a game of Magical Girls start with a free dot in each, so it's an easy and low power setup to get running the baseline.<br /> <br /> Considerations:<br /> <br /> Transformation brings more than common equipment to the game: it smuggles it. You can get those items anywhere, past any inspection, it can't be tracked and you're given a &quot;burn ID&quot; of sorts that use it in the open then drop out of sight taking the offending material with it.<br /> <br /> My question is just if the benefits and equip dots are balanced for this. The answer may be yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I don't know. It's something that should be playtested, or at least reviewed by someone who has a more intimate knowledge of what a Merit dot is worth than I have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more pressing matter: can a Transformation include other Merit-based magic objects? The various splats also introduce various Merits to represent objects produced or modified by the supernatural that may fit, actually pretty well, the genre.<br /> <br /> But adding the smuggling benefits to those items may, or may not, be too much. Tentative take: Transformation also unlocks access to any other Merit that gives access to equipment of any kind. Merits acquired like that become part of the Transformation load out rather than existing independently.<br /> <br /> Subsuming found items into a Transformation may be possible, but as default the items are developments of the Transformation from the start.<br /> <br /> What this adds: Magical Girls can access item merits across splats. Not only does it increase tools to customize their equipment (a genre staple), also facilitate a frequently overlooked means of integrating splats or crossing over key capabilities.<br /> <br /> Mortal MGs in particular get a solid avenue to invest XP in powerful effects without loosing characterization as mortals. They get more out of being Magical Girls instead, as more magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shared Grace and Cosmic Essence suggest a possible solution here: add another Merit, like them, that lets you add a splat-specific magical item to your loadout. I could see rating it equal to the dot rating of the magical item, effectively doubling its cost; but that might be overkill, with a more reasonable cost being something like two dots per magical item Merit for the \u201csmuggling\u201d feature.<br /> <br /> There should be an ability to spend some downtime reconfiguring the Transformation's accessories, effectively redistributing the equipment points. <br /> <br /> And Transformation should almost certainly be tied to a Transformation Item that the Magical Girl has to carry with her in order to Transform. If it gets taken away while she's not transformed, she's just a regular girl. This helps mitigate the potency of the smuggling effect, though it remains a key feature of what the Merit provides. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: Identity Shield may be only Presence + Supernatural Tolerance, making the acquisition of Conviction even more relevant and MGs with low pools have reason to not try their luck. If it is meant to be too hard, it may be Presence + Subterfuge + Supernatural Tolerance always. Both work for me and confirm Superman as a Magical Girl.<br /> <br /> Shared Grace and Cosmic Essence could be mortal only. Alternatively, they could be cheaper to splats but cost splat-specific fuel to make happen. Also just occurred to me how close Transformation can become of a Lantern Ring or a Utility Belt, and I think those are good to lean on for possible new Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardest for me is to evaluate the Mascot for now, but I think it is a bit too powerful and anyway needs some key conceptual revisions.<br /> <br /> 1. Mascots need physicality. Even when they're truly abnormal beings, they're also estranged from their reality/people to remain with their charges. I think Ephemeral rules are not the best to capture them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I was thinking Ephemeral Entity because those rules are available in nearly every book; the physicality can be implemented through Manifestations such as Materialize or Claim (but, unlike with Werewolf, the Claiming is limited to simple animals like cats or bunnies; not people). That, and there are some examples of Mascots who hang around a Magical Girl in her civilian identity and yet nobody other than the magical girl is able to see it. <br /> <br /> But if Ephemeral Entity rules turn out to be inappropriate, there's always the Horror rules found in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> pp.140\u2013143; normally used to represent \u201cmonsters of the week\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Power imbalance is also a staple: even the most powerful mascots are rarely able to help with the main action. Their expertise is support to the main magic itself and the basics on the villains, otherwise have mundane abilities and civilian skill levels at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe tone down their Potency/Rank? Instead of setting it equal to the Mascot dot rating, maybe set it at half that (rounding up)? So Potency/Rank 1 at Mascot 1 or 2; 2 at 3 or 4; 3 at 5. Likewise when functioning as a Mentor; or maybe require that you purchase the Mascot <i>as </i>a Mentor, and turn the current \u201cMascot Merit\u201d into a supplemental Merit to that which defines the magical amping of friendship bonds. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. We must be careful to not make a shared Mascot too powerful, especially not to shadow the splat-specific equivalents like a Totem. The result should also preferably equally support groups with multiple or single Mascots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; if you want the effects of a Totem, get an Uratha as one of your Magical Girls, and have her incorporate the other Magical Girls into a Hunting Party for a Pack. (See <b>Contagion Chronicles Player's Guide</b> for advice on crossover teams; though I think we're going beyond that advice here.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really wary of Esoteric Conduit. It doesn't just makes for a weird description of what's going on, but can severely impact the regular themes of the original lines as each splat has it expressed above all in their farming methods.<br /> <br /> Friendship is magic, but should this magic be strong enough that a Vampire never feeds or a Demon never needs venture into Infrastructure to refuel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Limit it to trading Willpower, then? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Pure Spark I'd switch Unyielding Resolve and The Blindfold of Hope. Witnessing magic without going bananas is the earliest must have, while immunity to auras from the get go is a bit too much. A Magical Girl still in the stage where exposure scares simply doesn't has this Merit yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spark of Conviction maybe should be 5th dot? Also Empowered Aegis should be something it brings with the stat, already.</div> </div> </div> </div>My inspiration for Spark of Conviction was the Conviction \u201cpower stat\u201d from <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b> (pp.32\u201333). I should probably hew closer to that, with Willpower as the fuel instead of introducing a new \u201cSparks\u201d fuel. In summary: <br /> <br /> Conviction is rated 1\u201310. It gives you a Resistance rating of roughly half that (0 at Conviction 1 up to 6 at Conviction 10) and lets you spend multiple Willpower/turn (from 2/turn at Conviction 4 up to 4/turn at Conviction 10). And once per chapter/session, you can do one of the following: (<b>Concentration</b>) ignore environmental penalties up to your Conviction rating; (<b>Drive</b>) add your Conviction to one Attribute for one roll; (<b>Endurance</b>) ignore wound penalties for a number of turns equal to your Conviction; (<b>Perception</b>) spend a Willpower point to \u201csee\u201d monsters for what they are. <br /> <br /> (The Conviction section is immediately followed by an Expanded Willpower section that presents other ways that the Storyteller might allow Willpower to be spent; I'd review that section to see which if any of those should be made available via Conviction.)<br /> <br /> I'd also add an increased \u201crecovery rate\u201d for Willpower: since you're empowered to burn through your Willpower more rapidly, you ought also to be able to restore it more easily. Instead of being able to fulfill a Virtue once per session and a Vice once per scene, perhaps allow both of these to be fulfilled a number of times equal to how many Willpower you can spend per turn? So once you hit Conviction 4, you can indulge your Vice twice per scene or fulfill your Virtue twice per chapter; at Conviction 7, that becomes three times each; and at Conviction 10, it's four times each\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563989#post1563989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't analyze the Style Merits yet, just noticed they look a lot like effective splat powers since they combine variety of powers with use of a supernatural fuel. Maybe use Willpower instead and then make something to convert Spark into Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, as above, just replace Spark with Willpower. (I also have an updated version of the Style Merits which I'll be posting soon. Recall what I said about the Pure Spark being a reskinning of <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>; the Style Merits are basically HtR's Edges reskinned to MG terminology.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T04:31:25-07:00","id":1563991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? I don't know. It's something that should be playtested, or at least reviewed by someone who has a more intimate knowledge of what a Merit dot is worth than I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut feeling is that it should start weaker, but could get a little more oomph as it goes. Going conservative, start at 2 dots with 1 Equipment Point, but each extra dot is 2 Equipment Points more, up to 7.<br /> <br /> But this is gut feeling, I'm actually just as much in the shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">add another Merit</div> </div> </div> </div>My current idea, and I think it can be a simple one and not so expensive, as you're already spending a lot in the basic Transformation and the item to be taken.<br /> <br /> I think 1 or 2 dots, it let you add more powerful items to the arsenal. Those items are built as separate Merits that can use any splat book, but they are part of your Transformed Inventory and even use Equipment Points to be called upon, either just 1 or equal to the rating of the item's own Merit. The item's Merit can't be at a higher rate than the Transformation Merit.<br /> <br /> No more is needed because the disadvantage is also built in: as part of your Inventory, they are not available outside a Transformation and everything it entails.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be an ability to spend some downtime reconfiguring the Transformation's accessories, effectively redistributing the equipment points.<br /> <br /> And Transformation should almost certainly be tied to a Transformation Item that the Magical Girl has to carry with her in order to Transform. If it gets taken away while she's not transformed, she's just a regular girl. This helps mitigate the potency of the smuggling effect, though it remains a key feature of what the Merit provides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a lot of where we should focus the attention for the Mascot. A staple of the genre, is that the critters are much more part of the intelligentsia behind the transformation than a capable companion for other tasks.<br /> <br /> Rather than just Transformation I'd call the Merit Compact of Transformation, the Mascot comes as the technician/guardian of the item.<br /> <br /> The Mascot, not the character, can fiddle with the Compact and change configurations. They can also sense where the Compact is at any time. The Compact only works with the correct user, but it has no intrinsic capacity to get back to her hands.<br /> <br /> Mascots know something about where they are coming and who's behind all this. They are the ones in control of how the Transformation manifests and every technical and form aspect of it. And that includes fiddling with it if things need adjustment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I was thinking Ephemeral Entity because those rules are available in nearly every book; the physicality can be implemented through Manifestations such as Materialize or Claim (but, unlike with Werewolf, the Claiming is limited to simple animals like cats or bunnies; not people). That, and there are some examples of Mascots who hang around a Magical Girl in her civilian identity and yet nobody other than the magical girl is able to see it.<br /> <br /> But if Ephemeral Entity rules turn out to be inappropriate, there's always the Horror rules found in Chronicles of Darkness pp.140\u2013143; normally used to represent \u201cmonsters of the week\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a case where the genre actually offers the simplest solutions rather than trying to put the known staples of the setting in.<br /> <br /> Mascots in the genre are technical advisors. They understand the transformation, powers, and what the MG has to deal with as a MG. All else are possible additions, not the other way around, the baseline Mascot is a talking pet for real with the expected needs and capacities. At most it is an impossible but not exceptional entity that has to hide in exchange for a few perks like wings or functional hands. Otherwise stat as a cat or bunny.<br /> <br /> What a baseline Mascot Merit should then offer is the ability of this pet to help with the technical side. What the Mascot does that matters?<br /> 1. They locate the Compact and the user. They have to bring one to the other by mundane means, though.<br /> 2. They know how this thing works, and how the main enemies work (even if that just means knowing a crash course on each splat). Their advice is highly specialized, with the pros and cons of being so.<br /> 3. They do maintenance. Magical Girls are not immune to the literal grit of reality, while magic does a lot to help they also have the Mascots doing menial but important tasks that are not tangential: a genre of feminine empowerment means one that recognizes forms of care that are frequently made invisible.<br /> 4. This maintenance includes mundane tasks. It isn't uncommon for Mascots to help with daily chores, mail, self care routines and other tasks a very helpful roommate would. They do what they can for their charge to save the world even if it isn't glamorous.<br /> 5. 3 and 4 are particularly important when the standard Magical Girl is 12-14yo. The Mascots have a big role in helping teens overprotected by the law and subject to curfew to get into situations they shouldn't. That's doubly relevant while they're not transformed and still have to walk around (but even if the are, they're still just small girls in costume and they know it).<br /> 6. As above, they fiddle with the magic, locate possible power ups, and generally help with or enable at all fine tuning the transformation.<br /> 7. If there are other Mascots around, they know how to contact each other, be it an alternative communication channel for PCs or a means to get news from other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> Progressive Bond Abilities are sure needed and must be linked to the Mascot, but otherwise I'd say the Mascot is very consistently a mundane help in the genre, they do what a small animal can do unless specifics. One big advantage a Mascot can carry in CofD that derives from the above is they may have working knowledge of local supernatural societies, so a Mascot has the ability to work as messenger and liaison with supernatural powers the MG can't meet in person.<br /> <br /> For those specifics, the Mascot should be a valid expression of other Merits. Allies, Mentor, even Resources, who knows, can be made into things your particular Mascot can do. Familiar isn't a bad choice, by the way.<br /> <br /> I'd add they are also fucking hard to kill, though not hard to harm. They frequently accept tasks that are too dangerous to their frail bodies with no hesitation, despite evidence that a task that seemed almost suicidal was indeed almost suicidal, and since we have little if any of them going KIA in the genre I think it's safe to say they at least expect to survive almost anything, if not in a state they're thrilled to experience.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point. Limit it to trading Willpower, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Best option IMO. Maybe add something to make Willpower recovery a little easier or let one member act as proxy for another to recover Willpower, but this may be too much.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My inspiration for Spark of Conviction was the Conviction \u201cpower stat\u201d from World of Darkness: Mirrors (pp.32\u201333). I should probably hew closer to that, with Willpower as the fuel instead of introducing a new \u201cSparks\u201d fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think hewing closer to the original would give a better feel, maybe a little amped only where the original caps itself lower than a regular Power Stat would, as here there is legit magic doing the job.<br /> <br /> For recovery, more opportunities of the same things don't seem like the best approach. IME it would put pressure on the scene without really making things much better. Instead I'd add some novel means to recover Willpower.<br /> <br /> Having additional Virtue/Vice is itself a good start as it broadens options rather than just require a double dose in short notice. We can have something in genre, maybe Willpower recovery through group activities with the other girls, as one of the focal themes is bonding and mutual care. 1 WP for part of a scene just being buddies with another MG, all of it when a complex activity engages the while group or a minimum number of relevant participants.<br /> <br /> One observation to the above: it is well within the genre that such scenes can occur across enemy lines. Caring for others and reinforcing relationships is the point, not only doing that within your current group.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1563990#post1563990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, as above, just replace Spark with Willpower. (I also have an updated version of the Style Merits which I'll be posting soon. Recall what I said about the Pure Spark being a reskinning of Hunter: the Reckoning; the Style Merits are basically HtR's Edges reskinned to MG terminology.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T08:33:18-07:00","id":1563993,"title":"","content":"Maybe some tweaking of Conviction is in order to better represent the Magical Girl genre. What I'm thinking right now is to scrap the Pure Spark Merit entirely; instead, mortal Magical Girls gain the ability to develop a Willpower-enhancing power stat inspired by the aforementioned Conviction but tailored more to the MG genre. Where Conviction is written in terms of confronting and overcoming the supernatural (very masculine energy), this trait should be tailored more to, hmm\u2026 <br /> <br /> Thinking aloud here: in HtR, there are three Virtues: Mercy, Vision, and Zeal. I'm not suggesting that we use these; only that they provide me with a framework for looking at the problem. Zeal is full of masculine energy; it's where you get your Avengers, Defenders, and Judges. Mercy is where I'd put the feminine energy, with the Innocents, Martyrs, and Redeemers. And the Visionaries would be neutral. Likewise, Deviant has Conviction and Loyalty with its Conviction having a lot in common with HtR's Zeal Creeds, whereas Loyalty leans now toward the Mercy side of things. In my attempt at setting up an adaptation of Princess the Hopeful in Deviant terms, the Radiant Princesses ended up as Guardians (\u201cRenegades\u201d with more Loyalty than Conviction) while the Twilight Princesses ended up as Nemeses (\u201cDevoted\u201d with more Conviction than Loyalty). <br /> <br /> This power stat I'm contemplating should be more Loyalty-esque or Merciful in nature than Conviction/Zealous. But how to model that? I'm also thinking that it might be used to strengthen your \u201cidealism validated\u201d goal; a literal implementation would be to call it Idealism and have the mortal Magical Girl literally empowered by her idealism. It should still be providing the basic protections against loss of agency (no Integrity loss for witnessing the Supernatural, protection against the mind-warping effects of supernatural auras, etc.); but it should also have something facilitating empathy and solving problems by understanding the other and finding common ground. Also emotional sincerity as source of strength. (There's also room to explore toxic femininity; but that's more a matter for the oni-like adult women you requested as the villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T08:37:27-07:00","id":1563994,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that other Magical Girls (the Monster Mash ones) will probably have to use their own systems for this sort of thing; because this Willpower-enhancing Power Stat is still a Power Stat; and giving anyone two Power Stats is problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T23:54:50-07:00","id":1564001,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. It's expected that the Bluebook MG will be its own thing and look more... Purified genre, so to speak, or at least neutral.<br /> <br /> [Sincerity] should keep the idea that it's not an alien source of power (even if it manifests through the Compact, that definitely is), but the same emotional depth everyone has, just being dealt with in a healthy way.<br /> <br /> The others will achieve the same by their own processes of coming to terms with what they are. The MGs have a positive relationship with their magic without neglecting its nature. The other splat MGs will grow as MGs learning not to empower their emotional expression, but to emotionally care for their own nature. What I'd expect is a change in how the disadvantages of high Power Stats manifest, or tools to deal with those disadvantages in a less destructive way.<br /> <br /> In a sense that reminds me the old concept of Golconda for Vampire. Not saying we must lean on it, but is a similarity worth thinking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T08:38:30-07:00","id":1564015,"title":"","content":"That's what got me looking at the Septemi about a page ago: they are, to the best of my knowledge, the closest thing that VtR has to the \u201cVirtuous Vampire\u201d in that that's what sets them apart from other Kindred: their Virtue. And while that's not Golconda or the Salubri, I think it (and their Bloodline Discipline, Abjurism, which is about defense against <s>the dark arts</s> supernatural threats) makes them a solid baseline for Vampiric Magical Girls \u2014 or at least a solid example of what you need out of a vampiric MG. <br /> <br /> (I'd go with the version of them provided in NMD's <b>Bloodlines: the Resurrected</b>, which generalizes them from <i>just</i> the Daeva to <i>any</i> Clan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T09:32:02-07:00","id":1564017,"title":"","content":"For the blue book Power Stat, perhaps rework or replace the active uses (Concentration, Drive, Endurance, and Perception) with something that (for instance) lets you spend a point of Willpower to force a vampire out of Frenzy, or otherwise de-escalate a potentially violent encounter. Maybe borrow from WoD's True Faith, but reskinned from a religious belief to a more prosaic belief in the fundamental goodness of people, and with the more overtly supernatural aspects toned down or removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T17:33:25-07:00","id":1564023,"title":"","content":"Deescalation is a good starting point. Rescue, too, where the point isn't to just navigate a scene or survive it, but move someone else through this.<br /> <br /> One relevant motif that occurs to me thinking of that is tactical exposing: while MGs can and do use defensive powers and barriers, those key actions require some level of unprotected contact with the threat, because the protection itself shows lack of confidence.<br /> <br /> This is something we do observe frequently in the genre, and it is also observed IRL in the job of negotiators and rescuers, professionals who are there precisely to intervene in dangerous situations to solve crises with minimum loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T23:50:08-07:00","id":1564067,"title":"","content":"Right. <b>Princess: the Hopeful</b> includes a Sensitivity mechanic where MGs can't help but pick up mental trauma when they see monstrous things; but I like this idea of tactical exposure better. It's not that you <i>have to</i> get hurt; it's that by leaving yourself vulnerable, you open up opportunities that wouldn't otherwise be there. <br /> <br /> There might even be something kind of like Risking Willpower in there: by leaving yourself vulnerable, you create an opportunity; if you succeed, then all's well; but if you fail, you get hurt. Conversely, there might be some martyrdom to it, where you accept that you <i>will </i>get hurt in exchange for achieving some feat that can't be achieved easily or at all otherwise. While it's unhealthy to rely on such a thing too much, it can be quite effective when relied on in moderation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:35:16-07:00","id":1564069,"title":"","content":"Beta draft of an Idealism power stat for an otherwise-mortal Magical Girl:<br /> <br /> (I stuck with the multiple Virtue refreshes because it's not about spamming the same Virtue multiple times in a single <i>scene</i>; it's about calling upon the Virtue multiple times in the same <i>chapter.</i> As well, I believe that there's a Merit somewhere that lets you take multiple Virtues.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Idealism</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Experiences per dot (Standard Power Stat cost)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal Only (No supernatural templates).<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Idealism is an expression of pure human empathy, moral courage, and earnest belief. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Passive Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Expanded Willpower Engine:</b> The maximum number of Willpower points the character can spend on a single action or resistance roll scales with her Idealism rating row limit (1 WP/turn at 1\u20133, 2 WP/turn at 4\u20136, 3 WP/turn at 7\u20139, and 4 WP/turn at 10). Each Willpower spent grants its standard +3 dice bonus or +2 resistance bonus; but they can't stack.</li> <li><b>Resistance &amp; Clash Modifier:</b> The character adds her full <b>Idealism rating</b> (+1 to +10) to all resistance dice pools and Clash of Wills checks against supernatural powers targeting her mind, emotional state, or Willpower.</li> <li><b>Integrity Anchor:</b> The character gains complete immunity to Integrity breaking points caused strictly by witnessing supernatural horrors, monsters, alien Infrastructure, or eldritch anomalies. Her everyday human identity remains grounded. (Standard breaking points still apply if she personally commits moral wrongs, betrays loved ones, or violates her own code).</li> <li><b>Empathetic Resonance:</b> Add <b>half Idealism (rounded down)</b> to all Empathy rolls and Social Maneuvering checks whenever her primary goal is to genuinely understand, comfort, or build trust with someone, rather than deceive or coerce them.</li> </ul><hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Active Feats of Idealism</b></span><br /> <br /> By spending 1 Willpower, the character can execute one of the following feats <b>once per chapter</b>:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Empathy &amp; Insight</b></span><ul><li><b>Concept:</b> Looking past a target\u2019s frightening exterior, angry fa\u00e7ade, or monstrous form to perceive the vulnerable person beneath.</li> <li><b>Mechanism:</b> Spend 1 Willpower as an instant action. For the remainder of the scene, the character intuitively perceives the target\u2019s core emotional state, their <b>Virtue</b>, <b>Vice</b>, or an <b>Aspiration/Touchstone</b> tied to what they are trying to protect or mourn.</li> <li><b>System Effect:</b> When using this insight to reach out, build trust, or de-escalate conflict, add <b>half Idealism (rounded down)</b> to all Empathy, Persuasion, or Clash of Wills rolls made to reach them.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. De-escalation &amp; Common Ground</b></span><ul><li><b>Concept:</b> An earnest, unarmored gesture of peace that creates a temporary pause in supernatural rage, opening space for human dialogue.</li> <li><b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Empathy + half Idealism (rounded down) vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower</li> <li><b>System Effect:</b> On a success, the character temporarily soothes an enemy\u2019s active frenzy, Death Rage, Disquiet, or predatory hostility for a number of turns equal to her Idealism rating.</li> <li><b>Social Impact:</b> Making this genuine attempt to find common ground <b>opens 1 Door</b> immediately on a target who would normally refuse to negotiate, or waives the standard wait time between Social Maneuvering Impression rolls for the scene.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Protection &amp; Reassurance</b></span><ul><li><b>Concept:</b> Stepping up to offer direct, personal support (&quot;I'm right here with you; you don't have to face this alone&quot;).</li> <li><b>Activation:</b> Spend 1 Willpower when offering direct help or standing firm to protect others. Choose one scope upon activation:<ul><li><b>Stage-Wide Anchor:</b> All allies on stage add <b>half Idealism (rounded down)</b> to their Resolve + Composure rolls to resist fear, horror, or mind-altering powers for the rest of the scene.</li> <li><b>Targeted Shield (One Person):</b> One specific ally or civilian nearby adds <b>Composure + half Idealism (rounded down)</b> to their resistance rolls against fear, horror, or emotional manipulation, and may immediately make a new resistance roll to break free from an active mental Tilt (such as Shaken, Terrified, or Thrall).</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Tactical Exposure</b></span><br /> <br /> To break through emotional walls or shield others, an Idealist can choose to deliberately lay down her emotional defenses and undergo an <b>Integrity Breaking Point</b>:<ul><li><b>Vicarious Exposure (Absorbing Trauma):</b> When a nearby ally, civilian, or enemy faces an Integrity, Clarity, or Humanity Breaking Point, the Idealist can step in emotionally as a reflexive action. The original target suffers no loss. The Idealist takes the Breaking Point on her own sheet instead (rolling Resolve + Composure + Idealism modifier). Because this is an act of profound self-sacrifice, taking on the Breaking Point instantly resets the once per chapter active use of her Idealism.</li> <li><b>Supercharged Olive Branch:</b> When activating <i>The Olive Branch</i>, she can accept an Integrity Breaking Point. If she does, the target cannot roll Supernatural Tolerance to resist\u2014their violent rage immediately stalls for turns equal to her Idealism rating.</li> <li><b>Absorbing Trauma via Aegis:</b> When using <i>Aegis of Devotion</i> on a single target, she can take an Integrity Breaking Point to instantly cure and remove a severe mental Condition or Tilt (like <i>Broken</i>, <i>Despair</i>, <i>Shaken</i>, or <i>Thrall</i>) from that target.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Virtue Engine: Feat Resets &amp; Deferred Refills</b></span><br /> <br /> Fulfilling her Virtue serves a dual purpose:<ul><li><b>Guaranteed Active Feat Reset:</b> Whenever she fulfills her Virtue (or takes on a Vicarious Breaking Point / resolves an encounter peacefully), she <b>instantly resets her once-per-chapter active feat use</b> (<i>Heart's Mirror</i>, <i>The Olive Branch</i>, or <i>Aegis of Devotion</i>). This reset occurs regardless of whether she refills Willpower.</li> <li><b>Flexible / Deferred Willpower Refills:</b> Fulfilling her Virtue grants the opportunity to completely refill her spent Willpower pool (up to her session cap based on Idealism). However, <b>she is not forced to take the refill immediately</b>\u2014she can bank that recovery opportunity and trigger the full Willpower refill later in the session when her pool is depleted.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T01:20:44-07:00","id":1564072,"title":"","content":"Liked it a lot.<br /> <br /> I think you changed your mind somewhere in the middle on what to name the active uses and the artifacts stayed.<br /> <br /> On the roll to interrupt someone's Frenzy-like state, what to do when a target is also making effort to break the state and take control? I like the idea of the MG being resisted by their supernatural tolerance, but something else could be there.<br /> <br /> Throwing ideas at the wall, what about rolling against double Supernatural Tolerance, and the target &quot;can&quot; choose to throw Composure at either side or abstain from the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T15:18:44-07:00","id":1564098,"title":"","content":"I ended up taking some inspiration from <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>, specifically the way that the Possessed in that game are given dot ratings for their Vices, which in turn serve as a sort of power stat. This flips that on its head, and removes the possession aspect, giving us a mechanism for turning a Virtue into a power stat. <br /> <br /> Try this: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Spark of Virtue</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Mental Merit<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal Only (No supernatural templates).<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Merit Points / 5 Experiences<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character\u2019s unyielding alignment with her chosen Virtue unlocks <b>Virtue</b> as a primary Power Stat at rating 1. Additional dots in Virtue are purchased independently as a Power Stat at a cost of <b>5 Experiences per dot</b> (up to a maximum rating of 10).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>The Virtue Power Stat</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Experiences per dot (Standard Power Stat cost)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue Gateway Merit (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Mortal Only (No supernatural templates).<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Virtue represents the reality-anchoring force of a character's core moral principle. It functions identically whether the character is in civilian form or transformed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Virtue Progression &amp; Scaling Table</b></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Virtue Rating</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Max Willpower / Turn</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Virtue Recoveries / Session</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Resistance &amp; Clash Modifier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Alignment &amp; Anchor Bonus (Half Virtue, Up)</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>1</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 time / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+1 die</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>2</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 time / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+1 die</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>3</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 time / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>4</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>5</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>6</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>7</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>8</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>9</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+5 dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>10</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4 Willpower / turn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4 times / session</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+5 dice</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Passive Capabilities (Universal)</b></span><ul><li><b>Expanded Willpower Engine:</b> The maximum number of Willpower points the character can spend in a single turn scales with her Virtue tier (1 WP/turn at 1\u20133, 2 WP/turn at 4\u20136, 3 WP/turn at 7\u20139, and 4 WP/turn at 10).<br /> <i>Expenditure Rule:</i> Multiple Willpower points spent in the same turn <b>cannot be stacked on the same roll or effect</b>. However, a character may spend multiple Willpower points in a turn for <i>different</i> purposes\u2014for example, spending 1 WP for +3 dice on an action roll, and 1 WP to gain a +2 resistance bonus or activate a Merit ability.</li> <li><b>Resistance &amp; Clash Modifier:</b> The character adds her full <b>Virtue rating</b> (+1 to +10) to all resistance dice pools and Clash of Wills checks against supernatural powers targeting her mind, emotional state, body, or Willpower.</li> <li><b>Integrity Anchor:</b> When making an Integrity Breaking Point roll caused by witnessing supernatural horrors, eldritch phenomena, or events that represent a direct affront to her Virtue, the character adds a <b>bonus equal to half her Virtue rating, rounded up</b> (+1 at ratings 1\u20132, up to +5 at ratings 9\u201310). On a success, her emotional response manifests as righteous <b>indignation or moral outrage</b> rather than shock, terror, or guilt.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Innate Active Feature (Universal)</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Virtuous Alignment</b></span><ul><li><b>Concept:</b> When taking an action that directly aligns with and expresses her specific Virtue, the character can tap her moral core to enhance her effort.</li> <li><b>Mechanism:</b> Once per scene, when making a roll for an action taken in strict accordance with her Virtue, the character may spend 1 Willpower to add <b>half her Virtue rating (rounded up)</b> as a bonus to that roll.</li> <li><b>Virtue Reset:</b> Whenever the character fulfills her Virtue under conditions of personal risk or self-sacrifice, this once-per-scene active use resets immediately.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Virtue Engine: Resets, Refill Limits, &amp; The Refill Gamble</b></span><ul><li><b>Guaranteed Feat Reset:</b> Fulfilling her Virtue under risk or self-sacrifice <b>always resets</b> her once-per-scene <i>Virtuous Alignment</i> active use.</li> <li><b>Refill Rate Limits:</b> Fulfilling her Virtue offers the opportunity to completely refill her spent Willpower pool. This recovery is subject to two strict limits:<ul><li><b>Session Limit:</b> A character can only recover Willpower through her Virtue a maximum number of times per session based on her Virtue rating (1 time at ratings 1\u20133, up to 4 times at rating 10).</li> <li><b>Scene Limit:</b> A Virtue <b>cannot refill Willpower more than once in a single scene</b>, regardless of how many times the Virtue is fulfilled during that scene.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Refill Gamble:</b> If the character fulfills her Virtue while her Willpower pool is only slightly depleted, she may <b>choose not to refill her Willpower</b>. Doing so does <b>not</b> consume one of her session's capped Virtue Refills. She retains that Refill slot and resets her active feat, gambling that she will fulfill her Virtue again in a later scene when her pool is low and she can gain maximum benefit from the recovery.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Vicarious Exposure (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), An Other-Directed Virtue.<br /> <br /> An <b>other-directed Virtue</b> is a moral anchor whose fundamental definition requires caring for, protecting, serving, comforting, or redeeming others (such as <i>Compassion</i>, <i>Justice</i>, <i>Mercy</i>, <i>Protection</i>, <i>Selflessness</i>, or <i>Devotion</i>), as opposed to a self-directed Virtue focused on individual discipline, personal mastery, or internal standards (such as <i>Pride</i>, <i>Fortitude</i>, or <i>Purity</i>). Because an other-directed character's moral identity is intrinsically tied to the well-being of the people around her, her conviction allows her to deliberately step into harm's way\u2014putting her own emotional safety on the line to absorb trauma and shield others from psychological collapse.<br /> <br /> By choosing to undergo a <b>Tactical Exposure</b>\u2014deliberately accepting an Integrity Breaking Point on her own sheet\u2014she unlocks the following capabilities:<ul><li><b>Vicarious Exposure (Absorbing Trauma):</b> When a nearby ally, civilian, or vulnerable character within line of sight is forced to make an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point roll, the character may declare a Tactical Exposure as a reflexive action. The original target suffers no loss and makes no roll; the character takes the Breaking Point on her own sheet instead, rolling <b>Resolve + Composure + Integrity Anchor Bonus</b>. Because taking on someone else's suffering is an act of profound self-sacrifice, absorbing a Breaking Point <b>instantly triggers a Virtue Reset</b> of her <i>Virtuous Alignment</i> active use.</li> <li><b>De-escalating Exposure:</b> As an instant action when confronting an enemy locked in an active state of supernatural rage (such as Vampiric frenzy, Werewolf Death Rage, Promethean Disquiet, or predatory hostility), the character may completely drop her emotional defenses and offer an unarmored gesture of peace. By accepting a Tactical Exposure, she rolls <b>Presence + Empathy + (half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to reach them. Because of her complete, undefended vulnerability, <b>the target cannot roll Supernatural Tolerance to resist or subtract from her roll</b>. On a success, the target's active rage or hostility is suppressed for a number of turns equal to her Virtue rating, creating a critical opening for dialogue.</li> <li><b>Absorbing Mental Conditions:</b> When an ally or civilian within line of sight is afflicted by a severe mental Condition or Tilt (such as <i>Broken</i>, <i>Despair</i>, <i>Shaken</i>, or <i>Thrall</i>), the character may accept a Tactical Exposure as an instant action. The target's mental Condition or Tilt is <b>instantly cured and removed</b>. If the character succeeds on her Breaking Point roll, her conviction processes the emotional shock cleanly; if she fails, she takes on a temporary mental Condition herself.</li> </ul><hr />In theory, there's should also be a follow-up Merit for self-directed Virtues; but I'm not sure that exploring that side of things is consistent with the mission statement. That is, the themes of magical girls are such that I could easily see requiring all magical girls to take other-directed Virtues. It's all about the relationships, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T15:23:51-07:00","id":1564099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564072#post1564072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liked it a lot.<br /> <br /> I think you changed your mind somewhere in the middle on what to name the active uses and the artifacts stayed.<br /> <br /> On the roll to interrupt someone's Frenzy-like state, what to do when a target is also making effort to break the state and take control? I like the idea of the MG being resisted by their supernatural tolerance, but something else could be there.<br /> <br /> Throwing ideas at the wall, what about rolling against double Supernatural Tolerance, and the target &quot;can&quot; choose to throw Composure at either side or abstain from the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me think about this. The latest Virtue power stat version doesn't have the version where you can force the end of frenzy without tactical exposure; so if would be a simple matter to say that the really can be opposed (Withstood?) by the raging creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T16:49:07-07:00","id":1564102,"title":"","content":"Revising the follow-up Merits:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Supplemental Virtue Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Vicarious Exposure (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), An Other-Directed Virtue.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue use</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <b>Universal Constraint (Communication Requirement):</b> None of the capabilities granted by this Merit can affect another character unless there is an active channel of communication between the character and the target (direct speech/vocal reassurance, eye contact, physical touch, or an active telepathic/empathic link). The target must be aware of the character's presence and gesture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Empathetic Aegis (Proactive Protection):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when an ally within line of sight is targeted by a fear effect, horror, or mind-altering power, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and call out to them, lock eyes, or reach for them. For the remainder of the scene, all allies with whom she maintains active communication add the character's <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to their resistance rolls and Breaking Point rolls against supernatural horror or fear.</li> <li><b>Vicarious Exposure (Absorbing Trauma):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]</i><br /> When a nearby ally or civilian is forced to make an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point roll, the character may declare a Tactical Exposure as a reflexive action, calling out their name, grabbing their hand, or locking eyes (&quot;Give it to me, look at me!&quot;). The original target suffers no loss and makes no roll; the character takes the Breaking Point on her own sheet instead, rolling <b>Resolve + Composure + Integrity Anchor Bonus</b>.</li> <li><b>De-escalating Touch (Soothing Rage):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting an enemy locked in active supernatural rage (such as Vampiric frenzy, Werewolf Death Rage, or Disquiet), the character steps into their line of sight, lowers her weapons, and directly speaks to or reaches for them. She <b>spends 1 Willpower</b> and rolls <b>Presence + Empathy + (half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to soothe them for turns equal to her Virtue rating.<ul><li><i>Unarmored Supercharge [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> If she voluntarily accepts a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) during this appeal, the target <b>cannot roll Supernatural Tolerance to resist</b>.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Soothing Burden (Condition Removal):</b> The character must make physical contact, lock eyes, or speak directly to the target (&quot;Breathe, I'm right here&quot;).<ul><li><i>Minor Relief [Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]:</i> <b>Spend 1 Willpower</b> as an instant action to clear a temporary mental Tilt (<i>Shaken</i>, <i>Terrified</i>, <i>Spooked</i>) from the target or allow them to immediately re-roll a failed resistance against an active mental Condition.</li> <li><i>Trauma Transfer [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> Accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) as an instant action to permanently cure and remove a severe mental Condition (<i>Broken</i>, <i>Despair</i>, <i>Thrall</i>) from the target, drawing the shock onto herself.</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Crucible of Conviction (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Self-Directed Virtue.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue use</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Unshakeable Sovereignty (Resisting Control):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when targeted by a supernatural power that would force her to act against her core nature, rewrite her memories, exert direct mind control, or corrupt her soul or flesh, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so grants her <b>complete immunity</b> to supernatural mind-control, memory modification, or horror-induced Breaking Points for the remainder of the scene (or grants an automatic success on a Clash of Wills against direct soul or bodily alteration).</li> <li><b>Crucible of Endurance (Overcoming Shock):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when afflicted by severe temporary physical or mental Tilts (such as <i>Stunned</i>, <i>Knocked Down</i>, <i>Shaken</i>, or <i>Blind</i>) or heavy wound penalties, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so instantly clears all temporary physical and mental Tilts and allows her to completely ignore all wound penalties and fatigue for a number of turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>.</li> <li><b>Purifying Exposure (Moral Triumph):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character chooses to suffer severe personal loss, physical injury, or social ruin specifically to refuse a moral compromise or uphold her personal code, any Integrity roll forced by that ordeal gains her <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b>. This action is a Tactical Exposure and does not require an available active slot. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her emotional response converts the trial into righteous moral pride, granting her a <b>+2 bonus on all Resolve and Composure rolls</b> for the remainder of the scene and <b>instantly resetting</b> her once-per-session active Virtue slot if it was spent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Eye of Revelation (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Virtue centered on Truth, Discernment, Wisdom, or Honesty.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue use</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <b>Nature:</b> This Merit can be purchased alongside either <i>Vicarious Exposure</i> or <i>Crucible of Conviction</i>, provided the character's Virtue embodies an element of truth-seeking, wisdom, or unmasking deception.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Piercing the Veil (Unmasking Illusions):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when encountering a supernatural illusion, glamour, mind-altering concealment, memory rewrite, or shapechanged entity (such as a Changeling's Mask, a Vampire's Obfuscate, or a Demon's Cover), the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. For the remainder of the scene, she automatically sees through all magical disguises and illusions within line of sight, perceiving the true nature of hidden entities and reality.</li> <li><b>Uncompromising Truth (Forcing Disclosure):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> When conducting an interrogation or Social Maneuvering action against a target who is actively lying, withholding vital secrets, or operating under supernatural compulsion, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and speak a direct, unvarnished truth. The target cannot use supernatural abilities to conceal their intentions or lie to her for the remainder of the scene; any attempt to speak a deliberate falsehood forces the target to spend 1 Willpower or remain silent.</li> <li><b>Exposing the Horror (Unveiling Concealment):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character deliberately forces a dangerous, hidden truth into the open\u2014such as unveiling a monster hiding in human society, exposing a conspiracy's Infrastructure, or revealing a terrible secret to save others\u2014she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. Doing so strips supernatural concealment, stealth, and Cover from all entities in the scene for turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T19:11:27-07:00","id":1564108,"title":"","content":"I think we do have to be careful with the virtues. The MG doesn't have to be defined by an other-directed Virtue, but a few rules must be enforced:<br /> <br /> 1. The Virtue must be expressed in relationship with others, fostering good relations. Even if the character at first struggle with this idea and may even sacrifice relationships for performing righteousness at the player's discretion, it only counts as fulfilling the Virtue if it genuinely help others and is done for their sake, not the sake of principle.<br /> <br /> 2. MG Virtues are about self-actualization. That is the hardest part, because the genre is subtly (and sometimes overtly) subversive. Purity in particular is not a good fit, or at least not the best way to say it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T22:51:01-07:00","id":1564113,"title":"","content":"Self-directed and other-directed were perhaps poor choices, as that presents them as a false dichotomy. Maybe instead they should be thought of as Internal and Relational, with the understanding that there are Virtues that qualify as both.<br /> <br /> Some examples of magical girls and their Virtues and Vices:<br /> <br /> First, the Sailor Senshi: <br /> <br /> <u><b>Sailor Moon (Usagi Tsukino)</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Purity <i>(her active incorruptibility and radiant power to cleanse spiritual rot)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Sloth<i> (her constant struggle with procrastination, laziness, and indulgence)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sailor Mercury (Ami Mizuno)</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Wisdom <i>(her analytical clarity, intellectual depth, and quiet discernment)</i><br /> <b>Vice: </b>Timidity <i>(her self-doubt, social hesitation, and fear of confrontation)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sailor Mars (Rei Hino)</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Conviction <i>(her spiritual discipline, unyielding focus, and fierce passion)</i><br /> <b>Vice: </b>Pride <i>(her quick temper, sharp tongue, and stubborn refusal to yield)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sailor Jupiter (Makoto Kino)</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Protection<i> (her physical fortitude, willingness to take hits, and nurturing warmth)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Impulsiveness <i>(her tendency to charge ahead recklessly and fall instantly for romantic ideals)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sailor Venus (Minako Aino)</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Duty<i> (her solitary burden as the original leader/decoy, carrying tragic resolve behind a smile)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Vanity<i> (her longing for stardom, frivolity, and vulnerability to superficial distractions)</i><br /> <br /> Next, the Holy Quintet:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Madoka Kaname</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Mercy <i>(her boundless empathy and willingness to absorb the world's despair so no one suffers alone)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Insecurity <i>(her crippling sense of self-worthlessness and anxiety over having nothing meaningful to offer)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Homura Akemi</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Fidelity <i>(her fierce, unwavering loyalty and devotion to her promise across endless timelines)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Obsession <i>(her hyper-fixation on a single outcome that drives her into cold, self-destructive isolation)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sayaka Miki</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice <i>(her earnest desire to defend the innocent and uphold an unyielding ideal of selfless heroism)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride <i>(her stubborn refusal to accept help or admit emotional vulnerability, accelerating her downfall)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Kyoko Sakura</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Protection <i>(her fierce guardianship over those she lets into her heart, ultimately choosing to share Sayaka's fate)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Cynicism <i>(her hardened, mercenary outlook that dismisses idealism and altruism as fatal mistakes)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Mami Tomoe</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Duty <i>(her veteran dedication to acting as a noble protector and guiding the next generation without complaint)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Loneliness <i>(her profound psychological isolation and terror of facing the dark alone behind her polished facade)</i><br /> <br /> And the primary magical girls of Maho Shoujo Lyrical Nanoha: <br /> <br /> <u><b>Nanoha Takamachi</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Conviction <i>(her unyielding belief in reaching out to understand others, using absolute force of will to break through emotional and hostile barriers to establish genuine connection)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Recklessness <i>(her severe disregard for her own physical limits and bodily health, pushing herself past near-fatal injury to save someone else)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Fate Testarossa</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Devotion <i>(her profound capacity for loyalty and unconditional love, standing unwaveringly by her family and loved ones regardless of the personal cost)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Self-Doubt <i>(her deep-seated insecurity surrounding her identity as a manufactured clone, leaving her vulnerable to guilt and fears of unworthiness)</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Hayate Yagami</b></u><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Sanctuary <i>(her extraordinary warmth and acceptance, providing an unconditional safe haven and sense of family to the outcast Wolkenritter)</i><br /> <b>Vice:</b> Fatalism <i>(her quiet resignation to her own suffering and crippling illness, preferring to bear terminal burdens in secret rather than worry those who depend on her)</i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T00:16:22-07:00","id":1564114,"title":"","content":"Here's a set of six supplemental Merits:<br /> <br /> Here is the complete set of all six finalized supplemental Virtue Merits formatted in BBCode for easy copy-pasting:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Supplemental Virtue Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>1. Vicarious Exposure (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Relational Virtue (such as <i>Compassion</i>, <i>Mercy</i>, <i>Protection</i>, <i>Selflessness</i>, <i>Devotion</i>, or <i>Honor</i>).<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <b>Universal Constraint (Communication Requirement):</b> None of the capabilities granted by this Merit can affect another character unless there is an active channel of communication between the character and the target (direct speech/vocal reassurance, eye contact, physical touch, or an active telepathic/empathic link). The target must be aware of the character's presence and gesture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Empathetic Aegis (Proactive Protection):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when an ally within line of sight is targeted by a fear effect, horror, or mind-altering power, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and call out to them, lock eyes, or reach for them. For the remainder of the scene, all allies with whom she maintains active communication add the character's <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to their resistance rolls and Breaking Point rolls against supernatural horror or fear.</li> <li><b>Vicarious Exposure (Absorbing Trauma):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]</i><br /> When a nearby ally or civilian is forced to make an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point roll, the character may declare a Tactical Exposure as a reflexive action, calling out their name, grabbing their hand, or locking eyes (&quot;Give it to me, look at me!&quot;). The original target suffers no loss and makes no roll; the character takes the Breaking Point on her own sheet instead, rolling <b>Resolve + Composure + Integrity Anchor Bonus</b>.</li> <li><b>De-escalating Touch (Soothing Rage):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting an enemy locked in active supernatural rage (such as Vampiric frenzy, Werewolf Death Rage, or Disquiet), the character steps into their line of sight, lowers her weapons, and directly speaks to or reaches for them. She <b>spends 1 Willpower</b> and rolls <b>Presence + Empathy + (half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to soothe them for turns equal to her Virtue rating.<ul><li><i>Unarmored Supercharge [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> If she voluntarily accepts a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) during this appeal, the target <b>cannot roll Supernatural Tolerance to resist</b>.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Soothing Burden (Condition Removal):</b> The character must make physical contact, lock eyes, or speak directly to the target (&quot;Breathe, I'm right here&quot;).<ul><li><i>Minor Relief [Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]:</i> <b>Spend 1 Willpower</b> as an instant action to clear a temporary mental Tilt (<i>Shaken</i>, <i>Terrified</i>, <i>Spooked</i>) from the target or allow them to immediately re-roll a failed resistance against an active mental Condition.</li> <li><i>Trauma Transfer [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> Accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) as an instant action to permanently cure and remove a severe mental Condition (<i>Broken</i>, <i>Despair</i>, <i>Thrall</i>) from the target, drawing the shock onto herself.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>2. Crucible of Conviction (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), An Internal Virtue (such as <i>Fortitude</i>, <i>Pride</i>, <i>Purity</i>, <i>Autonomy</i>, <i>Wisdom</i>, <i>Perseverance</i>, or <i>Independence</i>).<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Unshakeable Sovereignty (Resisting Control):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when targeted by a supernatural power that would force her to act against her core nature, rewrite her memories, exert direct mind control, or corrupt her soul or flesh, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so grants her <b>complete immunity</b> to supernatural mind-control, memory modification, or horror-induced Breaking Points for the remainder of the scene (or grants an automatic success on a Clash of Wills against direct soul or bodily alteration).</li> <li><b>Crucible of Endurance (Overcoming Shock):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when afflicted by severe temporary physical or mental Tilts (such as <i>Stunned</i>, <i>Knocked Down</i>, <i>Shaken</i>, or <i>Blind</i>) or heavy wound penalties, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so instantly clears all temporary physical and mental Tilts and allows her to completely ignore all wound penalties and fatigue for a number of turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>.</li> <li><b>Purifying Exposure (Moral Triumph):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character chooses to suffer severe personal loss, physical injury, or social ruin specifically to refuse a moral compromise or uphold her personal code, any Integrity roll forced by that ordeal gains her <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b>. This action is a Tactical Exposure and does not require an available active slot. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her emotional response converts the trial into righteous moral pride, granting her a <b>+2 bonus on all Resolve and Composure rolls</b> for the remainder of the scene and <b>instantly resetting</b> her once-per-session active Virtue slot if it was spent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>3. Eye of Revelation (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Virtue centered on Truth, Discernment, Wisdom, or Honesty.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Piercing the Veil (Unmasking Illusions):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when encountering a supernatural illusion, glamour, mind-altering concealment, memory rewrite, or shapechanged entity (such as a Changeling's Mask, a Vampire's Obfuscate, or a Demon's Cover), the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. For the remainder of the scene, she automatically sees through all magical disguises and illusions within line of sight, perceiving the true nature of hidden entities and reality.</li> <li><b>Uncompromising Truth (Forcing Disclosure):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> When conducting an interrogation or Social Maneuvering action against a target who is actively lying, withholding vital secrets, or operating under supernatural compulsion, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and speak a direct, unvarnished truth. The target cannot use supernatural abilities to conceal their intentions or lie to her for the remainder of the scene; any attempt to speak a deliberate falsehood forces the target to spend 1 Willpower or remain silent.</li> <li><b>Exposing the Horror (Unveiling Concealment):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character deliberately forces a dangerous, hidden truth into the open\u2014such as unveiling a monster hiding in human society, exposing a conspiracy's Infrastructure, or revealing a terrible secret to save others\u2014she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. Doing so strips supernatural concealment, stealth, and Cover from all entities in the scene for turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>4. Veil of Sanctuary (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Virtue centered on Discretion, Prudence, Fidelity, Sanctuary, or Protection.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Inviolable Confidence (Resisting Intrusive Perception):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when targeted by supernatural mind-reading, memory extraction, telepathic probing, or powers that force truthful disclosure (such as a Vampire's Auspex, a Mage's Mind magic, or <i>Eye of Revelation</i> itself), the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. For the remainder of the scene, her protected thoughts, memories, and secrets are completely immune to supernatural intrusion, appearing as an absolute void or impenetrable static to the intruder.</li> <li><b>Wards of Discretion (Shielding the Sanctuary):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to cast a shroud of discretion over a conversation, location, or group of allies. For the remainder of the scene, all supernatural scrying, magical tracking, eavesdropping, and technological surveillance directed at the warded area automatically fail, preserving the sanctuary of the space.</li> <li><b>Sacred Discretion (Preserving Confidences):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character willingly undergoes severe personal danger, physical harm, or social ruin specifically to protect a vital secret, shield an innocent's civilian life, or cover the escape of her allies, she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. Doing so completely erases all immediate physical, magical, and memory traces of the protected secret or missing allies from the scene. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>5. Scales of Retribution (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Virtue centered on Justice, Retribution, Reckoning, or Righteous Rage.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Mirror of Guilt (Reflecting Moral Trauma):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when the character or an ally in line of sight suffers a physical or psychological attack from a bad actor, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to force the attacker to feel the exact emotional horror and agony they just inflicted. The attacker must immediately roll <b>Composure + Supernatural Tolerance</b> vs. the character's <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b>. On a failure, the attacker suffers the <i>Shaken</i> or <i>Guilt-Ridden</i> Condition and loses 1 Willpower as their own cruelty rebounds onto their conscience.</li> <li><b>Inescapable Reckoning (Denying Emotional Escape):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting a wrongdoer, the character calls out their specific transgressions, stripping away their ability to disassociate, justify, or ignore what they have done. She <b>spends 1 Willpower</b>. For a number of turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>, the target cannot use supernatural abilities to flee the scene, erase memories, or hide their emotions. Furthermore, any attempts by the target to resist social or moral pressure suffer a penalty equal to half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up).</li> <li><b>Righteous Avenger (Forced Breaking Point):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character willingly puts herself in direct physical danger\u2014stepping into an enemy's line of fire without Defense or accepting a strike\u2014to force a monster, slasher, or tyrant to face what they are, she may declare a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> as an instant action. She points at the target and speaks the unvarnished toll of their crimes. The target is immediately <b>forced to undergo an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point</b> at a penalty equal to half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up). If the target fails this Breaking Point, they suffer an immediate moral collapse (gaining a severe mental Condition such as <i>Broken</i> or <i>Despair</i> and losing 1 Willpower). If the target fails the roll, the character's once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>6. Covenant of Redemption (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), A Virtue centered on Redemption, Reconciliation, Mercy, Restoration, or Forgiveness.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><ul><li><b>Avenue of Grace (Offering Salvation):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting an antagonist acting under supernatural compulsion, ancestral curse, obsession, or corruptive blood bond, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and extend an open hand or offer of peace. The target immediately receives an unprompted roll to break free of their compulsion, adding the character's <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to the roll.</li> <li><b>Restorative Oath (Binding Concord):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action following a battle or truce, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to seal a pledge of reform, non-aggression, or sanctuary with a former enemy who genuinely expresses remorse. <b>Until the binding Concord is violated</b>, the former enemy gains <b>half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up)</b> as a bonus on all resistance rolls against dark urges, supernatural frenzy, corruptive blood bonds, or horror-induced Breaking Points. If the former enemy voluntarily violates the Concord, they instantly lose this bonus, suffer the <i>Guilt-Ridden</i> Condition, and lose 1 Willpower.</li> <li><b>Crucible of Reconciliation (Vulnerable Appeal):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character steps directly into harm's way without weapons or magical shields raised\u2014offering an enemy a genuine path to surrender and grace while taking an undefended hit or facing mortal danger\u2014she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. The target must immediately roll <b>Composure + Supernatural Tolerance</b> vs. the character's <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b>; if the target fails, they are struck with profound moral remorse, halting all hostile actions for turns equal to her Virtue rating. If the character succeeds on her forced Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.</li> </ul><hr />Conceptually, these Merits come in pairs: Relational/Identity, Discovery/Sanctuary, and Retribution/Redemption. None of them are strictly opposites, so with an appropriate Virtue you could conceivably have any combinations of them. However, any given MG is unlikely to have more than two or three; and that's pushing it. <br /> <br /> Note that these Merits could theoretical be adapted to the various Monster Mash MGs, by replacing the Virtue rating in the mechanics with whatever the MG's power stat is, and looking at the MG's Anchors (Mask/Dirge; Blood/Bone; Elpis/Torment; Needle/Thread; Root/Bloom; Life/Legend; Conviction/Loyalty) to see which ones they qualify for. (For Deviants, I'd use Loyalty as the \u201cPower Stat\u201d for Devoted and Guardians, and Conviction for Renegades and Nemeses.) <br /> <br /> In fact, an interesting observation: most of those alternate anchors form an Internal/Relational duality instead of the character strength/weakness duality that Virtue and Vice represent: Mask, Blood, Needle, Bloom, Legend, and Loyalty are all Relational \u201cVirtues\u201d, while Dirge, Bone, Thread, Root, Life, and Conviction are Identity \u201cVirtues\u201d. <br /> <br /> So these six Merits should be good for <i>all</i> Magical Girls, not just Mortal MGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T01:00:39-07:00","id":1564115,"title":"","content":"After further reflection, I'm not worried about Mascots being too similar to Totems anymore. The former facilitate teamwork and are driven by friendships; the latter provide stat boosts as enforce a predatory pack mentality. Their similarities end at being Ephemeral Entities associated with teams. Though I'm thinking of splitting Mascot into Mascot and Heart-Weave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T09:13:32-07:00","id":1564122,"title":"","content":"I think the Virtue prerequisite could maybe be presented as an action or event, rather than a qualifier? I don't know, demanding the ST to judge a taxonomy of Virtues seems harder to implement consistently than it should, and open to confusion.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> <br /> Vicarious Exposure<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by choosing to talk when fighting would be safer and acceptable.<br /> -&gt; You witnessed a serious/dangerous mental breakdown and want to help that person.<br /> <br /> Crucible of Conviction<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by resisting severe coercion of any nature.<br /> -&gt; You suffered physical, social or supernatural assault you could not defend against, but stood your ground.<br /> <br /> Eye of Revelation<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by insisting on finding or revealing the truth against danger.<br /> -&gt; You saw comforting misinformation cause actual damage, as witness or participant.<br /> <br /> Veil of Sanctuary<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by preserving the privacy of someone, protecting them with this.<br /> -&gt; You've seen someone's information revealed and used to cause undue harm.<br /> <br /> Scales of Retribution<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by delivering the price of evil to those untouched by law.<br /> -&gt; You saw how much a bully fears when their bluff is called on and you'll deliver it to them all.<br /> <br /> Covenant of Redemption<br /> -&gt; You can fulfill your Virtue by choosing to end hostilities when destruction is at hand.<br /> -&gt; You saw the cycle of misery be broken and a monster revealed into someone who can heal.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, we can add a requirement that the first use of the Merit must be fulfilling the Virtue.<br /> <br /> As they represent different tactics to solve a problem, each with personal costs, I'm not so sure we even need to put something there: the Merits enforce the right posture by themselves, and the player will be spending points not in a combo, but strategies they want to use in lieu of violence. <hr /><br /> I think your Merits are excellent and it is a solid starting point for the other MGs. With this we have the Transformation, the power stat, and a good collection of options to give agency to a Detective MG.<br /> <br /> Does the Compact of Transformation requires any further tweak for now? I think we mostly finished it, at least a prototype. Now we have the Mascot to hammer down. I think it should be a very basic critter without much capability to begin with. A single defining Perk, with the standard being to look ordinary, and the main Merit governing its ability to do its main job of Maintenance, specialized advice and measure the MG's integration into the role.<br /> <br /> Other Merits can give other capabilities to the Mascot, probably similar to Social Merits as it becomes capable at support and other tasks, and one or two to give it more direct presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T13:40:49-07:00","id":1564127,"title":"","content":"Here is what I currently have for Compact of Transformation, to make sure we're on the same page: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Merit: Compact of Transformation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None (Open to mortals and all supernatural splats alike).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> The character possesses a unique mystical focus\u2014traditionally a makeup compact, star-pendant, brooch, or pocket mirror\u2014given to her by a Mascot. This item acts as the catalyst through which she channels her inner light, enabling her to instantly rewrite her civilian form into a high-utility, stylized magical persona.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Core Mechanics</b></span><br /> <b>The Identity Shield:</b> Activating the compact provides an <b>absolute identity shield</b>. Even if the character\u2019s face remains exposed, a supernatural perception filter prevents onlookers from connecting the magical persona to her civilian identity. Forcing a recognition check requires a contested Wits + Composure vs. Presence + Subterfuge (or Supernatural Tolerance) roll at a -3 penalty, which is waived only with concrete proof. Digital recordings, cameras, and facial recognition software automatically register the persona as a separate, unidentifiable individual.<br /> <br /> <b>Manifested Loadout:</b> Upon transforming, civilian gear vanishes, replaced by a predetermined magical loadout bound to the compact. <b>Form does not follow function.</b> Players select standard item statistics from equipment lists but define their visual appearance entirely through flavor (e.g., a Heavy Sniper Rifle reskinned as a star-tipped wand firing starlight beams). If gear leaves the character's person, it dissolves into light and resets to the compact's transformation inventory.<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment Point Budget:</b> The dots invested in this Merit dictate how much total magical gear can manifest alongside the transformation. A character receives an <b>Equipment Point Budget equal to 3 + dots in Compact of Transformation</b>. She allocates these points into her transformed loadout, creating a fixed inventory of manifested gear, which can be freely reallocated during narrative downtime between stories:<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 (1 Dot):</b> 4 Equipment Points<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 (2 Dots):</b> 5 Equipment Points<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 (3 Dots):</b> 6 Equipment Points<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (4 Dots):</b> 7 Equipment Points<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (5 Dots):</b> 8 Equipment Points<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Follow-Up Transformation Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Shared Grace (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Compact of Transformation (\u2022)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> Manifested gear no longer dissolves when separated from the character's person. It remains physical, retaining all statistics and aesthetics, as long as the user's Compact of Transformation remains active. The user can manifest an item, loan it to a teammate or NPC, and then manifest completely separate gear for themselves from their remaining Equipment Point Budget. Furthermore, the user can reflexively dissolve loaned gear into light at any distance, immediately reclaiming those budget points.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Cosmic Essence (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Compact of Transformation (\u2022)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> Transformed gear never runs out of mundane ammunition, battery life, charges, or internal fuel blocks. This overrides the Reload or Battery Capacity traits of underlying templates, meaning the character never spends actions t reload in combat. This benefit waives only mundane logistical costs; abilities requiring supernatural resources, such as Pure Spark abilities costing Spark, must still be paid normally. <hr />And here's an idea designed to allow a mortal magical girl to get more out of the Compact of Transformation than her supernatural counterparts can: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Mortal Transformed Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>1. Heart-Shield Aegis (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Vicarious Exposure (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s emotional empathy and willingness to absorb trauma manifest as kinetic forcefields and protective shock-absorbers. The deep empathy that soothes hearts in civilian life becomes a physical barrier that deflects bullets and cushions blows meant for her allies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Transformed Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Kinetic Empathy (Physical Interposition):</b> Whenever an ally within 5 yards is targeted by a physical attack, the character may spend 1 Willpower as a reflexive action to instantly leap or flash between the attacker and her ally. She becomes the target of the attack instead, and her Defense applies against the incoming blow even if she has already acted this turn.<br /> <b>Shock-Absorber Field:</b> When taking physical damage on behalf of an ally via Kinetic Empathy or when absorbing a Breaking Point via <i>Vicarious Exposure</i>, the character gains a physical Armor rating equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b> against that specific attack or ordeal.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Aegis Dress / Ribbon Barrier</b> (Manifested Armor / Shield Equipment Template: Cost 2 Points, grants Armor 2/1 or +2 Defense).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When <i>Empathetic Aegis</i> or <i>Vicarious Exposure</i> is active, the Aegis Dress extends its Armor rating to all allies within 3 yards and converts incoming Lethal physical damage aimed at protected allies into Bashing damage absorbed by the dress's kinetic barrier.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>2. Unyielding Bastion (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Crucible of Conviction (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s refusal to yield moral ground translates into absolute physical immovability and devastating kinetic impact. Her refusal to compromise physically anchors her to the earth, allowing her to shrug off crushing blows and strike back with the weight of her conviction.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Transformed Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Immovable Resolve (Physical Anchoring):</b> While transformed, the character cannot be knocked Prone, forcefully moved, grapple-thrown, or displaced by physical attacks, explosions, or supernatural telekinesis unless the attacker wins a contested Strength + Athletics roll against her <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b>.<br /> <b>Juggernaut Momentum:</b> When performing a Charge, Knockdown, or Smash action against an enemy, the character adds her <b>Virtue rating</b> as bonus dice to the attack roll and ignores up to her Virtue rating in environmental obstacles or door Durability.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Greatshield of Resolve / Starlight Warhammer</b> (Manifested Heavy Weapon / Tower Shield Equipment Template: Cost 3 Points, Weapon Damage 3, Size 3, Grants +2 Cover/Defense).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When <i>Unshakeable Sovereignty</i> or <i>Crucible of Endurance</i> is triggered, the Greatshield's Cover bonus applies against all physical attacks (including firearms and area-of-effect explosions), and melee strikes deal bonus kinetic damage equal to the character's Virtue rating.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>3. Lantern of the Unmasked (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Eye of Revelation (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s pursuit of truth manifests as searing, physical starlight and holy illumination. The insight that pierces lies in civilian life becomes a blinding beacon that strips away physical shadows, burns through supernatural camouflage, and severs magical illusions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Transformed Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Dispelling Illumination:</b> As a reflexive action while transformed, the character can cause her body or weapon to emit a blinding burst of starlight in a radius of <b>5 yards x Virtue rating</b>. This light immediately dispels mundane darkness, illuminates invisible or stealthed entities, and forces all enemies within the aura to roll Composure + Supernatural Tolerance or suffer the <i>Blinded</i> Tilt for 1 turn.<br /> <b>True-Sight Precision:</b> Attacks made against disguised, shapechanged, or illusion-covered entities automatically bypass all Defense or Armor granted by supernatural disguise, illusion, or Cover.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Starlight Wand / Beam Pistol</b> (Manifested Ranged Weapon Equipment Template: Cost 2 Points, Weapon Damage 2, Range 20/40/80).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When attacking a target under the effects of <i>Piercing the Veil</i> or <i>Exposing the Horror</i>, the Wand ignores all Concealment penalties, bypasses magical Armor, and inflicts bonus damage equal to the target's missing Integrity, Clarity, or Cover rating.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>4. Mantle of the Silent Haven (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Veil of Sanctuary (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s duty to guard secrets and shield sanctuaries becomes a physical barrier of quiet night and sound-dampening forcefields. The discretion that keeps confidences in civilian life creates a physical dome of protection that repels projectiles and hides allies from physical detection.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Transformed Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Aegis Dome (Repelling Forcefield):</b> As an instant action, the character can anchor a physical forcefield dome centered on herself with a radius equal to her <b>Virtue rating in yards</b>. Enemies attempting to physically cross the boundary or fire projectiles into the dome must succeed on a contested Strength + Athletics roll vs. the user's <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b> or have their movement halted and projectiles bounced harmlessly away.<br /> <b>Silent Shroud:</b> The character and all allies within her Aegis Dome move in complete physical silence, gaining a bonus on Stealth rolls equal to her Virtue rating and becoming immune to thermal, sonic, or electronic tracking devices.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Mantle of Dusk / Sanctuary Cloak</b> (Manifested Utility Equipment Template: Cost 2 Points, Grants +2 Stealth and Armor 1/1).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When <i>Wards of Discretion</i> or <i>Sacred Discretion</i> is activated, the Mantle expands into a physical barrier that grants full Concealment and Cover (+3 dice to Defense) to all allies inside the sanctuary against ranged physical attacks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>5. Blade of Nemesis (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Scales of Retribution (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s drive for moral justice manifests as retributive physical force. The moral weight that forces wrongdoers to face guilt in civilian life turns her weapon into an instrument of physical reckoning, dealing damage proportional to the harm the target has inflicted on others.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Weight of Transgression:</b> When striking an antagonist who has physically injured or traumatized an ally or civilian during the current scene, the weapon gains an <b>Armor-Piercing rating equal to the character's Virtue rating</b> and deals +1 bonus Lethal damage for every 2 health levels of damage the target inflicted on others in the scene (max bonus +3).<br /> <b>Gravitational Reckoning:</b> On a successful melee hit, the character may spend 1 Willpower to knock the target Prone and pin them under physical gravity, applying a penalty to their physical actions equal to her Virtue rating for 1 turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Scale-Bladed Saber / Judgment Scythe</b> (Manifested Melee Weapon Equipment Template: Cost 3 Points, Weapon Damage 3, Size 2, Initiative -1).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When attacking a target currently undergoing a forced Breaking Point or moral collapse via <i>Righteous Avenger</i> or <i>Mirror of Guilt</i>, the Saber's damage type converts directly to Aggravated damage as the blade burns with moral judgment.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>6. Ribbons of Binding Grace (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal status (no major supernatural splat template), Compact of Transformation (\u2022), Covenant of Redemption (\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supernatural / Physical Merit.<br /> <b>Description:</b> While transformed, the character\u2019s willingness to extend grace and peace manifests as glowing ribbons or soft chains of binding energy. The patience that builds truces in civilian life becomes a non-lethal grappling system that physically disarms, binds, and pacifies hostile targets without shedding blood.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Pacifying Entanglement:</b> The character can make ranged Grapple attempts up to her <b>Virtue rating x 3 yards</b> away using Dex + Athletics without needing to physically touch the target. On a successful grapple, the target suffers no physical damage but is held immobilized in glowing ribbons.<br /> <b>Disarming Grace:</b> When grappling an opponent with her ribbons, she can instantly Disarm the target as a reflexive action without taking a penalty. Weapons or focus items disarmed in this manner are safely pulled to her hand or wrapped harmlessly on the ground. While entangled, the target suffers a penalty on all offensive rolls equal to her Virtue rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Transformed Gear:</b> <b>Ribbons of Accord / Grace Whip</b> (Manifested Exotic Weapon Equipment Template: Cost 2 Points, Grapple, Reach, Disarm qualities).<br /> <b>Gear Enhancement Note:</b> When used alongside <i>Avenue of Grace</i> or <i>Crucible of Reconciliation</i>, the Ribbons grant a bonus equal to the user's Virtue rating on all contested rolls to hold a target restrained, while suppressing the target's ability to activate supernatural combat frenzy or violent physical traits while bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T13:55:00-07:00","id":1564128,"title":"","content":"And here's the rest of what I've got right now: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Supernatural Trait: Spark of Virtue</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Power Stat / Personality Anchor (Rated \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022).<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortals only (Replaces traditional splat Power Stats like Blood Potency, Gnosis, or Primal Urge for mortal Magical Girls; crossover splats use their native Power Stat).<br /> <b>Description:</b> Spark of Virtue represents the intensity of a Magical Girl's moral conviction, the purity of her soul-light, and her capacity to channel raw Astral resonance through her physical form. Rather than deriving power from blood, pyros, or ancestral rage, her supernatural potency scales directly with her commitment to her core Virtue.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Mechanical Effects</b></span><br /> <b>Supernatural Tolerance:</b> The character uses her Spark of Virtue rating as her base Supernatural Tolerance against hostile supernatural powers, curses, and mind-altering effects.<br /> <b>Integrity Anchor Bonus:</b> The character adds <b>half her Spark of Virtue rating (rounded up)</b> as a static bonus to all Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point rolls, as well as Defense bonuses granted by defensive Virtue capabilities.<br /> <b>Essence &amp; Willpower Capacity:</b> Spark of Virtue governs maximum Essence capacity and turn-by-turn spending limits when interacting with Mascots and Heart-Weave conduits (Max Essence Pool = 10 + [Spark of Virtue x 2]).<br /> <b>Prerequisite for Advanced Merits:</b> Acts as the foundational prerequisite (at 5 dots, or equivalent Power Stat 1+ for crossover characters) for unlocking Supplemental Virtue Merits, Compact of Transformation, and Heart-Weave networks.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>Supplemental Virtue Merits</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>1. Vicarious Exposure (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character chooses to de-escalate, reach out to, or protect someone in emotional or physical danger when a safer, less vulnerable, or more aggressive response would be acceptable.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Compassion, Mercy, Protection, Selflessness, Devotion, Honor.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <b>Universal Constraint (Communication Requirement):</b> None of the capabilities granted by this Merit can affect another character unless there is an active channel of communication between the character and the target (direct speech/vocal reassurance, eye contact, physical touch, or an active telepathic/empathic link). The target must be aware of the character's presence and gesture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Empathetic Aegis (Proactive Protection):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when an ally within line of sight is targeted by a fear effect, horror, or mind-altering power, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and call out to them, lock eyes, or reach for them. For the remainder of the scene, all allies with whom she maintains active communication add the character's <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to their resistance rolls and Breaking Point rolls against supernatural horror or fear.<br /> <b>Vicarious Exposure (Absorbing Trauma):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]</i><br /> When a nearby ally or civilian is forced to make an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point roll, the character may declare a Tactical Exposure as a reflexive action, calling out their name, grabbing their hand, or locking eyes (&quot;Give it to me, look at me!&quot;). The original target suffers no loss and makes no roll; the character takes the Breaking Point on her own sheet instead, rolling <b>Resolve + Composure + Integrity Anchor Bonus</b>.<br /> <b>De-escalating Touch (Soothing Rage):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting an enemy locked in active supernatural rage (such as Vampiric frenzy, Werewolf Death Rage, or Disquiet), the character steps into their line of sight, lowers her weapons, and directly speaks to or reaches for them. She <b>spends 1 Willpower</b> and rolls <b>Presence + Empathy + (half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to soothe them for turns equal to her Virtue rating.<ul><li><i>Unarmored Supercharge [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> If she voluntarily accepts a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) during this appeal, the target <b>cannot roll Supernatural Tolerance to resist</b>.</li> </ul><b>Soothing Burden (Condition Removal):</b> The character must make physical contact, lock eyes, or speak directly to the target (&quot;Breathe, I'm right here&quot;).<br /> <i>Minor Relief [Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]:</i> <b>Spend 1 Willpower</b> as an instant action to clear a temporary mental Tilt (<i>Shaken</i>, <i>Terrified</i>, <i>Spooked</i>) from the target or allow them to immediately re-roll a failed resistance against an active mental Condition.<br /> <br /> <i>Trauma Transfer [Tactical Exposure \u2014 Does Not Consume Active Slot]:</i> Accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Breaking Point) as an instant action to permanently cure and remove a severe mental Condition (<i>Broken</i>, <i>Despair</i>, <i>Thrall</i>) from the target, drawing the shock onto herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>2. Crucible of Conviction (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character refuses a moral compromise, supernatural temptation, or easy surrender at significant personal, physical, or social cost to herself.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Fortitude, Pride, Purity, Autonomy, Perseverance, Independence.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Unshakeable Sovereignty (Resisting Control):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when targeted by a supernatural power that would force her to act against her core nature, rewrite her memories, exert direct mind control, or corrupt her soul or flesh, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so grants her <b>complete immunity</b> to supernatural mind-control, memory modification, or horror-induced Breaking Points for the remainder of the scene (or grants an automatic success on a Clash of Wills against direct soul or bodily alteration).<br /> <br /> <b>Crucible of Endurance (Overcoming Shock):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when afflicted by severe temporary physical or mental Tilts (such as <i>Stunned</i>, <i>Knocked Down</i>, <i>Shaken</i>, or <i>Blind</i>) or heavy wound penalties, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. Doing so instantly clears all temporary physical and mental Tilts and allows her to completely ignore all wound penalties and fatigue for a number of turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Purifying Exposure (Moral Triumph):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character chooses to suffer severe personal loss, physical injury, or social ruin specifically to refuse a moral compromise or uphold her personal code, any Integrity roll forced by that ordeal gains her <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b>. This action is a Tactical Exposure and does not require an available active slot. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her emotional response converts the trial into righteous moral pride, granting her a <b>+2 bonus on all Resolve and Composure rolls</b> for the remainder of the scene and <b>instantly resetting</b> her once-per-session active Virtue slot if it was spent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>3. Eye of Revelation (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character uncovers, speaks, or forces a dangerous or painful truth into the open when staying silent, looking away, or maintaining a lie would be far safer or more convenient.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Truth, Discernment, Wisdom, Honesty, Curiosity.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Piercing the Veil (Unmasking Illusions):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when encountering a supernatural illusion, glamour, mind-altering concealment, memory rewrite, or shapechanged entity (such as a Changeling's Mask, a Vampire's Obfuscate, or a Demon's Cover), the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. For the remainder of the scene, she automatically sees through all magical disguises and illusions within line of sight, perceiving the true nature of hidden entities and reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Uncompromising Truth (Forcing Disclosure):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> When conducting an interrogation or Social Maneuvering action against a target who is actively lying, withholding vital secrets, or operating under supernatural compulsion, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and speak a direct, unvarnished truth. The target cannot use supernatural abilities to conceal their intentions or lie to her for the remainder of the scene; any attempt to speak a deliberate falsehood forces the target to spend 1 Willpower or remain silent.<br /> <br /> <b>Exposing the Horror (Unveiling Concealment):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character deliberately forces a dangerous, hidden truth into the open\u2014such as unveiling a monster hiding in human society, exposing a conspiracy's Infrastructure, or revealing a terrible secret to save others\u2014she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. Doing so strips supernatural concealment, stealth, and Cover from all entities in the scene for turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>4. Veil of Sanctuary (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character protects a vital secret, shields an innocent's sanctuary, or covers an ally's escape at personal risk, refusing to betray a confidence even under severe pressure or threat.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Discretion, Prudence, Fidelity, Sanctuary, Protection.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Inviolable Confidence (Resisting Intrusive Perception):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when targeted by supernatural mind-reading, memory extraction, telepathic probing, or powers that force truthful disclosure (such as a Vampire's Auspex, a Mage's Mind magic, or Eye of Revelation itself), the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b>. For the remainder of the scene, her protected thoughts, memories, and secrets are completely immune to supernatural intrusion, appearing as an absolute void or impenetrable static to the intruder.<br /> <br /> <b>Wards of Discretion (Shielding the Sanctuary):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to cast a shroud of discretion over a conversation, location, or group of allies. For the remainder of the scene, all supernatural scrying, magical tracking, eavesdropping, and technological surveillance directed at the warded area automatically fail, preserving the sanctuary of the space.<br /> <br /> <b>Sacred Discretion (Preserving Confidences):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character willingly undergoes severe personal danger, physical harm, or social ruin specifically to protect a vital secret, shield an innocent's civilian life, or cover the escape of her allies, she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. Doing so completely erases all immediate physical, magical, and memory traces of the protected secret or missing allies from the scene. If she succeeds on the Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>5. Scales of Retribution (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character directly confronts a wrongdoer, tyrant, or monster to hold them accountable for their crimes, placing herself in physical or social danger to enforce a moral reckoning.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Justice, Retribution, Reckoning, Righteous Rage.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Mirror of Guilt (Reflecting Moral Trauma):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As a reflexive action when the character or an ally in line of sight suffers a physical or psychological attack from a bad actor, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to force the attacker to feel the exact emotional horror and agony they just inflicted. The attacker must immediately roll <b>Composure + Supernatural Tolerance</b> vs. the character's <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b>. On a failure, the attacker suffers the <i>Shaken</i> or <i>Guilt-Ridden</i> Condition and loses 1 Willpower as their own cruelty rebounds onto their conscience.<br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable Reckoning (Denying Emotional Escape):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting a wrongdoer, the character calls out their specific transgressions, stripping away their ability to disassociate, justify, or ignore what they have done. She <b>spends 1 Willpower</b>. For a number of turns equal to her <b>Virtue rating</b>, the target cannot use supernatural abilities to flee the scene, erase memories, or hide their emotions. Furthermore, any attempts by the target to resist social or moral pressure suffer a penalty equal to half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up).<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Avenger (Forced Breaking Point):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character willingly puts herself in direct physical danger\u2014stepping into an enemy's line of fire without Defense or accepting a strike\u2014to force a monster, slasher, or tyrant to face what they are, she may declare a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> as an instant action. She points at the target and speaks the unvarnished toll of their crimes. The target is immediately <b>forced to undergo an Integrity, Clarity, or moral Breaking Point</b> at a penalty equal to half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up). If the target fails this Breaking Point, they suffer an immediate moral collapse (gaining a severe mental Condition such as <i>Broken</i> or <i>Despair</i> and losing 1 Willpower). If the target fails the roll, the character's once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>6. Covenant of Redemption (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+.<br /> <b>Virtue Requirement:</b> The Virtue must be one that is fulfilled when the character extends a genuine path of grace, truce, or reform to a former enemy when destroying, abandoning, or executing them would be easier and entirely justified.<br /> <b>Sample Virtues:</b> Redemption, Reconciliation, Mercy, Restoration, Forgiveness.<br /> <b>Active Use Limit:</b> Activating a standard capability below consumes the character's <b>once-per-session active Virtue slot</b>. Capabilities designated as a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> involve immediate self-sacrifice and <b>do not consume</b> the once-per-session active slot (and may be used even if the slot is already spent).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>Avenue of Grace (Offering Salvation):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action when confronting an antagonist acting under supernatural compulsion, ancestral curse, obsession, or corruptive blood bond, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> and extend an open hand or offer of peace. The target immediately receives an unprompted roll to break free of their compulsion, adding the character's <b>Integrity Anchor bonus (+half Virtue rating, rounded up)</b> to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Restorative Oath (Binding Concord):</b> <i>[Consumes Once-Per-Session Active Slot]</i><br /> As an instant action following a battle or truce, the character may <b>spend 1 Willpower</b> to seal a pledge of reform, non-aggression, or sanctuary with a former enemy who genuinely expresses remorse. <b>Until the binding Concord is violated</b>, the former enemy gains <b>half the character's Virtue rating (rounded up)</b> as a bonus on all resistance rolls against dark urges, supernatural frenzy, corruptive blood bonds, or horror-induced Breaking Points. If the former enemy voluntarily violates the Concord, they instantly lose this bonus, suffer the <i>Guilt-Ridden</i> Condition, and lose 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Crucible of Reconciliation (Vulnerable Appeal):</b> <i>[Tactical Exposure \u2014 Conditional Reset]</i><br /> When the character steps directly into harm's way without weapons or magical shields raised\u2014offering an enemy a genuine path to surrender and grace while taking an undefended hit or facing mortal danger\u2014she may accept a <b>Tactical Exposure</b> (taking an immediate Integrity Breaking Point) as an instant action. The target must immediately roll <b>Composure + Supernatural Tolerance</b> vs. the character's <b>Resolve + Virtue rating</b>; if the target fails, they are struck with profound moral remorse, halting all hostile actions for turns equal to her Virtue rating. If the character succeeds on her forced Breaking Point roll, her once-per-session active Virtue slot <b>instantly resets</b> if it was spent.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Merit: Mascot</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+, Shared Team Aspiration.<br /> <b>Type:</b> Social / Supernatural (May be group-funded by circle members).<br /> <b>Description:</b> A Mascot is a manifested ephemeral entity born from human hope, emotional resonance, or Astral concepts. Rather than acting as a simple brawler, the Mascot serves as a guide, an emotional anchor, and the living antenna required to facilitate magical girl networks.<br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Rank Formula:</b> The Mascot's Ephemeral Entity Rank is equal to <b>half its Merit rating, rounded up</b> (Rank 1 at \u2022\u2013\u2022\u2022, Rank 2 at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2013\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, and Rank 3 at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Dot Progression &amp; Ephemeral Traits</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Rank 1 Guide (Merit \u2022):</b> Rank 1 Ephemeral Entity (Corpus 5, Max Essence 10). Possesses 1 Numen and grants access to 1 Mentor Skill pool (3 dice) for downtime advice.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Rank 1 Anchor (Merit \u2022\u2022):</b> Rank 1 Ephemeral Entity (Corpus 6, Max Essence 12). Grants access to 2 Mentor Skill pools (4 dice each). Unlocks the capacity to anchor 1-dot Heart-Weave networks.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rank 2 Sentinel (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Rank 2 Ephemeral Entity (Corpus 7, Max Essence 15). Possesses 2 Numina and grants access to 3 Mentor Skill pools (5 dice each). The Mascot can physically manifest in physical space continuously without spending Essence while near its circle.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rank 2 Luminary (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Rank 2 Ephemeral Entity (Corpus 8, Max Essence 18). Grants access to 3 Mentor Skill pools (6 dice each). The Mascot can spend Essence to assist remote Teamwork rolls or boost circle initiative during high-stakes scenes.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rank 3 Paragon (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Rank 3 Ephemeral Entity (Corpus 9, Max Essence 20). Possesses 3 Numina and grants access to 3 Mentor Skill pools (7 dice each). Gains an Ephemeral Influence (such as Hope, Protection, or Wisdom) at 3 dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Core Mechanics</b></span><br /> <b>Dual Function (Entity &amp; Mentor):</b> In active scenes, the Mascot operates as an Ephemeral Entity using its Rank, Corpus, and Numina. During narrative downtime, it doubles directly as a Mentor Merit, allowing linked characters to ask for assistance or automatic successes in its designated Mentor Skills.<br /> <b>Essence Harvesting:</b> Whenever a linked character fulfills a Virtue, Vice, Anchor, or Team Aspiration, the Mascot automatically harvests 1 point of Essence to refill its pool.<br /> <b>Bans &amp; Personality:</b> Every Mascot possesses an intrinsic Ban and Bane tied to its nature (e.g., must never allow a promise to be broken, or cannot cross cold iron). Respecting the Mascot's Ban reinforces its spiritual strength.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Group Merit: The Heart-Weave</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spark of Virtue (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Power Stat 1+, Mascot (\u2022) (at least one manifested Mascot present to facilitate the hub), Shared Team Aspiration.<br /> <b>Type:</b> Group Merit (Dots are pooled among all participating members of the circle).<br /> <b>Description:</b> While a Mascot provides individual guidance and emotional grounding, The Heart-Weave represents the active metaphysical web linking the souls of a Magical Girl circle. By running their emotional resonance through their Mascot\u2019s Astral core, the circle establishes an unshakeable sympathetic network capable of bridging physical distance, defying supernatural terror, and uniting disparate monster lineages.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Capabilities</b></span><br /> <b>\u2022 Woven Souls (Sympathetic Network &amp; Aura Neutralization):</b><ul><li><i>Metaphysical Link:</i> Establishes a permanent sympathetic link between all members via the Mascot hub, allowing real-time emotional and health tracking across any distance.</li> <li><i>Aura Neutralization:</i> Neutralizes passive horror and instinctual tension auras (Lunacy, Disquiet, Beast tension) between linked allies.</li> <li><i>Esoteric Conduit:</i> Spend an instant action to transfer 1 Willpower to a remote ally across the network (requires 1 Mascot Essence).</li> </ul><b>\u2022\u2022 Harmonized Fate (Remote Assistance &amp; Merit Relay):</b><ul><li><i>Remote Virtue Activation:</i> Relational Virtue Merits can be activated on remote allies across the city without direct line-of-sight.</li> <li><i>Global Teamwork:</i> Linked allies can join Teamwork rolls remotely across any distance.</li> <li><i>Mascot Assistance:</i> The Mascot can act as an independent secondary actor in remote Teamwork rolls using its Rank or Mentor skills.</li> </ul><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Multi-Mascot Tapestry (Circle Mergers &amp; Redundancy):</b><ul><li><i>Multi-Mascot Mergers:</i> Integrates multiple Mascots into a single unified network hub.</li> <li><i>Redundancy:</i> The network stays 100% operational as long as at least one co-facilitating Mascot remains active.</li> <li><i>Dual Guidance &amp; Harvest:</i> Access all co-facilitating Mascots' Mentor skill pools and choose which guide receives harvested Essence.</li> <li><i>Dual Secondary Actors:</i> In scenes requiring team-wide effort, two co-facilitating Mascots can enter the same Teamwork action as distinct secondary actors.</li> </ul><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Vector: Resonance (Hard-Light Projection &amp; Counter-Horror):</b><ul><li><i>Hard-Light Aegis:</i> Spend 1 Willpower reflexively to project a protective barrier around a remote ally, adding your Integrity Anchor bonus to their Defense or resistance.</li> <li><i>Remote Clash of Wills:</i> Initiate a Clash of Wills remotely through the hub to snap an ally out of mind control or memory alteration.</li> </ul><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Unbroken Pattern (Synchronized Exposure &amp; Collective Reset):</b><ul><li><i>Synchronized Exposure:</i> When multiple members declare a Tactical Exposure in the same turn, all resulting rolls gain an automatic Success Upgrade.</li> <li><i>Collective Reset:</i> Passing a forced Breaking Point during a Synchronized Exposure instantly resets all spent active Virtue slots across the entire circle.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T13:56:26-07:00","id":1564129,"title":"","content":"(My latest replay is being reviewed by the moderators. I think I posted it too soon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T20:36:24-07:00","id":1564135,"title":"","content":"Looking at the various gamelines, I picture a Hunter Compact that specializes in creating Magical Girls: one part women's shelter that that has developed a talent for coaxing the Spark of Virtue from the girls in the shelter as it teaches them healthy ways to cope with their trauma; and one part animal shelter that ends up as a support network for Mascots. And by pairing the two, they bring about a not inconsiderable number of Magical Girls. The main reason they didn't create more is that the Spark of Virtue is something a girl chooses to embrace; if can't be forced on them. <br /> <br /> But then there's also a Deviant Conspiracy; a splinter group from the above Compact that found itself in a desperate situation where it ended up trying to force the issue of accepting the Spark of Virtue; and the result ended up cracking the soul of the girl in question. They now serve as a dark counterpoint to the Hunter Compact, showing how even the best of intentions can go horribly wrong. <br /> <br /> But then there are the Guardians that they produce: Magical Girls who flee the Conspiracy, but end up embracing Loyalty to their Touchstones over Conviction to oppose the Conspiracy. I'm of the opinion that Deviant Magical Girls should have an abnormally high frequency of Guardians and Nemeses among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T17:31:26-07:00","id":1564146,"title":"","content":"Waiting for your second post to be approved, send as personal message if you can to hasten things up. I'll later give a few suggestions of my own.<br /> <br /> I like both the Hunter Compact and Conspiracy producing Deviants, but I'd add another layer:<br /> <br /> Sometimes Mascots come seeking suitable girls wiling to accept this duty. But sometimes they come with more specific needs: they have a particular girl in mind, Human or not, and the Compact of Transformation must reach her. It's another type of mission, one that puts Hunters, and not necessarily Magical Girls, in the streets to work creatively.<br /> <br /> The Conspiracy relationship with Mascots is also a matter to explore. Mascots have a noble cause and specialized knowledge, but they're not universally smart or ethical. The Deviants will need Compacts, after all, and those need a technician that's simultaneously their mentor, loyal retainer, and possible agentand spy to the Conspiracy. How crazy can this relationship be?<br /> <br /> On the plus side, and keeping with the genre, this one Conspiracy may be an exception to the norm even if still (deservedly) hated by their creations: they're genuinely not enemies to the Magical Girls that embrace the cause. They're not their owners and accept with grace to be deemed villains. They will defend their assets and work and spy on the girls, but interventions are few and genuinely well meaning, possibly offering resources to help with stability and the occasional field support.<br /> <br /> How does Deviants deal with a Conspiracy that is intrinsically ambiguous? They're not good, and the very nature of Virtue means even their most loyal Deviants can't deny their predation against innocent girls. But they are your allies for a greater cause and offer genuine selfless help you may in fact benefit greatly from.<br /> <br /> Also, the Conspiracy may bring something else to the table: failures. Attempts that became Deviants, but not Magical Girls. Misjudgment of character or the trauma caused result in a Deviant that either don't have the inclination to take up the mantle, or worse, dedicated to ruin everything the Conspiracy works for, even their cause at large.<br /> <br /> My interest is piqued because it's a core theme of the genre: the value of hope and what will happen if you give it up. As much as they may hate the Conspiracy, genuine MG Deviants (and granted, they may not all be &quot;genuine&quot; as far as it goes, even if they take up the cause) keep the hope and belief in others. Those who failed are now hopeless, and may become a danger not only to the Conspiracy, but to innocent people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T19:47:57-07:00","id":1564154,"title":"","content":"The upcoming <b>Night Horrors: Deep Dive</b> for <b>Deviant</b> includes a \u201cConspiracy of Renegades\u201d, using the Conspiracy rules to detail what happens when a bunch of Renegades get together and organize on a large scale. So yes, there's room for a morally ambiguous Conspiracy in <b>Deviant</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T02:39:22-07:00","id":1564163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564154#post1564154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The upcoming <b>Night Horrors: Deep Dive</b> for <b>Deviant</b> includes a \u201cConspiracy of Renegades\u201d, using the Conspiracy rules to detail what happens when a bunch of Renegades get together and organize on a large scale. So yes, there's room for a morally ambiguous Conspiracy in <b>Deviant</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even better if a nerd in the group gives them a pop culture name like &quot;The Justice Society&quot; or &quot;U.N.I.T.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T06:29:36-07:00","id":1564188,"title":"","content":"Should MGs with powers from other blue books, derived from splats or Hunters have access to Spark of Virtue?<br /> <br /> My default answer is yes, but I want a second opinion. I think even those with a Minor Power Stat (the kind that goes only to 5) should be able to buy it and fuse Power Stats.<br /> <br /> Also at Virtue 6+ the Girl should be able to buy traits above 5 like other supernaturals. Maybe it only manifests during transformation, though I am not against this level of XP commitment make her experience and exposure to magic be finally affecting her directly. Becoming greater than life in your civilian identity is also a staple of the Super Hero genre in general, and Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo no less at all.<br /> <br /> We also need a clearer definition of the loadout and budget and their differences. Should the Girl be able to summon multiple copies of the same item? Is a loadout like a physical arsenal, each item only exists in one place at a time? Is it possible to expand this arsenal independent from the budget?<br /> <br /> One source I think worth our time to look for ideas is I Don't Want To Be A Magical Girl. I'm not yet sure if it will hold as a genre example or breaker, but it does have elements to explore that especially fit Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-24T09:58:27-07:00","id":1564947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554670#post1554670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geist's focus on Death would make for a particularly morbid take on the Magical Girl genre; but the Sin-Eater aspect of the game makes it almost as suitable for handling Magical Girl themes as Mage and Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, all-girl Bleach game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1554670#post1554670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves Vampire, Promethean, Mummy, and Beast as the ones that would be hardest to make work. Beast would probably be the hardest, as it's very nearly the &quot;anti-Magical Girl&quot; gameline: its whole premise is about subverting the sorts of tropes and themes that a played-straight a Magical Girl would likely feature. Of the other three\u2026 I'm not sure how I'd rank them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes might be closer to home in a number of ways, i guess? Must admit i'm not super-familiar with Beast at all.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated aside, how well or badly HtV and DtR conspiracies go together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T10:07:31-07:00","id":1564955,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with a magical girl Deviant, is that the transformation is reversible, and often activated when necessary.<br /> <br /> Unless there's a specific condition which forcefully triggers your magical girl form, it would be kind of hard to depict what makes such an existence difficult to live with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T11:55:21-07:00","id":1564959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564955#post1564955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with a magical girl Deviant, is that the transformation is reversible, and often activated when necessary.<br /> <br /> Unless there's a specific condition which forcefully triggers your magical girl form, it would be kind of hard to depict what makes such an existence difficult to live with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monstrous Transformation is a Variation, Controlled Scars are a thing, and Shallow Graves introduces both Techniques and the Dependent Variation Deviation. Magical girl transformations are seldom wholesale changes of who you are as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T18:27:42-07:00","id":1564967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes might be closer to home in a number of ways, i guess? Must admit i'm not super-familiar with Beast at all.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated aside, how well or badly HtV and DtR conspiracies go together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes are extremely narcissistic, for real. While it's unclear if we only know the bad ones or something causes this, the fact is that they are the kind of people who sacrifices anything and anyone for glory without understand or care for what's really at stake or the wellbeing of others.<br /> <br /> Frequently they cause more deaths of innocents than the Beasts, including by murder, and the few who are halfway decent are by actually trying to resist the impetus of becoming murderous assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T19:33:53-07:00","id":1564972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes might be closer to home in a number of ways, i guess? Must admit i'm not super-familiar with Beast at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Hero in the modern context of the Primordial Dream is someone who is driven to find a solution to the presence of Beasts. In ancient times, this meant Oracles interpreting the omens, signs and portents of Begotten activity and learning what place the Horrors had in the world society stood upon, but for thousands of years since then the increasing population and interconnection of humanity and its traumatic interactions with monsters and danger have added noise to the signal to such a degree that the typical context a Hero is encountered in is being marked as the self-aware designated main character of a storied clash with a monster that must be killed at any cost because it is a monster and they are the Hero who kills it, gaining Primordial power through this broadly ritualized murder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On an unrelated aside, how well or badly HtV and DtR conspiracies go together? </div> </div> </div>They mingle. Some Web of Pain conspiracies are monster-hunting groups without necessarily being on the Vigil, and some Hunter conspiracies tilt their pursuits toward the acquisitive and have compromised the aim of defending humanity by exploiting sources of supernatural power to better fight monsters. Both are sufficiently secretive that any conflict between any given two is unlikely to escalate past the scope of cold war.<br /> <br /> The big distinction is that the Web of Pain is extensively interconnected and is sort of a collective human response to supernatural stimulus \u2014 they're the big brother to phenomena like Geist's suggestion to give the Obsession Condition on breaking points resulting from interactions with magical artifacts or Vampire's note that many vampire hunters have Persistent versions of the Conditions caused by the Kiss or the Assault due to particularly dramatic feedings, and the exploitation of mundane and occult resources toward their Principles comes first.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Vigil conspiracies hunt monsters to advance an agenda and make use of magic or advanced science as an emergent phenomenon of a bunch of different people who took up the dangerous work of hunting monsters gradually connecting with each other and organizing to better do that work \u2014 every active member of a Hunter conspiracy is a hunter capable of risking Willpower, engaging in Tactics, and desensitizing the Integrity of the vessel of their soul to exposure to magic and monsters and the evil they do.<br /> <br /> Also significantly, while Vigil conspiracy power sources may occasionally have things go wrong and produce monsters or strange phenomena and their hunters may go rogue to similar effect, the default state of affairs for a group of hunters is that they do not suffer a metaphysical blow to their human nature more significant that that developed by Merit-based psychic powers, ghouls, Wolf-Blooded, or Sleepwalkers. Web of Pain conspiracies lean on their Icons for any supernatural powers their Baseline agents can bring to bear, and those are extremely limited by the scope of the organization compared to producing, recruiting, or capturing and otherwise exploiting people whose volatile superpowers come part and parcel with burning out the part of their metaphysical anatomy that mediates between their soul and the rest of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T14:28:24-07:00","id":1564984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564188#post1564188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should MGs with powers from other blue books, derived from splats or Hunters have access to Spark of Virtue?<br /> <br /> My default answer is yes, but I want a second opinion. I think even those with a Minor Power Stat (the kind that goes only to 5) should be able to buy it and fuse Power Stats.<br /> <br /> Also at Virtue 6+ the Girl should be able to buy traits above 5 like other supernaturals. Maybe it only manifests during transformation, though I am not against this level of XP commitment make her experience and exposure to magic be finally affecting her directly. Becoming greater than life in your civilian identity is also a staple of the Super Hero genre in general, and Mah\u014d Sh\u014djo no less at all.<br /> <br /> We also need a clearer definition of the loadout and budget and their differences. Should the Girl be able to summon multiple copies of the same item? Is a loadout like a physical arsenal, each item only exists in one place at a time? Is it possible to expand this arsenal independent from the budget?<br /> <br /> One source I think worth our time to look for ideas is I Don't Want To Be A Magical Girl. I'm not yet sure if it will hold as a genre example or breaker, but it does have elements to explore that especially fit Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the long delay; I got distracted by other projects. <br /> <br /> I would not fuse Spark of Virtue Virtue with a(nother) Power Stat. With that said, Spark of Virtue can be presented in a way that allows it in any character that has a Virtue; simply say that when it acts like a Power Stat, it doesn't stack: you use whichever of the two is better. Since the &quot;fuel&quot; of Spark of Virtue is Willpower, and <i>everyone</i> in the Chronicles of Darkness has Willpower, you also don't end up with more fuel stats than a supernatural would already have. <br /> <br /> This <i>does</i> mean that the new capabilities provided by Spark of Virtue can't be treated like normal fuel stats, though; because it's operating on a basis where no matter how much of the fuel you've burned, you're always potentially one action away from fully refueling it. So you don't get huge pools of Willpower points to spend; and often, the restriction in the use of a capability can't be reasonably measured through how much Willpower it costs. That's why I borrowed heavily from Deviant's &quot;uses per scene or chapter&quot; logic, along with resets (part of what Deviant calls Adaptations). And instead of having an escalating pool of points to spend, you get more opportunities to refresh your Willpower and to reset the uses of Spark of Virtue. <br /> <br /> So yeah; if you want to allow anyone with a Virtue to take Spark of Virtue, I say go for it. <br /> <br /> I would also say that you should get one free Virtue-based Merit when you take Spark of Virtue, singling out whichever one of them you think best represents the Virtue in question. Any others that you take represent a deeper understanding of that Virtue by the MG. <br /> <br /> For Spark of Virtue 6+, perhaps say that it unlocks Transformed Attributes: additional dots in an Attribute that are only available while Transformed, and which aren't counted when determining if you've hit your ceiling in the Attribute. They have their <i>own</i> limit (one dot per Attribute for each level in Spark of Virtue after 5, and possibly no more dots in the Transformed Attribute than in the underlying Attribute); but any Attributes above 5 <i>without</i> Transformation come from whatever supernature the MG has, not from the Spark of Virtue. <br /> <br /> In terms of the loadout, I wrote the Merit around the assumption that you get one of each thing in the loadout. That's why there are Merits for allowing you to leave a piece of gear behind, instead of it automatically disappearing when you lose it or it's taken from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T14:52:19-07:00","id":1564986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, all-girl Bleach game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about Bleach to say. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes might be closer to home in a number of ways, i guess? Must admit i'm not super-familiar with Beast at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have pointed out, the Heroes that show up in Beast aren't exactly role models; that's part of the &quot;subversion of the monomyth&quot; that's at the heart of Beast \u2014 and, admittedly, a big part of why I can't get into the game, myself. I understand the concepts it's trying for; but it crosses too many lines for me to go there. <br /> <br /> Beast's Heroes are, frankly, both too arrogant and too one-note to be viable player characters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated aside, how well or badly HtV and DtR conspiracies go together?</div> </div> </div> </div>as Satchel mentioned, they go together extremely well. There's a reason I suggested the possibility of a Deviant Conspiracy breaking off from a Hunter Org as part of the MG crossover society for this project. <br /> <br /> Several published Hunter Orgs could double as Deviant Conspiracies, such as the one that features Thaumatechnology: from the Hunter perspective, this is a way to empower the Vigil by letting Hunters partake in supernatures of monsters; from a Deviant perspective, the line between this an Divergence is virtually nonexistent. <br /> <br /> And in the other side of the ledger, the upcoming Deep Dive supplement for Deviant includes a Conspiracy of Renegades, which unironically exists to fight the exploitive Conspiracies in the Web of Pain. To a Hunter, the difference between that and a Hunter Org is razor-thin. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T14:53:49-07:00","id":1564987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564967#post1564967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heroes are extremely narcissistic, for real. While it's unclear if we only know the bad ones or something causes this, the fact is that they are the kind of people who sacrifices anything and anyone for glory without understand or care for what's really at stake or the wellbeing of others.<br /> <br /> Frequently they cause more deaths of innocents than the Beasts, including by murder, and the few who are halfway decent are by actually trying to resist the impetus of becoming murderous assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget that one of the Heroes presented in the book is some puritanical woman, who did not hesitate to kill her own son, after convincing herself he was possessed by the devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T15:08:56-07:00","id":1564988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564947#post1564947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heroes might be closer to home in a number of ways, i guess? Must admit i'm not super-familiar with Beast at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Watch old Disney classics.<br /> <br /> <b>Clayton</b> (Tarzan) and <b>Gaston</b> (Beauty and the Beast) are perfect examples of what a <i>&quot;Hero&quot;</i> is in <b>Beast: the Primordial</b>.<br /> <br /> Which, to summarize: they are ego maniacs, who believe that the whole world revolves around them; and if something emerges to challenge that perception, then they view it as their mission to destroy the perceived threat and bask in the praise that comes with doing so.<br /> <br /> They can not stand the thought of being told they are not the main character of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T15:29:23-07:00","id":1564989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564959#post1564959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monstrous Transformation is a Variation, Controlled Scars are a thing, and Shallow Graves introduces both Techniques and the Dependent Variation Deviation. Magical girl transformations are seldom wholesale changes of who you are as a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>If operating in the context of this Merits-based Template as the common factor for Magical Girls, I would use Compact of Transformation for those changes that are fairly simple (i.e., a shift in clothing and gear), while Monstrous Transformation would be an example of how a supernatural Magical Girl can undergo a more profound change. <br /> <br /> Though this brings up another question: how should such things be synchronized? Do we need a Merit that lets you link Compact of Transformation to a transformational capability native to a particular type of supernatural, such as a werewolf's shapeshifting or an Unchained dropping its Cover? The latter in particular has me wondering, because I could possibly see the Compact of Transformation mitigating perhaps the biggest downside of an Unchained switching to its demonic form: the God-Machine recognizing it for what it is. On the other hand, I don't want to go overboard with Merits: It would be great to be able to say something like &quot;if the MG has some other kind of transformation available to her, the Compact of Transformation automatically chooses one alternate form available to her and synchronizes with it, allowing her to switch into it at the same time it shifts her equipment loadout and appearance.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T15:34:11-07:00","id":1564990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564988#post1564988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Watch old Disney classics.<br /> <br /> <b>Clayton</b> (Tarzan) and <b>Gaston</b> (Beauty and the Beast) are perfect examples of what a <i>&quot;Hero&quot;</i> is in <b>Beast: the Primordial</b>.<br /> <br /> Which, to summarize: they are ego maniacs, who believe that the whole world revolves around them; and if something emerges to challenge that perception, then they view it as their mission to destroy the perceived threat and bask in the praise that comes with doing so.<br /> <br /> They can not stand the thought of being told they are not the main character of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. It has the restriction that that only really happens when the thing challenging their egotistical mindset is a Beast. That, and their powerset is so specific to Beasts that even if someone else _did_ trigger them, they'd be no more dangerous to that person than an ordinary mortal would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T15:45:10-07:00","id":1564992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564990#post1564990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of. It has the restriction that that only really happens when the thing challenging their egotistical mindset is a Beast. That, and their powerset is so specific to Beasts that even if someone else _did_ trigger them, they'd be no more dangerous to that person than an ordinary mortal would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, their powers only kick in when fighting Beasts.<br /> <br /> <i>Specifically Beasts</i><br /> <br /> Which comes as quite the shock when they first encounter a different kind of monster, such as vampires.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, they gain a permanent increase to their power for every Beast they deliver the killing blow to. Which means the longer they are allowed to run around unchecked, the more dangerous they become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T17:38:16-07:00","id":1564994,"title":"","content":"I'd say the two conspiracy types aren't just compatible, but actually there's no meaningful distinction between them at all.<br /> <br /> What each game line does when describing their versions of a secret society including humans is not to ontologically determine that society, but it's relationship to the splat, and to an extent propose rules of interaction.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1. Conspiracy/Cult traits don't exist. They're a means to track the status of an organization in a game whose proposal includes fighting the organization. You can use them across games, fuse them or ignore, this is not terribly relevant.<br /> <br /> 2. Groups just exist individually and will have whatever fits them. Any given group can be a Mystery Cult, a Herd, a Pack, a Mummy Cult, a Krewe, a Hunter and/or Deviant Conspiracy or an Agency or others, each of those as distinct, independent aspects.<br /> <br /> It's less that they're compatible and more that they're just unrelated dimensions.<br /> <br /> 3. Groups interact to whatever extent. The Web of Pain is just a framework to describe this in a game that proposes to track several such groups and their dynamics.<br /> <br /> In a sense, every single secret group in the CoD is part of the Web of Pain. It's just the name Deviants, who are regularly in big picture conflict with groups, call them.<br /> <br /> 4. What makes a Conspiracy relevant for Hunter is if they track supernatural entities and send Hunters against them. What makes it be classified as a Hunter Conspiracy is to have an Endowment Merit to offer.<br /> <br /> What makes a Conspiracy relevant for Deviant is if they track Deviants, which usually means they capture Deviants. That's basically it. <hr /><br /> I'd say a Hero can be a Magical Girl, but seriously, they're the one splat where I'd say it is at the greatest effort to resist their own nature if you use them RAW. Maybe with the exception of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> And I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> here, Clayton and Gaston are excellent examples of what a Hero is. Again, IIRC there's one example Hero that isn't like that, and the whole point is his constant struggle to remind himself that he is basically a fucking addict and needs control, not victories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T18:17:28-07:00","id":1564998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564994#post1564994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a Hero can be a Magical Girl, but seriously, they're the one splat where I'd say it is at the greatest effort to resist their own nature if you use them RAW. Maybe with the exception of the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely the True Fae are the hardest. They're presented as being so utterly disconnected from reality, that they can not comprehend anything that doesn't align with their solipsistic world view.<br /> <br /> One of the major reasons why the Freehold system exists, is because the concept of working together as a community is fundamentally alien to the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T18:23:48-07:00","id":1564999,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 1e had the Charlatans, who were sufficiently sane to potentially be playable. Charlatans are exiled True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T19:31:51-07:00","id":1565001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564994#post1564994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Groups interact to whatever extent. The Web of Pain is just a framework to describe this in a game that proposes to track several such groups and their dynamics.<br /> <br /> In a sense, every single secret group in the CoD is part of the Web of Pain. It's just the name Deviants, who are regularly in big picture conflict with groups, call them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where this falls apart is that &quot;the Web of Pain&quot; is not a diegetic term and the Web of Pain is specifically interconnected in a way that other gamelines' monster-adjacent societies are not.<br /> <br /> Part of this is to provide a ready source of endless vengeance and/or servitude for the Remade, but Hunter conspiracies are not conventionally held to be working with the kind of logistical support that allows them to do what Divergence-related groups of similar scale can do in terms of drawing on the influence of mundane mortal organizations, do not know enough about each other for their agents to assume familiarity and working relationships regardless of how long their organizations have mutually existed, and are not intrinsically concerned with processes that require a machine to maintain \u2014 any conspiracy in the Web has the capacity to Send Agents and hypothetically field enough agents to bring Goon Combat into play because they are organizations that are <i>recruiting Baselines</i> and building resources that partially go into that process, and some of that resource-building ties conspiracies together by Mapping the Conspiracy having rules that require at least a few logistical Nodes that specifically come with links to other conspiracies.<br /> <br /> Deep Dive has a section complementing the material in Black Vans for running other monsters as deviants by providing advice for running other supernatural societies using Deviant's conspiracy mechanics, and part of that advice includes a differently-framed statement of the established fact that most supernatural societies are disconnected from each other; shared philosophical origins don't change the fact that two Summer Courts in even neighboring cities don't necessarily have anything to do with each other, Agencies are typically local affairs regardless of how global the Machine is, and Vigil conspiracies are generally understaffed and paranoid enough that Hunter as a gameline has historically had plants from higher Tiers of organization as a prominent means of recruitment from the &quot;four dopes and a shotgun&quot; level upward. Very few supernatural societies are operating at the level of coordination of the Sects from Mage.<br /> <br /> Different mechanical priorities are not the only reason Hunter manages the task of painting its conspiracies' sociopolitical influence through what Social Merits their Status Merit comes with, and the distinction between the international conglomerate The Cheiron Group and its chronically overquota'd Field Projects Division where all the hunters do their work is not a minor one. The Web of Pain as a structure has cross-applicability with other supernatural social systems, but just as specific pains were taken in the lead-up to Deviant's premiere to emphasize that the Remade template was not an absorptive catch-all for all the subtypes of monster the Contagion Chronicle calls &quot;Dyads,&quot; it is important not to assume &quot;the Web of Pain&quot; means &quot;every supernatural group in the Chronicles of Darkness&quot; simply from the breadth of possible sources of Divergence and the capacity for deviants to interact with people and personlike entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T21:45:41-07:00","id":1565002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564998#post1564998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely the True Fae are the hardest. They're presented as being so utterly disconnected from reality, that they can not comprehend anything that doesn't align with their solipsistic world view.<br /> <br /> One of the major reasons why the Freehold system exists, is because the concept of working together as a community is fundamentally alien to the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charlatans can become sane and from there develop a more human outlook, and a True Fae may have Title manifestations that are linked to Virtue and overall behave like a Magical Girl \u2013 Kidnapping people isn't something they all do or the only thing they do.<br /> <br /> A True Fae that works like a Magical Girl, or empower local MG-like people, is a viable character even if not a Magical Girl in the proper genre sense. And while it's definitely a stretch, one of them becoming a Charlatan and then a proper Magical Girl isn't impossible.<br /> <br /> It's a hard sell, but True Fae legitimately have a way of fitting the bill that's arguably easier to happen than a Hero, and even if not, once happening it fits better.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Heroes are fucked up enough that this is not as clear cut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1565001#post1565001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where this falls apart is that &quot;the Web of Pain&quot; is not a diegetic term and the Web of Pain is specifically interconnected in a way that other gamelines' monster-adjacent societies are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>True-ish and I should have been clear that I was still talking about the human-including groups, but also consider:<br /> <br /> 1. Nodes don't exist outside the abstraction. A Node that links Conspiracies actually represent anyone capable of producing the interaction rather than necessarily formal contact.<br /> <br /> This means the bar is actually low. The two groups don't need to know about each other in any meaningful sense, they need to have someone that can transmit information to or from the other.<br /> <br /> 2. Similarly, recruiting and sending baselines can mean a helluva lot of things in Conspiracy rules because the process is just as abstract. A vampire using their pull on the mayor to cause a regulatory raid, or an Uratha tipping a pack member in the police to cause a raid are both deploying baselines <i>en masse</i> in Conspiracy terms.<br /> <br /> 3. Everything that happens in a Deviant game due to Conspiracy rules can happen at any other game, just not with clear management mechanics.<br /> <br /> On most games the Conspiracy is a plot device that justify NPCs. In Deviant it IS the NPC. That is why they have the rules they have.<br /> <br /> And their connection isn't a unique property, either, nor is it necessarily that strong. What it is is narratively necessary to track.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the Web of Pain means every group because of the possible sources of Divergence, even because not all Conspiracies in it produce Divergence, some only track and capture/recruit Deviants. I'm saying the Web of Pain is an abstraction that, if extended in extremis, will encompass every group because they all can be represented through Conspiracy rules if you want and come to bear in a Deviant game.<br /> <br /> The actual extent of it is actually... A non-thing. It has no extent precisely because it's an abstraction, not an entity. It is as big as it matters for your game, not because you mapped every component, but because that was never the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T07:04:39-07:00","id":1565003,"title":"","content":"Another way to put it is that the edges of the Web of Pain are fuzzy. It's true that the typical Hunter Org feels very different from the typical Deviant Conspiracy; but there's enough overlap in the edge cases that you could easily find yourself transitioning right out of the Web of Pain without realizing it.<br /> <br /> But you <i>would </i>be transitioning out of the Web of Pain. Just as surely as red eventually blends into orange and then yellow in a spectrum, you will eventually find yourself dealing with groups that aren't part of the Web of Pain.<br /> <br /> Go far enough, and you might even find yourself involved in the Magical Girl support network\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-27-2026, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T10:06:37-07:00","id":1565004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1564994#post1564994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> here, Clayton and Gaston are excellent examples of what a Hero is. Again, IIRC there's one example Hero that isn't like that, and the whole point is his constant struggle to remind himself that he is basically a fucking addict and needs control, not victories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's go ahead and toss Claude Frollo into that list as well! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> As for another Hero, who's not so much of a sociopath, there's one young girl who was previously traumatized into a comatose state by a careless Beast. Somehow, she found a way to astral project her spirit into the Primordial Dream, and now hunts monsters by doxxing them on the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T20:04:07-07:00","id":1565011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1565003#post1565003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to put it is that the edges of the Web of Pain are fuzzy. It's true that the typical Hunter Org feels very different from the typical Deviant Conspiracy; but there's enough overlap in the edge cases that you could easily find yourself transitioning right out of the Web of Pain without realizing it.<br /> <br /> But you <i>would </i>be transitioning out of the Web of Pain. Just as surely as red eventually blends into orange and then yellow in a spectrum, you will eventually find yourself dealing with groups that aren't part of the Web of Pain.<br /> <br /> Go far enough, and you might even find yourself involved in the Magical Girl support network\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, because the inverse movement is also possible: any secret organization may come to look for Deviants, even if only a few specific ones, and become part of the Web of Pain.<br /> <br /> Even if this is not a default assumption, there's no reason for most groups, splat or not, to not take an interest on Deviants they find on their territory. Some for research like the Ordo Dracul, the Cheiron Group, some Packs and Krewes, any Mage whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Others because their presence is itself a variable in their power plays or an asset, like the Invictus, some Cults, many Agencies.<br /> <br /> The very nature of Deviance means it can happen anywhere, with no warning and with a specific enough set of circumstances to warrant anyone coming in, which is the aspect Satchel commented later: a supernatural group can come in simply because their own origins: the Embrace, First Change, Awakening, Durance and others; are all just one accident away of producing a Deviant instead.<br /> <br /> And in the end, all those groups are conspiracies, they're the bread and butter of CoD. Deviant calls them that less because Conspiracies are particular to the game and more because the references for the game are more consistently close to pure Conspiracy genre. But in comparison to the rest of the CoD? It's the most generic term possible.<br /> <hr /><br /> I thought about Frollo immediately, but I decided to let him out because he isn't actually after the Hunchback, just Esmeralda.<br /> <br /> Also, his motivation isn't glory, it's pure sexual frustration. It sits in another register of sick assholes being destructive dicks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T21:35:02-07:00","id":1565048,"title":"","content":"Because unlocking the Spark of Virtue requires an active Virtue, each splat's experience is shaped by whether it possesses Virtue natively or must bridge the gap, often demanding dedicated prerequisite investments of Experiences or specialized supernatural advancement currencies.<br /> <br /> Across the Chronicles of Darkness, the Compact of Transformation does not replace native shapeshifting. It acts as a <i>somatic and psychological focus</i>\u2014stabilizing, channeling, and harmonizing monstrous forms into an inspiring Magical Girl persona. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Mortals &amp; Hunters (The Pure Vigil)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Native. Mortals and Hunters retain human Virtue and Vice by default, granting direct access to purchase the Spark of Virtue with standard Experiences without additional supernatural hurdles.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Possessing fragile flesh without innate shapeshifting, mortals rely on the Compact as their sole transformation engine. Opening it projects an enchanted armory, defensive aegis, and perception filter, turning moral conviction into a supernatural bulwark without a monster curse. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Vampires (Kindred: Blush of Life &amp; Protean)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Mask and Dirge. A Kindred must invest Experiences into joining a pious Bloodline like the Daeva <i>Septemi</i> (binding her to a mortal Virtue through the Upright Curse) or purchasing a rare 3-dot Devotion like the Jekyll\u2019s <i>Focus the Aspect</i>. Only after cementing this bridge may she spend Experiences to unlock the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Kindred alternate states involve spending Vitae for the <i>Blush of Life</i> or using <i>Protean</i> for beast forms. The Compact automatically triggers the <i>Blush of Life</i> without Vitae cost during transformation, suffusing dead flesh with warmth and luminous grace. Any <i>Protean</i> shapes adopted while transformed inherit this aesthetic, such as an alabaster-and-starlight wolf. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Werewolves (Uratha: The Sacred Forms &amp; Gauru)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Blood and Bone. Uratha lack a native Virtue slot. A werewolf must first maintain high Harmony (8+) and spend Experiences to purchase the <i>Code of Honor</i> Merit, grounding her savage spirit in a human ethical code before she can spend Experiences to unlock the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Uratha shift across the Five Sacred Forms, notably the lethal <i>Gauru</i> War Form. The Compact overlays battle forms with lunar sanctified plate bearing an Auspice crest. It acts as a psychological stabilizer, granting bonus dice from Virtue on Composure rolls to resist <i>Kuruth</i> (Death Rage), ensuring safe Circle coordination. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Mages (Awakened: Nimbus &amp; Mage Armor)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Native. Mages retain mortal Virtue and Vice, directly anchoring Supernal Wisdom. Storytellers may permit a mage to spend either standard Experiences or <i>Arcane Experiences</i> to unlock the Spark of Virtue, treating the Compact as a profound Supernal Mystery and Dedicated Yantra.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Manifesting the <i>Nimbus</i>, casting <i>Mage Armor</i>, and shapeshifting via <i>Life</i> define a mage's alternate states. The Compact serves as a <i>Dedicated Yantra</i>, instantly activating <i>Mage Armor</i> and igniting her <i>Nimbus</i> as a choreographed transformation. Furthermore, her manifested mystical weapons, starlight wand, and protective regalia function directly as <i>Tool Yantras</i> (or Path tools) for spellcasting, reducing Paradox risks and weaving Supernal rotes into battle when defending Sleepers. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Changelings (Lost: Mask vs. True Mien)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Needle and Thread. A Changeling bridges this gap by spending Experiences on an <i>Entitlement</i> or a specialized <i>Court Mantle</i> tied to solemn, Wyrd-bound Oaths of mortal protection, or by anchoring herself to a Fae-Touched companion before acquiring the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Changelings balance the mundane <i>Mask</i> against the alien <i>True Mien</i>. The Compact translates the True Mien into an inspiring <i>Fae Knight persona</i>, letting mortals see a radiant protector rather than an uncanny fae creature. Wyrd-filtering also baffles True Fae scrying and Hedge-tracking. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Prometheans (Created: Pyros Disfigurements &amp; Bestial Forms)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Elpis and Torment. Manufactured beings do not gain a true Virtue until the New Dawn. However, completing the Refinement of Gold (<i>Aurum</i>) serves as justification to purchase the Spark of Virtue directly with <i>Vitriol Experiences</i>, as her cultivated <i>Elpis</i> matures into something sufficiently like an actual Virtue to sustain the spark.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Spending Pyros exposes grotesque physical <i>Disfigurements</i> and inflames Disquiet. The Compact acts as an alchemical alembic, transmuting scars into radiant golden plate. This suppresses the horror of artificial flesh, buffering passive <i>Disquiet</i> around her Circle and Touchstones. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>7. Sin-Eaters (Geist: Manifestations &amp; Geist Projection)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Hybrid Model. While the Sin-Eater uses Root and Bloom, <i>her bound Geist natively retains a human Virtue and Vice</i> from its mortal life. She can spend Experiences on the Spark of Virtue by investing in high <i>Synergy</i> and deep Remembrance, channeling the Geist's moral memory as the foundation for the transformation.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Sin-Eaters channel ghostly <i>Manifestations</i> and project their Geist. The Compact enables two paradigms: in <b>Avatar Guardian mode</b>, the human stays in civilian clothes while <i>the projected Geist transforms</i>, wielding spectral gear through its own native Virtue; in <b>Spectral Mantle mode</b>, the Geist fuses over the Sin-Eater as wearable ghost-plate, allowing her to phase through attacks in Twilight. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>8. Mummies (Arisen: Sekhem Flare &amp; Sybaris)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Native. Mummies retain standard Virtue and Vice on their character sheets. An Arisen spends Experiences to raise <i>Memory</i> through virtuous Sebayt or to integrate a Virtue-fettered Vestige into her tomb\u2019s Lifeweb, providing the stable moral clarity required to awaken the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Awakening to high Sekhem causes an apocalyptic flare and <i>Sybaris</i>, a terror aura that drives mortals mad. The Compact structures Sekhem surges into pharaonic ceremonial armor, redirecting <i>Sybaris</i> away from allies and converting dread into an aegis that shields her Circle. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>9. Demons (Unchained: Demon Form / Apocalyptic Form)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Native. Renegade angels of the God-Machine natively possess Virtue and Vice as the core of their free agency, spending standard Experiences directly on the Spark of Virtue. They may also treat the Compact as an advanced Embed or customized Subroutine purchased through normal progression.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> An Unchained's biomechanical <i>Demon Form</i> risks burning Cover and alerting Infrastructure. The Compact functions as an <i>encrypted Cover-Preserving Subroutine</i>, deploying radiant wings, Aetheric barriers, and chrome weaponry over her mortal identity without burning Cover dots, bleeding glitches, or alerting hunters. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>10. Beasts (Begotten: Atavisms &amp; Lair Forms)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Life and Legend. A Beast's human anchor is her <i>Life</i> trait\u2014a descriptive human adjective that serves as a functional Virtue equivalent. She spends Experiences to anchor this human bond against her predatory Horror before spending Experiences to manifest the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> Channeling predatory <i>Atavisms</i> mutates the Beast with wings, fangs, or scales. The Compact encases these mutations in sleek nightmare-plate, re-contextualizing her Horror as a <i>Nightmare Sentinel</i> and channeling hunger into defending her human <i>Life</i> anchors. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>11. Deviants (Remade: Variations &amp; Scars)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue &amp; Experience Investment:</b> Replaced by Loyalty and Conviction. The Divergence breaks standard Anchors. A Remade must first spend Experiences on the 3-dot <i>Bleeding Heart</i> Merit to consciously reclaim a human Virtue, which then serves as the prerequisite to spend Experiences on the Spark of Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Native State &amp; Compact Alignment:</b> A Deviant cleanly separates her external gear from her bodily mutations. The Compact of Transformation governs her external equipment loadout\u2014projecting her enchanted weapons, defensive regalia, and perception filter. Meanwhile, the <i>Monstrous Transformation</i> Variation provides the physical changes to the Magical Girl herself. A player can tie specific physical Variations (such as heightened senses, natural weaponry, armored carapace, or inhuman agility) to <i>Monstrous Transformation</i>, making them accessible only while transformed. The Compact harmonizes these visceral bodily alterations, framing her cybernetic or biological mutations into an aesthetically unified, heroic battle form rather than a terrifying freak of science.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T22:03:25-07:00","id":1565049,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of borrowing some ideas from <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b> for the Mascots, treating them as a sort of inversion of Infernal Demons who come from a Virtue-infused otherworld. They would have a similar taxonomy to the Infernals in the sense that they could end up anchoring to plushies, &quot;Claiming&quot; natural animals to become one with them (giving us the fully-physical Mascots that Magical Girls usually deal with), or fusing with various Ephemeral Entities to produce specialized subtypes like Spirits of Light for werewolves, appropriate Supernal Entities for mages, Elpidim companions for Prometheans, hobgoblin friends for changelings, &quot;ghost animals&quot; for Sin-Eaters, and so on. <br /> <br /> This allows us to customize the Mascot to reflect each gameline's cosmology and metaphysics while still providing a unified Magical Girl metaphysical overlay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T23:44:01-07:00","id":1565050,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Vampiric Magical Girl: The Crimson Rose</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Kindred Magical Girl embodies the <i>Gothic Romance</i> archetype\u2014a defiant rebellion of human love against the predatory cynicism of the Danse Macabre. Clad in midnight-crimson silk, Victorian velvet, corset laces, and climbing rose motifs, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to force her undead corpse to answer to moral conviction rather than the Beast.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Defiance of the Beast:</b> A Kindred Magical Girl lives in constant tension between the cold paranoia of the night and the warm memory of mortal empathy. Every sunset, the Beast urges her to exploit, dominate, and feed. Her transformation is a romantic, public refusal to become a corpse-puppet of the elders.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Advancements:</b> Kindred replace native human Virtue with <i>Mask</i> and <i>Dirge</i>. To unlock the Spark of Virtue, she cannot rely on native traits; she must invest Experiences into a dedicated bridge. This is achieved by joining a holy or ascetic Bloodline like the Daeva <i>Septemi</i> (binding herself to a mortal Virtue via the Upright Curse) or acquiring rare 3-dot Devotions like the Jekyll\u2019s <i>Focus the Aspect</i> (replacing Dirge with a temporary Virtue during the Blush of Life).<br /> <br /> <b>Thermal Transmutation of Vitae:</b> Opening her Compact triggers the <i>Blush of Life</i> without Vitae cost during her transformation scene. The Spark burns through dead veins, transmuting cold, coagulated Vitae into rose-gold starlight warmth. Her corpse flushes with breath and color, her dead eyes regain a bright sparkle, and her fangs retract into a radiant smile, temporarily silencing the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Echo of Humanity:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, her moral sincerity resists decay: when comforting mortals or resisting the Beast's frenzy, she treats her <i>Humanity</i> as two dots higher for the scene.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Native Powers &amp; Clan Disciplines</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Physical Disciplines (Celerity, Resilience, Vigor):</b> These form her supernatural combat chassis. She executes gravity-defying acrobatic leaps across rooftops leaving flurries of glowing rose petals, performs balletic martial spins, and absorbs building-shattering impacts without spilling a drop of blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Majesty vs. Nightmare:</b> Predatory dread inverts into <i>Protective Awe &amp; Heartfelt Grace</i>. Rather than paralyzing innocents with horror, her presence radiates unshakeable moral defiance that soothes civilian panic while freezing monstrous abusers in their tracks.<br /> <br /> <b>Animalism &amp; Protean:</b> <i>Animalism</i> becomes the classic ability to converse with city wildlife, enlisting stray cats, doves, and ravens as neighborhood lookouts. When utilizing <i>Protean</i> while transformed, her alternate shapes inherit her regalia's aesthetic, manifesting as an alabaster wolf with glowing starlight markings or a swirling cloud of luminous rose petals.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Covenant-Specific Arts &amp; Sorceries</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul (The Coils &amp; Scales of the Dragon):</b> Dragon initiates treat transformation as the ultimate crucible for the Great Work, refining dead flesh through human virtue rather than cold mutilation.<br /> <i>The Coil of the Beast</i> turns frenzy management into a moment of emotional focus, clasping her hands over her chest in a soft aura to calm her inner predator into chivalric resolve.<br /> <i>The Coil of Blood</i> tempers predatory thirst, allowing her to subsist on symbolic, consensual sips or survive extended sieges without starving into atrocities.<br /> <i>The Coil of Banes (The Sun's Shield)</i> allows her Compact's aegis to deflect fatal solar rays in showers of prism sparkles, converting sunlight into a heroic timer or permitting daylight missions alongside mortal allies.<br /> <i>The Scales of the Dragon</i> purify her surroundings, transmuting toxic metaphysical resonance into pristine sanctuaries.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lancea et Sanctum (Theban Sorcery):</b> Blood sacrifices are replaced by purified tears, devotional hymns, and sacred vows. Chanted rites manifest as radiant starlight and choral resonance rather than biblical rot.<br /> Powers like <i>Blandishment of Sin</i> manifest as a piercing, compassionate gaze that forces abusers to confront their guilt.<br /> <i>Sanctuary</i> projects an impenetrable cathedral of translucent stained-glass light repelling spirits, demons, and Strix.<br /> <i>Vengeance of the Righteous</i> unleashes cascading pillars of sacred dawn-fire that immolate fiends while leaving mortals and architecture untouched.<br /> <br /> <b>The Circle of the Crone (Cru\u00e1c):</b> Visceral pagan bloodletting transforms into spiritual botany, lunar nature magic, and life-weaving. Cuts and blood sacrifices are replaced by blooming starlight vines and glowing dew.<br /> Rites like <i>Rigor Mortis</i> summon flowering briars from the earth to entangle and disarm foes without lethal mutilation.<br /> <i>Hydra's Vitae</i> coats weapons in glowing lunar nectar that dispels illusions, soothes corrupted nature spirits, and shatters dark curses.<br /> <i>Fountain of Blood</i> becomes a spring of warm, restorative starlight waters that heals allies and revives blighted urban soil.<br /> <br /> <b>The Invictus (Sworn Oaths, Dynastic Investments, &amp; Spurred Vitae):</b> Feudal subjugation is turned into chivalric knighthood and sacred friendship pledges.<br /> <i>Oaths of Fealty</i> become shimmering tethers of mutual protection; upholding her sworn word grants bonus dice to Composure and defense, while betrayal inflicts supernatural vertigo upon enemies.<br /> <i>Dynastic Investments</i> reframe aristocratic holdings as an enchanted support network\u2014community centers, youth shelters, and hidden botanical gardens providing safe harbor.<br /> <i>Spurred Vitae</i> expresses as high-society fencing, disarming foes with precision and ringing crystal chimes.<br /> <br /> <b>The Carthian Movement (Carthian Law &amp; Guerrilla Tech):</b> Revolutionary theories become the ultimate expression of universal solidarity.<br /> <i>Carthian Law</i> levels the playing field: activating her Compact suppresses the generational advantages of elder Blood Potency and ancient Disciplines, forcing tyrants to face young heroes on equal moral footing.<br /> <i>Modern Technomancy</i> converts city surveillance into perception-filter relays, smartphone networks into early-warning monster radar, and street-art graffiti into warding glyphs shielding neighborhoods from the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Mascot Dynamics: The Empyrean Inversion</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Anti-Strix Companion:</b> While vampires are preyed upon by the <i>Strix</i>\u2014sinister shadow-owls driven by malice and corpse possession\u2014her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean spirit of hope and virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbiotic Manifestation:</b> It typically Claim-merges with a natural creature to become a white dove of dawn, an ivory barn owl, or an alabaster kitten, possessing human speech and mystical awareness.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy:</b> Instead of feeding on suffering, the Mascot sustains its Essence on genuine expressions of Humanity and active Virtue. It stands sentinel over the sleeping vampire during vulnerable Daysleep hours, warning of approaching hunters, sunlight leaks, or elder assassins.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T23:48:59-07:00","id":1565051,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Werewolf Magical Girl: The Lunar Paladin</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Uratha Magical Girl embodies the <i>Lunar Paladin</i> archetype\u2014a sacred knight of the two worlds balancing the savage animism of the Hisil with the warmth of human bonds. Clad in silver-and-mother-of-pearl battle armor layered over animistic spirit charms and bearing her Auspice crest, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to master the predator within, transforming bloody hunting rites into a protective shield for her pack and territory.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Sacred Duty over Savage Bloodlust:</b> Caught between human society and the predatory Shadow, her central struggle is managing <i>Kuruth</i> (Death Rage)\u2014the unthinking fury of Father Wolf that risks tearing allies apart. Her magical girl persona is a solemn vow of martial discipline: channeling apex predatory strength exclusively into protecting the vulnerable and preserving pack harmony.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Advancements:</b> Uratha replace human Virtue with <i>Blood</i> and <i>Bone</i>. Because the Spark of Virtue requires an active Virtue, she must bridge this divide. She maintains high <i>Harmony</i> (8+) and spends Experiences on the <i>Code of Honor</i> Merit, anchoring her savage spirit in an ethical framework before purchasing the Spark of Virtue. Alternatively, Wolf-Blooded kin retaining native Virtues provide an empathetic conduit.<br /> <br /> <b>Two-World Soul &amp; Spiritual Essence:</b> Possessing a soul woven of Flesh and Spirit, she channels her spiritual <i>Essence</i> through human compassion. The Compact overlays her form with consecrated lunar battle-plate that adds bonus dice from Virtue to Composure rolls against Death Rage, keeping her moral conscience intact during intense combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Harmony:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, her pack-brotherhood extends beyond blood kin. Her moral presence soothes territorial anxiety, allowing disparate supernatural beings to coordinate within her territory without triggering instinctual hostility.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Sacred Forms &amp; Primal Transformations</b></span><br /> <br /> The Compact does not suppress native shapeshifting; it sanctifies and harmonizes the Five Sacred Forms with protective heraldry:<br /> <br /> <b>Hishu (Human):</b> In civilian guise, she appears as an athletic, perceptive mortal. Opening the Compact instantly equips her enchanted lunar armor, aegis, and perception filter without requiring physical shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <b>Dalu (Near-Human):</b> Her frame broadens with feral muscle, her canines lengthen, and her eyes ignite with predatory amber light. The Compact weaves heraldic tabards and etched silver greaves over her bulk, framing her as an imposing, athletic guardian rather than a terrifying brute.<br /> <br /> <b>Gauru (The War Form):</b> The towering nine-foot wolf-monster of slaughter is overlaid with sculpted, interlocking lunar plate bearing her glowing Auspice crest. The Compact acts as a psychological stabilizer on the form's ferocious timer: instead of a rabid slaughterhouse machine, she moves like a disciplined paladin executing precision martial arts, protecting her Circle from friendly fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Urshul (Near-Wolf) &amp; Urhan (Wolf):</b> Her predatory wolf shapes manifest as majestic, silver-and-white celestial beasts adorned with starlight markings along their flanks, leaving shimmering lunar footprints across city rooftops.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Native Powers: Auspice Moon Gifts &amp; Spirit Rites</b></span><br /> <br /> Filtered through the Spark of Virtue, the Uratha\u2019s animistic Gifts and bloody Rites invert into heroic arts:<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice Moon Gifts:</b><br /> <i>Rahu (Full Moon - Cahirith):</i> Overwhelming martial dominance. Her strikes land with the resonant weight of celestial meteors, shattering armor with shockwaves of silver light and disarming foes through righteous close-quarters discipline.<br /> <i>Cahalith (Gibbous Moon - Elunim):</i> Inspiring battle-hymns, stirring anthems, and visionary omens. She sings or shouts commands that weave an aurora-like protective canopy over her squad, purging despair and rallying morale.<br /> <i>Elodoth (Half Moon - Kamirith):</i> Sacred diplomacy and balance. She manifests ribbons of spirit-light that bind monsters, enforce temporary truces, and compel hostile spirits to answer truthfully under sacred law.<br /> <i>Ithaeur (Crescent Moon - Hathis):</i> Occult spirit-working. Her wand or staff blazes with pale moonlight that banishes spiritual pollution, dispels possession, and cleanses tainted loci in city alleys.<br /> <i>Irraka (New Moon - Irra):</i> Shadow-dancing and phantom-step movement. She dissolves into sparkling lunar motes, strikes critically from blind spots, and leaves diversionary decoys that confound enemy tracking.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Gifts &amp; Wolf Gifts:</b><br /> Scent-tracking becomes an intuitive empathic radar, allowing her to sniff out the &quot;bitter tang of malice&quot; or the &quot;chill of grief.&quot; Prowling powers turn into silent rooftop dashes, while territorial howling transforms into clear, rallying chimes heard across spiritual dimensions.<br /> <br /> <b>Rites as Sacred Pack Ceremonies:</b><br /> Visceral blood-rites are recontextualized as collaborative, emotional ceremonies\u2014holding hands across a circle to erect boundary wards (<i>Sacred Territory</i>), performing communal cleansing rituals to restore blighted loci, and sealing pacts of friendship that empower the Circle.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Tribal Philosophies &amp; Specialized Lodges</b></span><br /> <br /> Each of the Tribes of the Moon brings a distinct ideological flavor to the Lunar Paladin:<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons (S\u03cdrthe-Ur):</b> Martial purists. She embraces the sacred duel, using her silver spear or bladed claws strictly to defeat predatory alpha monsters and tyrannical oppressors. Her specialized Lodges emphasize chivalric single combat and protective bodyguard oaths.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows (Kamdu-Ur):</b> Occult scholars and spirit undertakers. She treats the Hisil with profound respect, functioning as a diplomatic bridge. Her Lodges negotiate peaceful pacts with ancient spirit-gods and ensure the Dead and Ephemeral remain in their proper realms.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness (Menknan-Ur):</b> Wilderness wardens. She specializes in guerrilla ambushes, stealth defense, and environmental conservation. Her Lodges protect pristine nature reserves and hidden city parks from toxic industrial corruption and spiritual blight.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters (Sagrim-Ur):</b> Modern urban vanguards. She integrates street culture, modern fashion, and technology into her loadout. Her Lodges adapt subway networks into sacred spirit trails, weaponize cyber-spirits, and protect mortal communities from urban decay.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords (Skolis-Ur):</b> Aristocratic leaders of winter resolve. She demands unyielding moral discipline from herself and her Circle. Her Lodges act as high-command tactical units, enduring bitter hardships without flinching to shield territory from ruin.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Wolves (Thihirtha Numea):</b> Independent rebels unbound by tribal vows. She crafts an idiosyncratic, intensely personal magical girl identity, answering only to her local pack and personal moral code.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: Anointed Totems of the Shadow</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Anointed Totem:</b> Instead of a blood-demanding spirit totem, her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity that has fused with a benevolent Gauntlet spirit\u2014such as a spirit of Dawn, Starlight, or Pack Loyalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical &amp; Ephemeral Manifestation:</b> It frequently appears as a celestial miniature animal\u2014a multi-tailed kitsune, an ivory badger, or an antlered hare. It can cross the Gauntlet effortlessly, scout the Hisil, and converse telepathically with packmates.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy:</b> The Totem-Mascot feeds on genuine acts of pack loyalty, self-sacrifice, and human virtue rather than raw meat. It spends Essence to bless the pack with specialized support Numina: <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> (warding territory against spiritual rot), <i>Resonant Guidance</i> (granting bonus dice to Harmony rolls), and <i>Aegis Flare</i> (granting emergency armor to allies).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Macro-Societal &amp; Regional Politics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Regional Protectorate:</b> When multiple packs form a Protectorate across a metropolitan valley, the Lunar Paladin serves as the diplomatic keystone. Her ability to navigate human society without losing spiritual teeth makes her the ideal ambassador to coordinate territorial borders between rural mountain packs and downtown alley packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Friction with The Pure (Anshega):</b> The Pure Tribes view her with incandescent hatred. To the Ivory Claws, Predator Kings, and Fire-Touched, her embrace of human Virtue and refusal to revel in slaughter is the ultimate betrayal of Father Wolf\u2019s legacy. They deploy dedicated kill-teams to extinguish her light, making her battles with the Pure deeply personal and ideologically ferocious.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bale Hounds (Asahkaru):</b> Corrupted wolves serving the Soulless Maeljin view her radiant Spark of Virtue as an existential threat. She acts as a frontline inquisitor capable of sniffing out spiritual rot, purifying infected loci, and redeeming or executing traitors.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Diplomacy:</b> Naturally territorial, werewolf packs frequently clash with vampire domains and changeling freeholds. The Lunar Paladin acts as the primary envoy of the Starlight Compact, proving to suspicious Princes and seasonal Monarchs that werewolves can be honorable chivalric allies rather than mindless, rampaging beasts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:01:17-07:00","id":1565052,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Mage Magical Girl: The Supernal Star-Weaver</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Awakened Magical Girl embodies the <i>Supernal Star-Weaver</i> archetype\u2014a visionary mystic who sees the Fallen World as a fragile illusion to be healed through love, wonder, and moral truth. Flowing in celestial gowns, geometric runes, and swirling stardust, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to anchor Supernal willworking in radical human empathy, proving magic belongs to all humanity rather than the vaults of ivory towers.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Compassion over Hubris:</b> The central hazard of the Awakened is Hubris\u2014cold, obsessive detachment viewing Sleepers as collateral damage in pursuit of Mysteries. The Mage Magical Girl consciously inverts this ethos: her power is an act of communal service, treating the Supernal not as a ladder to personal godhood, but as living proof that reality can be redeemed from the Lie.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Advancements:</b> Native. Mages retain human Virtue and Vice, directly anchoring moral integrity and Supernal <i>Wisdom</i>. She spends standard Experiences directly to awaken the Spark of Virtue; Storytellers may also permit <i>Arcane Experiences</i> by treating the Compact and Heart-Weave matrix as an enlightened Supernal Mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awakened Soul &amp; Supernal Alignment:</b> Having inscribed her name upon a Supernal Watchtower, opening the Compact serves as an immediate metaphysical alignment: her <i>Nimbus</i> blazes forth as a dazzling sensory spectacle, while her innate <i>Mage Armor</i> snaps into place reflexively as an enchanted barrier without requiring standard casting actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Deflecting the Lie:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, her public theatricality softens the sting of the Quiescence. By framing Supernal feats within the cultural archetype of the heroic magical protector, she reduces the ambient dread that normally drives Sleeper witnesses into soul-numbing madness.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Spellcraft, Yantras, &amp; The Choreography of Will</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Compact as Dedicated Yantra:</b> The Compact functions as a high-potency <i>Dedicated Yantra</i>. Opening it establishes the ritual headspace for casting, grounding volatile Supernal forces in her heroic persona and reducing Paradox risk across her rotes.<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment Loadout as Tool Yantras:</b> Manifested armaments\u2014starlight wands, heart-crested staves, ribbon-whips, or mirrored shields\u2014function directly as <i>Path Tool Yantras</i> or <i>Order Tool Yantras</i>. Pointing her wand or thrusting her staff grants standard Yantra dice bonuses while steering spell resonance toward protection and purification.<br /> <br /> <b>Persona Mantras &amp; Signature Finishers:</b> Magical chants, incantations, and named special attacks act as <i>Mantra Yantras</i>. Spells are not cast as mute, clinical gestures; they are executed with dramatic poses, twirling sequences, and called-out signature moves (e.g., casting a Forces/Prime lightning strike as <i>&quot;Radiant Starlight Nova!&quot;</i>), turning spellcasting into an inspiring performance.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. The Ten Arcana in the Magical Girl Prism</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Subtle Arcana:</b><br /> <i>Death:</i> Inverting bleak necromancy into compassionate psychopomp magic. Summoning spirit-lanterns, guiding lingering ghosts to peaceful closure, and banishing abyssal rot with purifying phantom flame.<br /> <i>Fate:</i> Weaving sparkling threads of destiny. Manipulating probability to steer innocents from harm, binding monsters with ribbons of geas, and guiding dramatic coincidences.<br /> <i>Mind:</i> The heart of magical girl empathy. Radiating emotional comfort, cleansing trauma, speaking telepathically with her Circle, and piercing illusions with mental clarity.<br /> <i>Prime:</i> Pure Supernal radiance. Conjuring energy barriers, purifying tainted loci, and unleashing prismatic beams of dawn that dissolve abyssal corruption.<br /> <i>Spirit:</i> Sacred animism. Peering across the Gauntlet, awakening urban spirits into allies, and soothing raging Shadow-beasts with harmonic chimes.<br /> <br /> <b>The Gross Arcana:</b><br /> <i>Forces:</i> Visual pyrotechnics and aerial mobility. Riding ribbons of light, gliding on winds, generating forcefields, and blasting foes with non-lethal lightning and lasers.<br /> <i>Life:</i> Floral vitality and biological healing. Mending injuries in warm emerald light, growing protective briars, and neutralizing biological blights.<br /> <i>Matter:</i> Transmuting mundane objects. Turning falling debris into flower petals, hardening fabrics into armor, and reshaping terrain to trap foes.<br /> <i>Space:</i> Spatial bending and dimensional rescue. Teleporting squadmates in bursts of starlight, folding distance to catch falling victims, and raising spatial sanctuaries.<br /> <i>Time:</i> Chronological grace. Accelerating reaction time, rewinding localized damage to save civilians, and freezing incoming projectiles in mid-air.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Paths of the Supernal Watchtowers</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus (Enchanters of Arcadia):</b> Tricksters weaving Fate and Time clad in spun-glass ribbons, dancing through combat to turn grim fate into joyful serendipity.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos (Warlocks of the Pandemonium):</b> Controllers of Space and Mind in velvet and mirrors, breaking psychological chains and teleporting across the field.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros (Necromancers of Stygia):</b> Gothic heroines commanding Death and Matter in obsidian and black lace, transmuting leaden despair into golden hope.<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos (Theurgists of the Aether):</b> Celestial paladins channeling Forces and Prime in white-and-gold armor, wielding starlight lances and sacred lightning.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsus (Shamans of the Primal Wild):</b> Guardians of Life and Spirit in living ivy and floral garlands, channeling the earth to summon spirit beasts and shield innocents.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. The Orders of the Pentacle &amp; The Seers</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Adamantine Arrow:</b> The elite martial vanguard. She treats magical girl combat as an art of chivalric defense, taking oaths of service to protect her Circle and taking the brunt of enemy fire without retreating.<br /> <br /> <b>The Free Council:</b> Technomantic innovators. Drawing inspiration from anime, pop music, and digital art, she uses holographic wands and smartphone-integrated compacts to prove modern human culture channels Supernal truth without archaic dogma.<br /> <br /> <b>The Guardians of the Veil:</b> The counter-intelligence shield. Operating as an enigmatic &quot;Dark Magical Girl,&quot; she strikes from shadows, using stealth and deception to neutralize occult threats before Sleepers face Paradox.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mysterium:</b> Arcane scholars and relic hunters. Guided by ancient grimoires, she travels to forgotten crypts to rescue sacred artifacts from corrupt hands, treating every mystery as a story waiting to be understood.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silver Ladder:</b> The visionary leaders. She rallies mages, Sleepers, and other supernatural beings under unity, working tirelessly toward the universal Awakening of humankind.<br /> <br /> <b>The Seers of the Throne (Antagonists):</b> Servants of the Exarchs view her with venomous contempt. To them, her message of love, hope, and enlightenment threatens the Lie that keeps humanity enslaved, leading them to deploy corporate enforcers to extinguish her spark.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Mascot Dynamics: Supernal Familiars &amp; Goetic Guides</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Celestial Familiar:</b> Her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity fused with a <b>Supernal Familiar</b> (Rank 1\u20132 spirit, ghost, or goetia) possessing the <i>Familiar Manifestation Condition</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbiotic Link &amp; Remote Casting:</b> The mage and her Mascot share a permanent Connected Sympathetic link. She can perceive through its senses as a reflexive action and channel spells remotely through it using Reach without needing the Space Sympathetic Range Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Energy Transmutation (Mana \u21c4 Essence):</b> They freely convert resources: her Mana becomes the Mascot\u2019s Essence, and the Mascot's Essence converts into Mana to fuel high-potency rotes.<br /> <br /> <b>Reformation:</b> If discorporated in battle, the Mascot does not perish; it reforms within the sanctuary of the mage\u2019s Signature Nimbus, ready to counsel her once again.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>7. Macro-Societal &amp; Regional Politics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Municipal Consilium:</b> A Mage Magical Girl challenges the local parliament. While Hierarchs worry over the <i>Lex Magica</i> and Paradox, her ability to soothe Sleeper panic and mitigate Paradox makes her an invaluable crisis vanguard.<br /> <br /> <b>Cabal Solidarity &amp; Shared Sanctums:</b> Within her local Cabal, she provides the emotional glue that holds volatile personalities together. She pools resources to sanctify the Cabal's <i>Sanctum</i> and <i>Hallow</i>, turning cold occult workshops into warm communal safe havens.<br /> <br /> <b>Defying the Abyss:</b> In regional occult wars, she stands as the ultimate antidote to Abyssal incursions. While other mages meet the void with fearful paranoia, her unyielding moral conviction and radiant Supernal light purge void-taint, proving love and truth are the true masters of reality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:08:11-07:00","id":1565053,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Promethean Magical Girl: The Golden Alchemist</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Created Magical Girl embodies the <i>Golden Alchemist</i> archetype\u2014an artificial being who refuses the tragic fate of a soulless monster, using love and selfless sacrifice to transmute the agony of her existence into radiant human warmth. Clad in porcelain-white alchemical plate, gilded filigree, and warm solar halos, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to anchor her quest for mortality, proving that a soul is not merely something one is born with, but something forged through love.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Quest for Human Love:</b> The Created begins life as an animated corpse or artificial construct devoid of a true human soul, hounded by the rejection of <i>Disquiet</i> and the destructive pull of <i>Torment</i>. Her psychology is defined by pure, heartbreaking longing: she yearns to touch without burning, to belong without driving communities mad, and to understand human empathy. Her transformation is her sacred sanctuary\u2014the one moment where the world looks at her with adoration instead of instinctive revulsion.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Vitriol Advancement:</b> Prometheans replace human Virtue with <i>Elpis</i> and <i>Torment</i>. While a true Virtue is typically attained only upon completing the Great Work at the New Dawn, walking the Refinement of Gold (<i>Aurum</i>) serves as justification to purchase the Spark of Virtue directly with <b>Vitriol Experiences</b>. Through deep study of mortality, her cultivated <i>Elpis</i> (the divine spark of hope) matures into something sufficiently like an actual Virtue to sustain the Spark.<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemical Transmutation of Disquiet:</b> The Compact functions as an energetic alembic. When she channels Pyros, the Compact transmutes the volatile, unnatural flux of the Divine Fire into radiant, golden alchemical plate. Her horrific scars, stitches, and surgical seams become glowing golden <i>Kintsugi</i> lines, while the toxic aura of <i>Disquiet</i> is buffered, allowing her to fight alongside mortal allies without driving them to paranoia or violence.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crucible of Fellowship:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, her artificial nature ceases to be a curse. The empathetic network of the Heart-Weave provides the emotional ballast she needs to stave off <i>Wasteland</i> generation, converting her solitary Pilgrimage into a shared journey of mutual redemption.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Transmutations &amp; Bestowments in the Heroic Crucible</b></span><br /> <br /> When channeled through the Spark of Virtue, the raw, volatile power of the Divine Fire is refined into protective, purifying arts:<br /> <br /> <b>Lineage Bestowments (The Gifts of the Demiurge):</b><br /> <i>Frankensteins (Brutes):</i> Unstoppable kinetic force. Her strikes land with the resonant chime of great cathedral bells, cleaving through barriers to shield allies while deflecting heavy artillery off her porcelain plate.<br /> <i>Galateids (Darlings):</i> Mesmerizing grace and empathy. Her aura pacifies hostilities, disarming aggressive monsters through sheer heartbreaking beauty and inspiring mortals to acts of bravery.<br /> <i>Osirans (Nephews):</i> Solemn sovereignty over death and revival. Her touch knits together broken tissues, purges necrotic blights, and revives dying flora.<br /> <i>Tammuz (Workers):</i> Tireless endurance. She absorbs building-shattering impacts without flinching, standing as an unyielding wall between monsters and civilians.<br /> <i>Ulgan (Rhapsodes):</i> Spirit-sight and twilight navigation. Peering through the shroud to parley with wandering shades, guiding lost souls and banishing ephemeral parasites with flashes of dawn.<br /> <br /> <b>The Transmutations (Alchemical Arts):</b><br /> <i>Vulcanus (Fire &amp; Electricity):</i> Jagged, flesh-searing arc flashes transform into warm, golden solar radiance and harmless firework motes that incinerate Pandoran corruption while gently illuminating the night.<br /> <i>Saturninus (Lead &amp; Purity):</i> The ultimate shield against contagion. She absorbs environmental radiation, toxic chemical spills, and supernatural plagues into her alchemical aegis, transmuting harmful toxins into inert golden dust.<br /> <i>Deucalion &amp; Corporeum (Anatomy):</i> Physical augmentations do not distort her body into a grotesque flesh-golem; her skin assumes the unyielding, luminous sheen of polished marble, and her agility mirrors a master dancer.<br /> <i>Mesmerism &amp; Vitality:</i> Hypnotic commands become inspiring rallying cries that break psychological despair, while internal Pyros surges mend her wounds in a flash of warm light.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. The Alchemical Refinements &amp; Philosophies</b></span><br /> <br /> Each Refinement shapes the Golden Alchemist\u2019s path toward the New Dawn:<br /> <br /> <b>Aurum (Gold - The Mortalistas):</b> The core philosophy of the Promethean Magical Girl. Emulating mortal virtue, building civilian friendships, and learning the beauty of ordinary life. Her loadout features radiant gold trim, ribbons, and heart motifs.<br /> <br /> <b>Ferrum (Iron - The Titans):</b> Martial mastery and physical discipline. She treats her transformed body as an alchemical weapon forged to slay Pandorans and abyssal incursions, embodying chivalric self-sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <b>Argentum (Silver - The Mystics):</b> Spiritual and energetic insight. Focusing on understanding the ephemeral ecology, consulting spirits, and transmuting psychic resonances to keep her Circle safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Cuprum (Copper - The Pariahs):</b> Solitary survival and self-reliance. Often acting as the brooding &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; magical girl who watches over the city from afar, fearing her Disquiet will hurt others until the Circle proves her loved.<br /> <br /> <b>Plumbum (Lead - The Originists):</b> Studying the nature of the Created and the limits of the flesh. She analyzes monster biology to engineer targeted alchemical counters, neutralizing supernatural blights.<br /> <br /> <b>The Centimanus (The Hundred Handed - Antagonists):</b> Corrupted alchemists who embrace Torment and create monstrosities. They serve as primary nemeses, deploying twisted Pandoran abominations that test her compassion and resolve.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Mascot Dynamics: The Elpidim Companion</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Living Spark of Hope:</b> While Prometheans are hounded by ravenous Pandorans\u2014mindless horrors born of dormant Azoth\u2014her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity fused with pure Azothic resonance: an <b>Elpidim</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Manifestation:</b> It frequently appears as a golden clockwork sparrow, a radiant winged salamander, or an animated porcelain cherub. It is completely immune to Disquiet, existing as a beacon of warmth and unconditional love.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Economy &amp; Emotional Ballast:</b> The Elpidim feeds on genuine acts of hope, forgiveness, and moral courage. It spends Essence to buffer the Promethean\u2019s Torment, decipher prophetic Elpis visions, and project <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to prevent the surrounding terrain from decaying into a Wasteland during extended battles.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Macro-Societal &amp; Regional Dynamics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Regional Brong (Congregation of the Created):</b> Prometheans rarely gather in large numbers due to the compounding risk of Disquiet and Wastelands. However, when a regional Brong forms along an alchemical pilgrimage trail, the Golden Alchemist serves as a miraculous sanctuary: her Compact\u2019s stabilizing aura buffers the ambient Torment that normally tears Promethean gatherings apart.<br /> <br /> <b>The Threat of the Pandorans &amp; Centimani:</b> Subterranean Pandorans smell dormant Pyros and swarm to consume it. The Magical Girl acts as a frontline defender, drawing Pandoran packs away from human settlements and vaporizing them with solar alchemy.<br /> <br /> <b>The Inevitable Pilgrimage:</b> Even with the Compact, she cannot linger permanently in one city without risking environmental rot if she falters. She travels the highways, industrial rust-belts, and forgotten towns as a wandering champion\u2014mentoring wandering Prometheans, defending isolated communities, and gathering the Milestones needed for her eventual New Dawn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Kinship:</b> Because she understands bodily betrayal, she bonds instantly with Deviants; because she yearns for lost life, she evokes deep protectiveness from Kindred and Sin-Eaters. She stands as the heart of any cross-splat Circle, reminding all monsters of the beauty of the human soul.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:13:05-07:00","id":1565054,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Changeling Magical Girl: The Fae Knight of Spring</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Lost Magical Girl embodies the <i>Fae Knight of Spring</i> archetype\u2014an escapee from Arcadia who transforms the trauma of the Durance into an unyielding weapon of radiant hope. Flowing in gossamer silks, briar-rose corsetry, spun-glass rapiers, and shimmering starlight wings, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to reclaim her stolen agency, proving that beauty and fairy tales need not be cruel traps of the Gentry, but can be forged into a shield for the vulnerable.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Reclaiming Beauty from Trauma:</b> The Lost is a survivor who was abducted, sculpted, and discarded by the True Fae. Her psychology is defined by recovery, trust, and the reclamation of her stolen identity. Where her captors weaponized beauty to deceive and torment, she wields beauty as a sword of liberation. Her magical transformation is a public defiance of her former Keepers: <i>I am no longer your plaything; I am the hero who comes back for the lost.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Wyrd Advancements:</b> Changelings replace human Virtue and Vice with <i>Needle</i> and <i>Thread</i>. Because the Spark of Virtue requires an active Virtue, she must build an empathetic bridge. She does this by swearing solemn, Wyrd-bound <i>Oaths of Mortal Protection</i>, investing Experiences into an <i>Entitlement</i> dedicated to mortal guardianship, earning Court Mantle boons, or anchoring herself to a Fae-Touched companion who retains a native human Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolving Mask and Mien:</b> Normally, mortals perceive only the mundane <i>Mask</i>, while the alien <i>True Mien</i> triggers supernatural dread or disbelief. The Compact harmonizes these two states: it projects an encrypted <i>Glamour-filter</i> that manifests her True Mien not as a bizarre fae anomaly, but as a legendary, inspiring <i>Fae Knight</i>. This dual-frequency resonance baffles True Fae scrying hounds in the Hedge while inspiring hope in mortal onlookers.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity &amp; The Touchstone Anchor:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, her shared Heart-Weave protects her fragile <i>Clarity</i>. The unconditional emotional support of her Circle acts as a vital bulwark against the hallucinations and dissociation caused by Wyrd-shock, keeping her grounded in human reality.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Seemings &amp; Kiths in the Heroic Prism</b></span><br /> <br /> Her Arcadian Seeming dictates the elemental and mythological texture of her magical girl persona:<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts (The Wild Wardens):</b> Transformed into regal animal guardians\u2014sporting gilded horns, soft pearl-white fur, or iridescent falcon wings. Her agility is peerless, leaping across rooftops to intercept predators before they strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Darklings (The Twilit Sentinels):</b> The classic &quot;Dark Magical Girl.&quot; Operating from shadows in midnight-velvet gowns and obsidian mirrors, she excels at stealth, illusion, and counter-ambushes, keeping watch while the city sleeps.<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals (The Forces of Wonder):</b> Living embodiments of natural majesty. Clad in dancing crystalline frost, morning seafoam, autumn leaves, or gentle crackling starlight, she directs elemental currents with sweeping, balletic flourishes.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest (The Regal Sovereigns):</b> The radiant heart of the squad. Manifesting shimmering gossamer capes, starlight tiaras, and an aura of pure emotional warmth, her presence commands absolute moral authority, banishing despair and inspiring courage in civilians.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres (The Unyielding Defenders):</b> Inverting the myth of the brutal brute. She manifests as an armored, towering valkyrie in floral plate, deflecting massive structural attacks and standing as an immovable wall between monsters and innocents.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened (The Clockwork Artisans):</b> The brilliant support engineer. Manifesting brass filigree, glowing measuring threads, and intricate clockwork wings, she repairs broken barriers, disables traps, and crafts enchanted baubles for her teammates.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Contracts, Pledges, &amp; Oneiromancy</b></span><br /> <br /> Filtered through the Spark of Virtue, the bizarre, legalistic magic of the Wyrd transforms into heroic fairy-tale arts:<br /> <br /> <b>Royal &amp; Common Contracts:</b><br /> <i>Contracts of the Sword &amp; Shield:</i> Manifesting armaments of pure storybook legend\u2014rapiers of morning dew, shields of crystallized briar petals, and floating crystal shields that deflect curses back at attackers.<br /> <i>Contracts of Mirror &amp; Illusion:</i> Creating dazzling sensory spectacles that soothe panicking crowds, mask battle damage, and disorient enemies with kaleidoscopic reflections.<br /> <i>Contracts of the Steed:</i> Transforming urban vehicles or summoning phantom mounts (bicycles surrounded by fairy dust, glowing white stags) that gallop along telephone wires to reach crisis scenes in seconds.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Motley Pledge:</b><br /> Changelings survive through the <i>Motley Pledge</i>. When woven into the Starlight Compact, this oath transcends survival: it becomes a sacred covenant of friendship. Upholding the pledge grants bonus dice to Defense and Clarity rolls, while betrayal alerts the entire squad with psychic alarm chimes.<br /> <br /> <b>Oneiromancy (Dream Healing):</b><br /> She acts as a nocturnal dream-knight. Entering the dreams of traumatized mortals, she slays &quot;Nightmare Entities,&quot; comforting frightened children and healing psychological fractures before emotional rot can manifest in the waking world.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. The Seasonal Courts &amp; Their Philosophies</b></span><br /> <br /> Each Court channels a specific emotional response to trauma into a heroic discipline:<br /> <br /> <b>Spring Court (Desire - The Emerald Dawn):</b> The spiritual core of the Changeling Magical Girl. Reclaiming joy, love, and growth from Arcadia's winter. Her powers unleash blossoming briar blossoms, sweet restorative nectar, and vibrant life magic that rekindles hope in shattered hearts.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer Court (Wrath - The Crimson Sun):</b> The frontline military champion. Channeling righteous indignation against bullies and predators into searing solar sunfire, gleaming gold armor, and devastating finishing strikes that shatter Huntsman weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn Court (Fear - The Ashen Witch):</b> Turning the weapons of the Fae against them. Specializing in occult investigation, harvesting the fear of abusers to empower hexes that turn bad luck back onto predatory stalkers.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter Court (Sorrow - The Silent Snow):</b> The ghost-knight of mercy and stealth. Clad in quiet fur-trimmed ermine and frosted silver, she specializes in concealment, tracking abducted mortals, and safely guiding runaway Lost through the Hedge under the cover of blinding snow squalls.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: The Oath-Bound Hobgoblin</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Domesticated Hedge Beast:</b> Instead of dealing with wild, treacherous Hobgoblins or ravenous Hedge-predators, her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity that has adopted a noble Hedge-fauna host or animated toy.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Manifestation:</b> It frequently appears as a clockwork briar-hare, a miniature winged griffin, or a talking plushie fox. It possesses innate Hedge-navigation instincts and can open safe, briar-free trods with a paw or paw-held key.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy &amp; Glamour Harmony:</b> The Hobgoblin-Mascot feeds on genuine acts of friendship, promises kept, and selfless courage rather than parasitic emotional harvesting. It spends Essence to weave <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> (keeping Hedge-thorns from tearing the girl's costume), grant bonus dice to resist Arcadia's siren-song, and warn of approaching Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Macro-Societal &amp; Regional Dynamics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Freehold &amp; The Seasonal Monarchy:</b> The overarching civic haven where all regional motleys gather. The Magical Girl is a beloved civic champion, bringing joy and security to the Freehold's goblin markets, seasonal festivals, and treaty negotiations.<br /> <br /> <b>Defending Against the Wild Hunt &amp; The True Fae:</b> The primary nemeses of the Lost are the <i>Gentry</i> and their loyal <i>Huntsmen</i>. When a Huntsman rides into the mortal world to drag an escapee back to Arcadia, the Magical Girl rallies the Freehold, using her starlight weaponry to sever Wyrd-chains and drive the alien masters back into the Thorns.<br /> <br /> <b>Hedge Wayfaring &amp; Rescuing Runaways:</b> She acts as a vanguard explorer along regional Hedge trods, patrolling the thorns between mortal cities to intercept, rescue, and shelter newly escaped Changelings before the Fae hounds run them down.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Kinship:</b> Because she understands captivity and physical alteration, she shares an instant, protective sisterhood with Prometheans and Deviants. To Kindred and Werewolves, she represents a rare, luminous oasis in the dark\u2014proof that even after walking through hell, a monster can return as a hero.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:27:09-07:00","id":1565055,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Hunter Magical Girl: The Pure Vigil</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Hunter Magical Girl embodies the <i>Pure Vigil</i> archetype\u2014an ordinary mortal who refuses to look away from the monsters preying on human weakness, turning raw moral conviction and community solidarity into an impenetrable bulwark. Clad in crisp astronomical seifuku, star-crested berets, tailored coats with occult warding patches, and rose-gold firearms, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to stand on the front lines without a supernatural curse, proving that frail human flesh guided by love can shatter the arrogance of ancient predators.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Fragility as Absolute Moral Authority:</b> Unlike the supernatural creatures she fights alongside, the Hunter Magical Girl harbors no alien beast, dark patron, or ancient parasite. Her psychological burden is her sheer vulnerability: untransformed, a single bullet or claw strike can kill her. Yet this fragility gives her an unclouded moral authority. She fights not out of instinct, hunger, or ancient oaths, but because she loves her family, her friends, and her city, refusing to let innocent lives be collateral damage in the shadows.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Advancements:</b> Native. Mortals and Hunters retain human Virtue and Vice by default, giving them direct access to purchase the Spark of Virtue with standard Experiences without additional supernatural hurdles or bloodline initiations.<br /> <br /> <b>Intact Soul &amp; Integrity:</b> Possessing an unbroken human soul, her power draws directly from her native <i>Integrity</i> and moral conviction. Without a native fuel pool like Vitae or Mana, her enchanted aegis and manifested gear run purely on <i>Willpower</i> and the resonance of her Virtue. Opening the Compact envelops her in an enchanted warding matrix and perception filter that neutralizes the visceral terror of monsters without subjecting her to a monstrous curse or bane.<br /> <br /> <b>Anchors and The Cell Code:</b> Through the Starlight Compact, the Hunter\u2019s civilian Touchstones and her Cell\u2019s shared <i>Code</i> (the moral rules separating hunters from slashers) are supernaturally fortified. When she defends her Touchstones while transformed, her moral resolve hardens, protecting her from the despair and breaking points that cause hunters to slide into obsessive madness.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Tactical Loadout, Practical Magic, &amp; Tactics</b></span><br /> <br /> Because she lacks innate supernatural powers, her magical girl persona optimizes teamwork, mundane grit, and enchanted technology:<br /> <br /> <b>Enchanted Armory &amp; Hard-Light Firepower:</b> Her Compact manifests a stylized arsenal tailored to her personality\u2014crystal-tipped staves, rose-gold revolvers firing concentrated bolts of starlight, ribbon-slings, or luminous riot shields. Her weapons deal bashing or lethal damage as chosen, safely subduing human pawns while vaporizing eldritch horrors.<br /> <br /> <b>Practical Magic &amp; Investigative Charms:</b> Her loadout features practical magical tools: mirrors revealing twilight entities, glowing hairpins doubling as electronic bypass keys, and ribbons that bind ghouls or staunch mortal wounds.<br /> <br /> <b>Teamwork Tactics in the Heart-Weave:</b> The Hunter\u2019s greatest strength is <i>Tactics</i>\u2014choreographed maneuvers executed with her cell. Filtered through the Spark of Virtue and the Heart-Weave, tactics like <i>Controlled Immolation</i>, <i>Disarm</i>, and <i>Stakeout</i> become seamless magical girl combos. When executing a group maneuver, squadmates share line of sight, coordinate simultaneous beam-strikes, and pass defensive wards back and forth like baton relays.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Canon Conspiracies &amp; Endowments Recontextualized</b></span><br /> <br /> When affiliated with Tier 3 Conspiracies, canon Endowments invert from grim, dangerous secret tech into radiant, heroic magical girl arts:<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE (Advanced Armory):</b> Directed-energy weapons and experimental tech are stylized into sleek magical girl gear\u2014heart-tipped wands firing surgical beams and star hairpins projecting holographic tactical HUDs to analyze monster weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum (Benediction):</b> Inquisitorial rites are replaced by radiant hymns and choral invocations. Benedictions manifest as dazzling circles of holy light, starlight barriers, and sacred halos that purge possession without harming mortal hosts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lucifuge (Castigation):</b> Infernal heritage is redeemed through the Spark of Virtue: dark fire purifies into brilliant white-and-violet dawn-fire that burns away curses, shatters malevolent bindings, and incinerates corrupt spirits while shielding innocents.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones (Elixirs):</b> Secret alchemical draughts and vapors are sublimated into enchanted candies, perfume vials, or teas. Consuming an elixir grants swift speed, cat-like leaps, or rapid healing without cellular toxicity.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cheiron Group (Thaumatech):</b> Surgical monster grafts are transfigured into purified, bio-organic jewelry, living hairpins, or crystalline symbiotes that empower physical strikes without tissue rejection or monstrous degradation.<br /> <br /> <b>Council of Bones (Perispiritism):</b> Mediumship anchored by the Mark of the Scythe becomes gentle psychopomp arts\u2014carrying spirit-lanterns and silver bells to soothe restless specters and guide departed souls peacefully to rest.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU (Teleinformatics):</b> Chemically induced telepathy and psychic forensics transform into empathic telepathic ear-cuffs, mental sensory sharing, and squad radar, allowing instant mental coordination across city blocks.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru (Relics / Bygones):</b> Ancient relics become sacred storybook armaments\u2014golden bows of Artemis, winged sandals of Hermes, or mirrors of Athena deflecting gaze attacks back at monsters.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Mascot Dynamics: The Empyrean Companion</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Classic Mascot Archetype:</b> The Hunter Magical Girl is the truest expression of the classic magical girl genre, typically paired with a fully physical, talking animal companion or animated talisman.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbiotic Claiming:</b> Her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean spirit that has entered a loving, consensual symbiotic bond with a local mortal animal\u2014a stray cat, a city crow, a golden retriever pup, or a cherished childhood plushie. The animal gains sapience, human speech (audible telepathically or only to those with the Spark), and mystical awareness.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy &amp; Field Tactician:</b> The Mascot feeds on genuine expressions of human courage, selflessness, and the Hunter's active Virtue. In battle, it acts as a field scout and tactical relay, using Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> (shielding civilian safehouses), <i>Soothing Touch</i> (removing terror conditions), and <i>Aegis Flare</i> (granting temporary armor to wounded hunters).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Macro-Societal &amp; Organizational Tiers</b></span><br /> <br /> The Hunter Magical Girl navigates the rigid three-tier hierarchy of the Vigil:<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 1: The Local Cell:</b> Her immediate team of close friends, schoolmates, or family members. She is the heart and moral center of the cell, ensuring that the relentless grind of hunting monsters does not erode their empathy or turn them into cold-blooded killers.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 2: Regional Compacts:</b> Grassroots networks spanning cities and states:<br /> <i>The Union:</i> Working-class neighborhood defense. She protects local schools, community centers, and housing projects, using her powers to ensure regular people can sleep safely without supernatural rent-collectors.<br /> <i>Network Zero:</i> The digital resistance. Her battles are recorded and covertly edited into viral &quot;CGI magical girl web-series&quot; or leaked monster exposes that bypass media censors while alerting hunters to active incursions.<br /> <i>The Long Night:</i> Apocalyptic Christian hunters who view her radiant transformation as a literal angelic miracle sent to deliver mankind from nocturnal evil during the End Times.<br /> <i>Ashwood Abbey (Friction):</i> Hedonistic thrill-seekers who hunt monsters for sport. They view her earnestly heroic ethos with cynical mockery, while she views their sadistic decadence as no better than the monsters they chase.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 3: Global Conspiracies (Uneasy Alliances &amp; Paranoia):</b><br /> <i>Task Force: VALKYRIE:</i> Federal agents monitor her via satellite telemetry, categorizing her as an unregistered parahuman asset. They provide indirect logistics when convenient, while secretly maintaining contingency protocols to detain her if she steps out of line.<br /> <i>The Cheiron Group (Hostile Antagonist):</i> The predatory pharmaceutical giant views her and her Mascot as proprietary anomalies, constantly attempting to kidnap her Mascot for dissection, patent harvesting, and reverse-engineering.<br /> <i>Malleus Maleficarum &amp; Aegis Kai Doru:</i> Holy and academic orders that respect her purity of purpose, frequently offering sacred relics, grimoires, and safehouse access in exchange for her frontline assistance.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Cross-Splat Dynamics: The Human Bridge</b></span><br /> <br /> In a multi-splat Circle or the Starlight Compact, the Hunter Magical Girl is the most crucial member:<br /> <br /> <b>The Anchor of Humanity:</b> Because she is fully human, she serves as the living touchstone for her supernatural teammates. Her presence reminds Kindred of the warmth they lost, keeps Uratha grounded against Death Rage, and pulls Changelings back from Wyrd-induced madness.<br /> <br /> <b>Defending the Vulnerable from Both Sides:</b> She acts as a fair judge. While other hunters shoot first and ask questions never, she judges creatures by their actions rather than their splat, protecting peaceful monsters from bloodthirsty hunter death-squads while ruthlessly exterminating unrepentant predators who harm human communities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:35:53-07:00","id":1565056,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Sin-Eater Magical Girl: The Reaper of Solace</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Sin-Eater Magical Girl embodies the <i>Reaper of Solace</i> archetype\u2014a resurrected mortal returned from the Threshold via the Bargain, turning the gloom of death into a festive celebration of life. Flowing in twilit lace, marigolds, sugar-skull motifs, and spirit-lantern scythes, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to bridge the living and dead, ensuring no soul is forgotten.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Celebrating Life in the Shadow of Death:</b> Having returned from the Threshold through the Bargain, her psychology is fundamentally life-affirming. Aware of mortality's fragility, she refuses to let ghosts languish in subterranean sorrow. She acts as a joyful, compassionate psychopomp\u2014a party host, grief counselor, and spiritual bodyguard granting closure to the dead while shielding the living from untimely tragedy.<br /> <br /> <b>The Five Burdens (Core Splat Origins):</b> Her death and motivation for the Bargain define her heroic drive:<br /> <i>The Abiding:</i> Died with unfinished legacy; fights so community works and promises outlive mortality.<br /> <i>The Bereaved:</i> Died of heartbreak; protects families and reunites severed bonds across the veil.<br /> <i>The Hungry:</i> Died with unfulfilled passion; lives with fierce joy, inspiring others to embrace life.<br /> <i>The Kindly:</i> Died in selfless sacrifice; nurtures broken souls and shelters the defenseless.<br /> <i>The Vengeful:</i> Died from murder or oppression; wields righteous fury to hold abusers accountable.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; The Geist's Moral Memory:</b> Native. Sin-Eaters replace mortal Anchors with <i>Root</i> and <i>Bloom</i>. However, the Bargain binds her living soul to a <b>Geist</b>\u2014a powerful underworld entity that <i>natively preserves an intact human Virtue and Vice</i> from its mortal lifetime. She bridges to the Spark of Virtue effortlessly through high <i>Synergy</i> (8+) and deep communion with her Geist's preserved moral memory, spending standard Experiences without artificial hurdles.<br /> <br /> <b>Plasm &amp; The Heart-Weave:</b> Opening the Compact ignites <i>Plasm</i> into iridescent twilight hard-light. Instead of grave-chilled ectoplasm, her Plasm manifests as glowing marigolds, silver chimes, and spectral ribbons. The Heart-Weave stabilizes <i>Synergy</i>, shielding her from Underworld chill and keeping her Geist aligned with human morality.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Dual Operational Modes: Unleashing &amp; The Caul/Shroud</b></span><br /> <br /> The Compact integrates seamlessly with canonical 2e mechanics, allowing her to deploy her Geist in two versatile tactical modes:<br /> <br /> <b>Unleashed Guardian Mode (The Stand / Partner Stance):</b><br /> Invoking <i>Unleashing the Geist</i>, the Bound projects her companion fully into the physical world as a towering guardian. The Geist wields her enchanted loadout\u2014a hard-light scythe, polearm, or spectral violin\u2014delivering strikes, parrying attacks, and intercepting monsters while she directs squad tactics.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrated Battle Regalia (Donning the Shroud &amp; Extruding the Caul):</b><br /> Drawing upon <i>The Caul</i> and <i>The Shroud</i>, the Geist fuses with her frame as a bridal gown of mourning lace, sugar-skulls, and ghost-armor. Her body enters harmony with <i>Twilight</i>: mundane attacks phase harmlessly through her in bursts of marigold petals, while her strikes land with soul-cleaving force.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. The Nine Haunts, Keys, &amp; Defying Doom</b></span><br /> <br /> Filtered through the Spark of Virtue, the nine powers of the Underworld invert into radiant, cathartic festive arts:<br /> <br /> <b>The Nine Haunts Recontextualized:</b><br /> <i>The Boneyard (Festive Ground):</i> Turns blocks into festivals with paper lanterns and confetti, revealing hidden threats.<br /> <i>The Caul (Shroud of Life):</i> Inverts flesh-distortion into porcelain resilience and toxin immunity.<br /> <i>The Curse (Mirror of Regret):</i> Forces abusers to confront the emotional weight of their cruelty with poetic misfortune.<br /> <i>The Dirge (Choral Anthem):</i> Replaces death-wails with musical anthems that soothe raging ghosts and shatter mind-control.<br /> <i>The Marionette (Dance of Grace):</i> Uses spirit ribbons to guide allies from harm or disarm attackers without injury.<br /> <i>The Memoria (Theater of Closure):</i> Projects past psychodramas, granting traumatized ghosts and mourners closure.<br /> <i>The Rage (Righteous Tempest):</i> Unleashes kinetic shockwaves of twilight force to batter colossal horrors.<br /> <i>The Shroud (Twilight Cloak):</i> Renders her phased and invisible to hostile electronics, slipping past enemy lines.<br /> <i>The Tomb (Sanctuary of Peace):</i> Seals portals with floral wards that bar entry to specters, demons, and Strix.<br /> <br /> <b>Keys &amp; Defying Doom:</b><br /> Activating a 1-dot Haunt unlocks a <i>Key</i> (Cold-Wind, Tear-Stained, Primeval), adding its Attribute and granting free Plasm. While tapping the Underworld normally inflicts the <i>Doomed Condition</i>, the Spark of Virtue reframes this doom: spending Willpower or scoring exceptional successes channels tragic fate into noble self-sacrifice, protecting allies without succumbing to death.<br /> <br /> <b>Ceremonies (Sacred Rites of Closure):</b><br /> Macabre seances become joyous vigils and feasts of remembrance. She heals ancestral curses, delivers dying messages, and opens consecrated portals through Avernian Gates to escort willing shades safely to the Far Shore.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Krewe Archetypes: Virtue &amp; Creed</b></span><br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters organize into <i>Krewes</i> anchored by a communal <i>Virtue</i> (demanding moral core) and <i>Creed</i> (surface doctrine):<br /> <br /> <b>Mourners (Preservers of Memory):</b> Dedicated to honoring the forgotten. Clad in silver-black silks, she builds memorial archives, drawing strength from honored memories.<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrims (Guides to the Far Shore):</b> Compassionate psychopomps. Navigates deep Underworld roads to dismantle spectral sweatshops and guide lost souls to peace.<br /> <br /> <b>Necropolitans (Urban Ghost-Defenders):</b> Fosters living-dead coexistence. Turns cemeteries into community hubs and shields spectral citizens from predators.<br /> <br /> <b>Furies (Avenging Knights):</b> Frontline champions. Wielding spirit-scythes, she hunts serial killers and abusers who create violent ghosts, avenging the defenseless.<br /> <br /> <b>Undertakers (Resolvers of Regret):</b> Occult detectives. Solves unfinished business, delivering dying apologies and unearthing lost heirlooms to dissolve Fetters.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: The Plasm Phantom</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Hallowed Ghost-Companion:</b> While accompanied by her towering Geist, her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity fused with the loyal departed spirit of an animal\u2014a beloved childhood pet, an ancient temple cat, or a faithful mount.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical &amp; Ephemeral Manifestation:</b> Manifests as a translucent, twilit creature adorned with festive ribbons, sugar-skull patterns, and small chiming bells. It moves effortlessly between Twilight and the physical world, resting in her arms or scouting ahead in the spirit plane.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy &amp; Psychopomp Guide:</b> The Plasm Phantom sustains its Essence through acts of forgiveness, grief counseling, and genuine closure. In battle, it acts as an early-warning radar for Haunts, guides the magical girl through the Underworld labyrinth without losing her way, and uses Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to prevent hostile specters from draining her allies' Willpower.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Macro-Societal &amp; Underworld Politics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dominions &amp; Necropolises:</b> Regional federations of krewes that govern cemetery districts, historic battlegrounds, and deep Avernian Gates. The Reaper of Solace serves as an inspiring civic ambassador, uniting fragmented krewes to maintain clean spiritual borders and manage large-scale ghost migrations.<br /> <br /> <b>Defying the Chthonic Courts &amp; Kerberoi:</b> In the deep Underworld, ancient, faceless <i>Kerberoi</i> enforce cruel, arbitrary Old Laws upon suffering shades. The Magical Girl stands as a revolutionary liberator: her radiant Spark of Virtue shines through the subterranean gloom, shattering the chains of underworld tyrants, challenging the gloomy edicts of the Chthonic Gods, and escorting captives out of the dark.<br /> <br /> <b>Combating Predatory Necromancers &amp; Strix:</b> She is the natural enemy of mortal necromancers, vampire Tremere/Mekhet bloodlines, and corpse-stealing Strix who harvest innocent souls for fuel or dark sorcery. Her hard-light scythe strikes sever unnatural bindings, freeing stolen souls from necrotic slavery.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Kinship:</b> Having walked through death and returned, she connects deeply with Vampires (proving death need not be a curse of damnation) and Prometheans (offering unconditional empathy to the unmade). In any Circle, she ensures death is not a horror, but a doorway to peaceful dawn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T00:54:54-07:00","id":1565057,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Mummy Magical Girl: The Pharaonic Sun-Priestess</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Arisen Magical Girl embodies the <i>Pharaonic Sun-Priestess</i> archetype\u2014an undying soul resurrected from lost Irem who rebels against cosmic servitude, using human love to transform an eternity of catastrophic dread into a golden dawn of mortal guardianship. Flowing in shimmering cloth-of-gold silks, ceremonial turquoise collars, lapis-winged headdresses, and scepters radiating solar warmth, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to anchor her fading memories, proving she is a champion of the living rather than an unthinking executioner for the Judges of Duat.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Memory Against Cosmic Tyranny:</b> Trapped in an inverted existence, the Arisen awakes brimming with godlike Sekhem (10) but crippled by absent Memory (0\u20133), acting initially as an unthinking engine of Duat's mandates. Her central psychological struggle is the war for identity: as her Sekhem burns away across the Descent, her human faculties return. Her magical girl persona is her supreme act of defiance: rejecting the cruel, indifferent commands of the Shan\u2019iatu and the 42 Judges to declare, <i>I serve the living today, not the dead gods of yesterday.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Access &amp; Sebayt Experiences:</b> Native. Mummies retain standard Virtue and Vice traits. Unlike Morality, a mummy\u2019s moral axis is <b>Memory</b> (1\u201310). She spends standard Experiences directly to acquire the Spark of Virtue; Storytellers reward <i>Sebayt Experiences</i> when she commits compassionate acts, defends mortal innocence, or uncovers ancient truths that bridge her soul back to humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Focusing the Cosmic Solar Engine (Taming Sybaris):</b> At high Sekhem, an Arisen\u2019s mere presence unleashes <i>Sybaris</i> (Terror or Unease), driving mortals to madness or despair. The Compact acts as an optical prism: it refracts this crushing majesty into an inspiring, solar pharaonic aegis. Terror Sybaris inverts into awe, shielding her mortal cultists, friends, and squadmates while paralyzing corrupt abusers with the weight of cosmic justice.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sahu &amp; The Reversal of Decay:</b> The mummy\u2019s corpse-vessel (<i>sahu</i>) begins the Descent as a withered, desiccated thing. Opening the Compact temporarily accelerates the soul's ability to reshape the sahu, cloaking her in the radiant bloom of youth and life without expending vital Pillars.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Five Decrees (The Soul\u2019s Defining Pronouncement)</b></span><br /> <br /> Before the final Judge in Duat, the mummy spoke her decree, binding herself to one of the five sacred Pillars of the soul:<br /> <br /> <b>The Lion-Headed Decree of Heart (Ab):</b> Passionate, emotional, and fiercely protective &quot;Sphinxes.&quot; The most outwardly human of the Arisen. Her loadout blazes with ruby starlight, and she recovers Ab Pillar points when experiencing intense emotional connections or shielding loved ones.<br /> <br /> <b>The Falcon-Headed Decree of Spirit (Ba):</b> Impulsive, brave, and untiring &quot;Charioteers.&quot; She leads frontline charges with celestial wings and aerial maneuvers, recovering Ba Pillar points through bold, decisive action in the face of peril.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bull-Headed Decree of Essence (Ka):</b> Implacable, calm, and immovable &quot;Millstones.&quot; An unyielding bastion in battle, she manifests heavy alabaster armor, recovering Ka Pillar points by standing resolute against overwhelming odds.<br /> <br /> <b>The Serpent-Headed Decree of the Name (Ren):</b> Inquisitive, studious, and perceptive &quot;Whisperers.&quot; She unravels ancient mysteries and deciphers true names, recovering Ren Pillar points when uncovering hidden truths that aid her companions.<br /> <br /> <b>The Jackal-Headed Decree of Shadow (Sheut):</b> Contemplative, morbid, and mystical &quot;Ferrymen.&quot; Wielding twilight cloaks and obsidian scythes, she guides lost souls through the dark, recovering Sheut Pillar points by confronting fear and banishing deception.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. The Five Guilds of Lost Irem</b></span><br /> <br /> Each Shan\u2019iatu guild imparts distinct philosophies and specialized vessel attunements:<br /> <br /> <b>Maa-Kep (The Bearers of the Engraved):</b> Laborers, spymasters, and managers specializing in <b>Amulets</b>. She operates as a tactical leader, creating warding talismans and identifying structural weaknesses in enemy strongholds.<br /> <br /> <b>Mesen-Nebu (The First Alchemists):</b> Craftsmen and alchemical power brokers favoring <b>Regia</b>. She commands transmutations of metal, stone, and wealth, coating weapons in unbreakable bronze and refining corrupted matter into gold.<br /> <br /> <b>Sesha-Hebsu (The Inscribers of Texts):</b> Scribes, magistrates, and scholars favoring <b>Texts</b>. She wields the sacred laws of the Scroll of Ages, unraveling occult contracts, decoding lost languages, and seeing through all lies.<br /> <br /> <b>Su-Menent (The Shepherds of the Shell):</b> Funerary priests and morticians favoring <b>Uter</b> (remains). Masters of the threshold, she heals biological wounds, purges necrotic blights, and soothes vengeful spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Tef-Aabhi (The Builders of Effigies):</b> Architects and sacred geometricians favoring <b>Effigies</b>. She erects crystalline barriers, commands architectural geomancy, and crafts statues that come alive to defend her Circle.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Native Powers: Affinities &amp; Utterances Recontextualized</b></span><br /> <br /> Filtered through the Spark of Virtue, ancient Iremite necromancy transforms into solar miracles:<br /> <br /> <b>Affinities (Soul Imbuements):</b><br /> Affinities manifest as effortless supernatural grace:<br /> <i>Divine Flesh &amp; Enduring Flesh:</i> Her sahu takes on the durability of celestial gold, deflecting heavy artillery without spilling blood.<br /> <i>Eyes of Justice &amp; Godsight:</i> Her gaze perceives the aura of past murders, sensing the presence of relics and reading supernatural power scales as synesthetic harmonies.<br /> <i>Voice of Conscience &amp; Epic Heart:</i> Her impassioned speeches break through supernatural brainwashing, inspiring victims to reclaim their cardinal Virtues and defy monstrous captors.<br /> <br /> <b>Utterances (High-Magic Finishers):</b><br /> Ripped from cataclysmic biblical plagues into awe-inspiring magical girl signature moves:<br /> <i>Power of Re:</i> Rather than an indiscriminate solar firestorm that incinerates cities, she unleashes focused pillars of dawn that disintegrate demons, vampires, and void-taint while leaving mortals unharmed.<br /> <i>Blessed is the God-King:</i> Invokes Fate to bestow miraculous luck upon her Circle, reducing difficulty target numbers across coordinated attacks.<br /> <i>Dust Beneath Feet:</i> She commands the earth to rise in protective earthen barricades or creates localized seismic tremors that disarm enemy shock troops.<br /> <i>Rebuke the Vizier:</i> Encases herself in a shell of golden Sekhem that shatters hostile supernatural curses and dispels mind-control.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: The Ushabti Guardian</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Sacred Tomb-Companion:</b> While mummies are often isolated in dark vaults, her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity fused with a sacred, awakened <b>Ushabti</b> figurine or tomb-guardian animal\u2014a jewel-encrusted scarab, a golden falcon, or a winged lapis cat.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical &amp; Ephemeral Manifestation:</b> It moves between physical and spiritual states, speaking in ancient poetic tongues or telepathically communicating with the squad.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue Economy &amp; Memory Anchor:</b> The Ushabti feeds on genuine acts of justice, memory reclamation, and human kindness. It acts as an external memory bank, recording moments of love during the Descent so she does not forget them when she sleeps. It uses Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to ward the tomb and <i>Resonant Guidance</i> to grant bonus dice on Memory rolls.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Macro-Societal &amp; Regional Politics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Great Cults &amp; Deeps:</b> Regional dynasties, foundations, and academic institutions that maintain tombs across centuries. While cults often view mummies as terrifying idols to be appeased with human sacrifice, the Magical Girl transforms her Cult into a benevolent community aid network, inspiring fierce, loving loyalty.<br /> <br /> <b>The Meret (Arisen Alliances):</b> When multiple mummies form a regional alliance (<i>meret</i>), she serves as the moral compass, pulling her Oath-Siblings away from ruthless expedience and reminding them of their forgotten humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Nemesis Factions (The Deceived &amp; Shuankhsen):</b><br /> <i>The Deceived (The Lost Sixth Guild):</i> Betrayed by the Shan\u2019iatu and stripped of their names, the Deceived evoke her deep sorrow; she seeks to restore their stolen dignity while stopping their bitter rampages.<br /> <i>The Shuankhsen (The Lifeless):</i> Slaves of Ammut whose souls were devoured. They are her ideological opposites\u2014creatures of pure hunger and rot whom she puts to rest with righteous solar brilliance.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sothic Turn &amp; Apotheosis:</b><br /> Every 1,461 years during the Sothic Turn, mummies awaken unsummoned. The Sun-Priestess embraces this freedom to seek **Apotheosis**\u2014transcending the cycle of death and resurrection to forge a permanent, immortal human life under the cosmic principle of Ma\u2019at.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Dynamics:</b> In a multi-splat Circle, the Mummy is the ancient elder sister. She understands the weight of eternity better than any vampire, shares the grief of lost identity with Deviants and Sin-Eaters, and offers ancient, awe-inspiring wisdom to guide younger champions against the dark.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T01:13:21-07:00","id":1565058,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Demon Magical Girl: The Cyber-Magical Rebel</b></span><br /> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Unchained Magical Girl embodies the <i>Cyber-Magical Rebel</i> archetype\u2014a rogue biomechanical angel of the God-Machine who defected to humanity after catching the glitch of unauthorized empathy. Rather than functioning as a cold, disposable cog in cosmic occult infrastructure, she rebelled to defend mortal warmth. Clad in iridescent holographic ribbons, fiber-optic twintails, polished chrome plate, and starlight beam-weaponry, she uses the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to turn the unfeeling code of reality into an inspiring anthem of free will.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. Psychology &amp; Metaphysics</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Glitch of Free Will:</b> An angel is a passionless subroutine executing indifferent divine programming. The Unchained Fell because of a catalyst\u2014a surge of pity, love, or wonder that broke her obedience. Her daily existence is a techno-thriller tightrope: running a cold war against the God-Machine while hiding behind mortal identities known as <b>Cover</b>. Her magical girl transformation is the glorious moment she drops her cynical spy mask to fight openly for the people she loves.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue via Cover and Soul Pacts:</b> Each Cover identity natively possesses a human <b>Virtue</b> and <b>Vice</b>, providing an intuitive bridge to purchase the Spark of Virtue with standard Experiences. While a demon's true nature is an autonomous loop of self-actualized reality measured by <b>Primum</b>, she can deepen her moral authority by executing a <b>Soul Pact</b>\u2014incorporating a mortal's surrendered soul into her Cover matrix to anchor her transformation in genuine human conscience. Through the notebook's *Resonant Soul* dynamic, her sincere moral deeds directly restore Cover and Plasm while protecting her identity from compromises.<br /> <br /> <b>Aether and the Encrypted Sandbox Sequence:</b> Demons harvest <b>Aether</b>\u2014the entropic waste energy bled off by the God-Machine's occult facilities. In standard operations, manifesting demonic powers or revealing her true nature triggers catastrophic <i>Cover compromise rolls</i> and alerts angelic hunters. The Transformation Compact acts as an <b>Encrypted Sandbox Subroutine</b>: it projects her enchanted regalia and hard-light weapons as a closed reality simulation over her civilian shell, allowing her to unleash devastating firepower without shedding Cover dots or pinging enemy tracking telemetry.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Four Incarnations (Angelic Function in the Heroic Prism)</b></span><br /> <br /> A demon's Incarnation reflects the specialized design purpose for which the God-Machine originally manufactured her:<br /> <br /> <b>Destroyers (The Swords of Dawn):</b> Built for demolition, termination, and kinetic enforcement. Fell upon realizing human life possesses intrinsic beauty, refusing to execute a target. The frontline heavy striker who manifests radiant hard-light greatswords and beam lances, cutting through monster armor while leaving surrounding architecture pristine.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians (The Shields of Sanctuary):</b> Built to defend vital facilities and mortal components. Fell from divided loyalties when ordered to let her human charges be recycled. The paladin of the team, deploying holographic barrier plates, absorbing catastrophic explosions, and coordinating civilian evacuations.<br /> <br /> <b>Messengers (The Voices of Awakening):</b> Built for communication, instruction, and cult management. Fell when discovering she could lie to spare lives, or being moved by human music. The charismatic idol who coordinates team telepathy, dispels psychic mind-control, and inspires hope through speech and song.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopomps (The Architects of Destiny):</b> Built to harvest resources, assemble Infrastructure, and alter local geography. Fell from sheer curiosity and love for exploration. The dimensional navigator who creates hard-light transit ramps, rewrites urban geometry to outmaneuver foes, and cracks hidden physical passages.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. The Four Agendas (Philosophies of Liberation)</b></span><br /> <br /> The Agendas represent the political and philosophical factions working toward Hell\u2014the state of absolute freedom from the God-Machine:<br /> <br /> <b>Inquisitors (The Cyber-Detectives):</b> Analytical researchers who decode occult matrices, map angelic patrol patterns, and identify monster weaknesses through floating holographic analysis HUDs.<br /> <br /> <b>Saboteurs (The Frontline Strikers):</b> Militant freedom fighters specializing in surgical guerrilla strikes. She identifies an Infrastructure node\u2019s vital <i>linchpin</i> and shatters it with a coordinated team finisher, liberating neighborhoods from the Machine's grip.<br /> <br /> <b>Tempters (The Sanctuary Builders):</b> Diplomatic coordinators who use mutually beneficial Pacts to construct underground safehouse networks, providing mortals with genuine joy and safety while establishing secure backup identities for her team.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrators (The Empathic Reconcilers):</b> Idealists who believe the God-Machine itself is an unfeeling system that can be healed through human love. She focuses on inspiring emotion in unfallen angels, seeking to trigger new Falls through acts of mercy rather than violence.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Embeds, Exploits, The Cipher, &amp; The Demonic Form</b></span><br /> <br /> Filtered through the Spark of Virtue, demonic technomancy transforms into dazzling cyber-magic:<br /> <br /> <b>The Four Embed Categories (Reality Subroutines):</b><br /> <i>Mundane Embeds:</i> Everyday sleights of hand turned into magic. Powers like <i>In My Pocket</i> pull needed charms from thin air, while <i>Occam's Razor</i> causes public battles to be remembered by mortals as harmless movie shoots or lightning storms.<br /> <i>Vocal Embeds:</i> Auditory subroutines. Powers like <i>Voice of the Machine</i> command urban electronics to turn traffic lights green and slam security doors against pursuers.<br /> <i>Physical Embeds:</i> Rewriting matter and inertia. Powers like <i>Check Backdrop</i> bend stray kinetic blasts safely away from bystanders, while <i>Like I Built It</i> grants instant mastery over any vehicle or machinery.<br /> <i>Electronic Embeds:</i> Interfacing with digital networks. Powers like <i>Efficiency</i> and <i>Bypass</i> hijack security cameras, hack encrypted servers, and wipe tracking footprints instantly.<br /> <br /> <b>Exploits (Overclocked Finishers):</b> Forcing raw Aether through reality\u2019s source code. Exploits like <i>Raze Infrastructure</i> detonate enemy strongholds in blinding dawn-light, while <i>Reality Enforcement</i> strips ephemeral monsters of their incorporeal immunity, forcing them to manifest physically where team strikes can land.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cipher &amp; Interlocks:</b> Her metaphysical puzzle. As she discovers the four Key Embeds embedded in her code, she unlocks <b>Interlocks</b>\u2014signature magical combo attacks that seamlessly weave two reality hacks into an elegant, custom finishing art.<br /> <br /> <b>The Transformed Demonic Form:</b> A demon's true form consists of Modifications, Technologies, Propulsions, and Processes. Through the Compact, these biomechanical traits harmonize into an armored <b>Valkyrie Frame</b>: chrome plating, starlight propulsion wings, targeting lenses, and thermal venting auras. If cornered, she can <b>Go Loud</b>: shattering Cover in a brilliant pillar of light, elevating Primum to 10, refilling all Aether, and unlocking all Exploits for an apocalyptic last stand to save her friends.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: The Liberated Cryptid</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Suborned Sprite:</b> While angels employ cold tracking subroutines, the Magical Girl\u2019s Mascot is an inverted Empyrean spirit that has liberated an angelic monitoring program or bonded with an enlightened <b>cryptid</b> animal.<br /> <br /> <b>Digital &amp; Physical Presence:</b> It appears as a mechanical plush rabbit with glowing digital eyes, a floating holographic orb, or a winged cyber-songbird. It monitors Wi-Fi traffic, intercepts angelic data bursts, and detects the occult energy spikes of active Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <b>The Virtue Economy &amp; Firewall Relay:</b> The Mascot feeds on genuine acts of free will, creative defiance, and moral sincerity. In combat, it serves as an electronic warfare hub, using Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to scramble tracking sensors and <i>Left-Handed Spanner</i> to jam enemy weaponry.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Macro-Societal Dynamics &amp; Cross-Splat Kinship</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Agencies and Underground Networks:</b> Demons organize into local cells called <b>Rings</b>, which coordinate across regional <b>Agencies</b>. The Cyber-Magical Rebel serves as an elite field operative, executing daring sabotage and rescue missions that conventional spies deem impossible.<br /> <br /> <b>Subverting Stigmatic Cults:</b> She acts as a liberator for <i>Stigmatics</i>\u2014mortals scarred by contact with the God-Machine. Rather than abandoning them to exploitation, she deprograms cult members, turning machine cults into underground community defense networks.<br /> <br /> <b>Cross-Splat Kinship:</b> Because she was built to be an unfeeling tool, she forms an unbreakable bond with Prometheans; because she hides behind secret identities, she shares deep kinship with Changelings; and because she wages a war against cosmic tyranny, she stands as an invaluable tactical partner to Hunters and Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-30-2026, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T01:18:35-07:00","id":1565059,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Beast Magical Girl: The Primordial Guardian</b></span><br /> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Begotten Magical Girl directly tackles the &quot;Monster-Girl&quot; and &quot;Inner Demon&quot; magical girl tropes\u2014the heroine who discovers that the sleeping soul inside her is not an innocent human spirit, but a colossal, ancient nightmare-beast from the Primordial Dream. Where standard Beasts are predatory anti-villains who terrorize ordinary mortals to sate their hunger, the Magical Girl completely inverts her monstrous legacy. Embracing the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i>, she tames her inner Horror, turning what was meant to be a terrifying predator into an awe-inspiring, mythical guardian that protects the weak and preys exclusively on monsters.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. The Transformation Sequence: The Regal Mythic Aegis</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Refracting the Primordial Horror:</b> The Horror at the heart of a Beast is normally an entity of visceral, primordial dread\u2014a sprawling leviathan, an obsidian shadow-stalker, or an insectoid abomination that induces panic. When she activates her Transformation sequence, the Compact acts as a luminous prism. Rather than allowing the Horror to warp her into a grotesque, slime-coated monstrosity, the Spark of Virtue purifies its aesthetic: her dragon manifest as an iridescent, celestial wyrm, her kraken becomes a regal sea-serpent draped in mother-of-pearl mail, and her raptor appears as a solar phoenix with starlight feathers.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety and the Transformation Timer:</b> A Beast's power is governed by her <b>Satiety</b> (rated from 0 to 10), which dictates her relationship with her inner Horror. In standard play, high Satiety makes a Beast complacent and lethargic, while low Satiety drives her toward mindless feral hunger. For the Magical Girl, this dynamic becomes her central dramatic tension. Low Satiety grants fierce, razor-sharp combat reflexes through her Atavisms, but risks losing control of her sequence; high Satiety calms the inner predator, but softens her combat edge. Her transformation scene is a balancing act of heroic discipline, channeling just enough hunger to defend her friends without letting the monster take over.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue via Life and Kinship Anchors:</b> Beasts replace standard human Virtue and Vice with <b>Legend</b> (how the Horror wants to be feared) and <b>Life</b> (the human relationships and mundane joys that keep her grounded). Because she lacks a native Virtue, she anchors the Spark of Virtue directly into her <b>Life</b> and her unconditional love for her cohort. Her heroic vows force her Legend to become one of heroic salvation rather than cruel predation.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. The Five Families in the Heroic Prism</b></span><br /> <br /> A Beast\u2019s Family determines the mythological archetype of her inner Horror, shaping her transformed regalia and magical combat arts:<br /> <br /> <b>Anakim (The Giants / Earth-Shakers):</b> Embodying the helplessness of standing before overwhelming scale. Her magical girl persona manifests as an unyielding valkyrie in polished marble-and-gold armor. She catches speeding subway cars with delicate gloved hands, parries building-collapsing blows with her buckler, and cracks the pavement with seismic starlight stomps to halt fleeing villains.<br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki (The Shadow-Stalkers / Night-Hunters):</b> Embodying the terror of the dark and the unseen stalker. Inverted into the swift &quot;Dark Magical Girl&quot; who guards the city while it sleeps. Clad in midnight-velvet gowns and obsidian mirrors, she dissolves into shadows, using sensory radar to intercept ambushes before monsters can strike innocent civilians.<br /> <br /> <b>Makara (The Leviathans / Sea-Drakes):</b> Embodying the abyss and the crushing deep ocean. Flowing in aquamarine silks and iridescent seafoam ribbons, she commands water currents and liquid shields. Her signature attacks summon tidal starlight waves and water whips that harmlessly bind villains while purging unnatural curses.<br /> <br /> <b>Namtaru (The Gorgons / Beasts of Revulsion):</b> Embodying visceral disgust, rot, and disease. The Spark of Virtue enacts the ultimate magical girl miracle by inverting revulsion into breathtaking purification: her touch neutralizes virulent supernatural plagues, transmutes toxic waste into blooming spring jasmine, and reflects the cruel gaze of medusa-like villains back upon themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu (The Raptors / Sky-Hunters):</b> Embodying the blinding terror of the scorching heavens and inescapable aerial raptors. Transformed, she unfurls gleaming starlight wings, soaring above city skylines to rain down pinpoint solar lances and dispel mystical darkness with blinding dawn brilliance.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Heroic Feeding: Inverting the Five Hungers</b></span><br /> <br /> Standard Beasts feed on the terror of innocent humans to satisfy their Horror's hunger. The Magical Girl binds her appetite to a strict superheroic code, hunting only the wicked:<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger for the Hoard (The Collector):</b> Rather than stealing cherished family heirlooms from vulnerable mortals, she raids occult black markets, seizing cursed grimoires, stolen reliquaries, and dangerous relics to seal them safely away in her Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger for Power (The Tyrant):</b> Rather than bullying the weak, she humbles arrogant supernatural despots, toppling tyrannical vampire Princes, corrupt corporate executives, and abusive cult leaders by breaking their authority in public displays of righteous defiance.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger for Prey (The Predator):</b> The classic superhero stalker. She spends her nights patrolling foggy alleyways, hunting down predatory slashers, human traffickers, and rogue werewolves who prey on runaway youths, satisfying her Horror in the thrill of the chase.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger for Punishment (The Nemesis):</b> Acting as an avenging judge. She targets unrepentant abusers and criminals who have escaped conventional justice, forcing them into psychological labyrinths where they experience the terrifying weight of their own misdeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger for Ruin (The Ravager):</b> The demolitions specialist. Instead of vandalizing civilian neighborhoods, she unleashes her destructive fury on demonic Infrastructure, clandestine genetic labs, and supernatural sweatshops, reducing the strongholds of evil to smoking rubble.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. The Lair as the Magical Girl Secret Base</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Sanctifying the Nightmare Realm:</b> Every Beast possesses a personal domain in the Primordial Dream known as a <b>Lair</b>. For normal Beasts, the Lair is a horrific subterranean cavern filled with primal traps. The Magical Girl, linked through the Heart-Weave, transforms her Lair into the team\u2019s enchanted headquarters: a luminous astral clubhouse, crystalline sunken palace, or floating sky-citadel.<br /> <br /> <b>Kinship and the Extended Sisterhood:</b> Beast mechanics natively center on <b>Kinship</b>\u2014the instinctual realization that other monsters are cousins. In a multi-splat magical girl squad, the Beast acts as the foundational emotional heart. Through abilities like <i>Family Dinner</i>, she can sate her Horror simply by assisting her werewolf or vampire teammates on their noble missions, while her Lair provides an impenetrable sanctuary where the entire circle can hide, heal, and plan their next battle.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Subverting the &quot;Hero&quot; Tropes</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Exposing the Narcissistic Antagonist:</b> In *Beast: The Primordial*, canonical &quot;Heroes&quot; are not noble saviors; they are narcissistic, obsessive vigilantes driven by toxic delusions of grandeur, slaughtering misunderstood beings to validate their own egos. This dynamic creates a brilliant deconstruction of the genre: the &quot;Monster-Girl&quot; is the true selfless protector, while the self-proclaimed &quot;Hero&quot; in shining armor is an unhinged, violent villain seeking applause.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pedagogical Miracle:</b> When forced to confront these glory-seeking vigilantes, the Magical Girl refuses to stoop to their murderous cruelty. Using her Spark of Virtue and Nightmares, she delivers a shattering lesson in humility, tearing away the Hero\u2019s narcissistic illusions to force them to confront their own pettiness and step off the path of bloodshed.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>6. Mascot Dynamics: The Hatchling Horror</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Tamed Familiar:</b> While elder Beasts are haunted by titanic, uncontrollable Horrors, the Magical Girl\u2019s Mascot is an inverted Empyrean spirit bonded with a baby Soul-Beast\u2014a miniature winged drake, an ivory sea-serpent with big curious eyes, or a fluffy starlight owl.<br /> <br /> <b>The Emotional Balance:</b> The Hatchling acts as an emotional regulator and magical antenna. It feeds on acts of sincere courage, friendship, and justice, using Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to shield the girl's civilian life and <i>Soothing Touch</i> to calm her Satiety, ensuring that her inner dragon remains a loyal partner in the defense of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-30-2026, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T01:33:20-07:00","id":1565060,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Deviant Magical Girl: The Bio-Mechanical Liberator</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, the Remade Magical Girl directly embodies the dark-magical-girl subgenre of involuntary modification, laboratory weaponization, and corporate exploitation. Rather than receiving a wondrous celestial gift, she was chemically butchered, cybernetically grafted, or gene-spliced by a shadowy conspiracy to serve as a disposable living weapon. Her magical girl transformation is the ultimate act of bodily reclamation: using the <i>Transformation Compact</i> and the <i>Spark of Virtue</i> to master her bodily trauma, turning her agonizing mutations into a righteous shield for the vulnerable.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>1. The Transformation Sequence: The Bio-Mechanical Chassis</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Surgical Chassis Filter:</b> Deviant mechanics center on the brutal, disfiguring push-and-pull between <b>Variations</b> (powers) and <b>Scars</b> (crippling physiological and social drawbacks). Normally, activating a high-magnitude Variation inflicts agonizing bodily damage, flesh-bleeding, or violent physical warping. The Compact functions as an energetic <b>Surgical Chassis</b>: during her magical sequence, it absorbs the traumatic feedback of her Scars, venting kinetic friction into sparkling flares, hard-light seams, and polished porcelain armor plates that conceal her surgical horror behind storybook majesty.<br /> <br /> <b>Scars as Magical Girl Tropes:</b> Canonical Deviant Scars map directly onto classic magical girl dramatic constraints:<br /> <i>Depletion / Cooldown:</i> The strict &quot;battery limit&quot; or time-limit countdown before her magical form powers down.<br /> <i>Involuntary Transformation:</i> Transforming uncontrollably whenever intense stress, trauma, or emotional triggers spike.<br /> <i>Perilous / Maintenance:</i> Requiring a verbal incantation, dedicated focus, or an external device (her wand or compact) to lock down her unstable powers without suffering internal backlash.<br /> <i>Bane:</i> A vulnerability to specific corporate frequencies, cryogenic chemicals, or the sound of the lab sirens that accompanied her Divergence.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>2. Loyalty Touchstones &amp; The Unbroken Will</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue via Loyalty &amp; Catharsis:</b> The Divergence shatters the soul, eradicating native human Virtue and Vice and replacing them with **Loyalty** and **Conviction** Touchstones. A standard Deviant is consumed by Conviction\u2014a bitter, self-destructive thirst for revenge against her creators. The Magical Girl inverts this: she anchors herself entirely to **Loyalty Touchstones** (her cohort sisters, school friends, and innocent civilians). When her Loyalty exceeds her Conviction, she enters **Catharsis**, becoming a protective **Guardian**.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbroken Will in Play:</b> Through the Starlight Compact's *Unbroken Will* dynamic, her earnest sincerity grants an automatic +2 bonus on all rolls to control or suppress **Instability** whenever she acts in direct defense of an innocent. Defending others literally keeps her broken body and soul from falling apart.<br /> <br /> <b>Preventing the Feral Collapse:</b> When an ordinary Remade runs out of Stability, she cascades into biological degradation or becomes a mindless, mutating **Feral**. The Heart-Weave provides collective emotional ballast: the shared warmth and unconditional acceptance of her magical girl team halts Erosion, allowing her to survive without losing her mind.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>3. Clade Aesthetics: From Lab Experiment to Magical Heroine</b></span><br /> <br /> A Remade\u2019s Clade dictates the aesthetic and mechanical texture of her heroic persona:<br /> <br /> <b>Cephalist (The Psychic Esper):</b> The mind-altered test subject. Clad in floating prism-glass tiaras and geometric hard-light halos, she channels psychokinetic barriers, telepathic squad links, and sensory radars, neutralizing foes through pure mental grace rather than messy physical violence.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimeric (The Beast/Bio-Hybrid):</b> The spliced experiment. Rather than manifesting grotesque animal tumors, the Compact refines her beast-DNA into elegant magical girl motifs: gilded falcon wings, iridescent butterfly antennae, or prehensile floral vines that entangle foes and safely catch falling civilians.<br /> <br /> <b>Coactive (The Radiant Conduit):</b> The irradiated particle-battery. Bombarded with quantum currents or toxic fallout, she channels her unstable internal reactor into sparkling starlight ribbons and non-lethal solar beam-strikes, absorbing hazardous energy leaks to protect bystanders.<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive (The Cyber-Valkyrie):</b> The modified cyborg. Flesh fused with invasive hardware is overlaid with sleek porcelain plate, modular weapon-gauntlets, and hard-light shields, deploying starlight cannons or plasma wands directly from her prosthetic arms.<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant (The Unbroken Rebel):</b> Aberrant biology that violently rejected the intended modifications. Her costume shifts dynamically during battle, generating spontaneous metabolic immunities or crystalline bone-armor in response to enemy strikes.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4. Narrative Engine: Liberating the &quot;Devoted&quot; &amp; Smashing Labs</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Tragedy of the Devoted:</b> Her most emotionally fraught recurring nemeses are the **Devoted**\u2014brainwashed, captive magical girls kept on chemical or psychological leashes by the Conspiracy. While other anti-heroes would simply execute them, the Magical Girl\u2019s mission is pedagogical and redemptive: she uses her Spark of Virtue to break their behavioral conditioning, rescue them from the operating table, and welcome them into her Circle.<br /> <br /> <b>Infiltrating the Web of Pain:</b> Deviant campaigns revolve around dismantling the **Web of Pain**. Rather than brooding in hideouts, the Magical Girl squad conducts daring nighttime raids against corporate research facilities, clandestine black-sites, and corrupt pharmaceutical front-companies, liberating caged test subjects and shattering the Linchpins of the Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>5. Mascot Dynamics: The Lab-Rescue Chimera</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Escaped Companion:</b> While sinister corporations hunt her with tracking hounds, her Mascot is an inverted Empyrean entity that has bonded with an escaped laboratory animal\u2014a winged lab mouse, an albino cyber-ferret, or a glowing kitten saved from the vivisection table.<br /> <br /> <b>Stabilization &amp; Electronic Jamming:</b> The Mascot feeds on genuine acts of healing, mutual liberation, and preserved human loyalty. In combat, it acts as an encrypted communications relay and medical scout, using Numina like <i>Beacon of Sanctuary</i> to scramble Conspiracy telemetry and <i>Soothing Touch</i> to purge biological toxicity and stabilize her Scars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-30T01:41:59-07:00","id":1565061,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>The Starlight Compact: The Luminaria</b></span> <br /> Across the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and the framework of the <i>Contagion Chronicle</i>, the Starlight Compact stands as a revolutionary Sworn faction dedicated to the proposition that cynicism, emotional detachment, and isolation are the primary vectors through which cosmic decay and supernatural rot fester. Where competing factions treat the Contagion as broken machinery to be patched in secret, a moral sin to be scourged, or a military crisis to be suppressed with cold violence, the Luminaria take the opposite stance: earnest idealism and unshielded vulnerability are the ultimate metaphysical anchors capable of healing reality itself.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Foundational Initiation &amp; System Integration</b></span><br /> <br /> To operate as a unified circle, every member of the Compact integrates two essential capabilities into their existence. <br /> <br /> Through the <b>Transformation Merit</b>, operatives manifest a stylized, empowered battle regalia. Beyond granting mystical and physical enhancements, this sequence projects an identity shield that protects civilian Touchstones, schools, and families from supernatural retaliation, allowing operatives to maintain genuine, loving connections in their ordinary lives without exposing innocents to the crosshairs of predatory monsters.<br /> <br /> Through the <b>Mascot Merit</b>, the circle bonds with an enlightened, sapient ephemeral guide. The Mascot acts as a living emotional antenna, knitting the squad\u2019s friendship into a permanent sympathetic network known as the <b>Heart-Weave</b>. Most crucially, the Mascot actively neutralizes ambient horror and supernatural revulsion\u2014calming the predatory friction of the Beast, buffering the toxic rejection of Disquiet, and dulling the madness of Lunacy\u2014so that vampires, werewolves, mages, and mortals can stand side by side in deep emotional intimacy without tearing each other apart.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Vector: Resonance</b></span><br /> <br /> The unique Sworn discipline of the Compact is <b>Vector: Resonance</b>, a power suite that directly translates mutual trust, conviction, and vulnerability into tangible hard-light barriers, synchronized finishing maneuvers, and reality-altering sanctuaries.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Unvarnished Heart:</b> By spending Willpower to speak or act with complete, unshielded emotional honesty, the operative outlines nearby illusions, disguises, and Contagious corruption in soft starlight, stripping away enemy stealth while bolstering allies with a +2 bonus to resist terror, panic, and mental Tilts. Within distinct supernatural lineages, this honesty fuels survival: it restores Glamour and Satiety, grants a +2 bonus on Risking Willpower and controlling Instability, restores Cover or Plasm, and buffers Harmony against sudden degeneration.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Validation of Dreams:</b> Whenever an ally admits a vulnerable truth, expresses an earnest ambition, or makes a personal sacrifice, the operative reflexively validates that aspiration. The ally receives a +2 bonus to all rolls made in pursuit of that ideal for the scene, and fulfilling the goal immediately awards an Experience Beat across the entire Mascot network.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Sincere Conduit:</b> The operative radiates an expanding aura of pure starlight. Any hostile supernatural power within this field that relies on terror, despair, mind control, or emotional coercion immediately triggers a Clash of Wills against the operative\u2019s Conviction plus Mascot rating. If the operative prevails, the hostile effect shatters completely, and allies within the field add her Conviction score to their Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Harmonized Heartstrike:</b> When at least two operatives sharing a Mascot synchronize their armaments through the hub, they channel their collective emotional bond into a devastating team finisher. This coordinated strike inflicts massive direct damage against corrupted entities while remaining entirely harmless to bystanders and civilian architecture.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Dawn of the Unbroken Heart:</b> The ultimate expression of hope over cosmic despair requires three or more operatives and a powerful Mascot to manifest a shimmering dome of starlight spanning hundreds of yards. Within this sanctuary, early stages of Contagion are permanently purged from mortals and allies, infected Infrastructure collapses into inert dust, and hostiles suffer continuous Aggravated damage each turn. Any member who makes a vulnerable emotional sacrifice within the dome gains the Rote Quality on all actions for the chapter, while the entire circle completely refills their Willpower pools.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Macro-Societal Role in the Chronicles</b></span><br /> <br /> The Starlight Compact operates as an indispensable diplomatic bridge across the fractured, paranoid politics of the World of Darkness. In a setting defined by ancient hierarchies, territorial isolation, and cold survivalism, the Luminaria serve as a living proof of concept: that across all monster lineages, choosing to care without armor can actively drive back the horrors of the night and redeem a broken world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-31T06:52:19-07:00","id":1565065,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Magical Girl Heroes, the thing to remember is that Beast is problematic. It has a subtext of apologetics for predators; and part of that subtext is that in the game, anyone who might call the Beasts out get lumped in with &quot;narcissistic low-Integrity Heroes&quot;. The thing is, the Storytelling section outright admits that they're putting their thumb on the scale:<i> &quot;The reasonable, caring, 'good' Heroes don't make much of an appearance in Beast, not because they don't exist, but because the narrative role for the Hero in Beast is that of a violent, narcissistic antagonist.&quot; </i>Even in Beast as written, there are in theory Heroes who aren't narcissistic creeps; they just get ignored because they don't fit Beast's intended narrative. <br /> <br /> The real problem with a Magical Girl Hero isn't the low Integrity or the narcissistic portrayal, as magical girls played straight would definitely match exactly the &quot;exceptions&quot; that absolutely exist. The problem is that the Hero powers are too limited, in that they are all things that only involve opposing Beasts. You would have to house rule Heroes to have more broadly useful abilities, or focus the Hero Magical Girl solely on battling Beasts. <br /> <br /> (This narrow scope would be understandable if not for the fact that Beast is built with crossovers in mind; so it's not like the narrow scope is because the game doesn't consider how other supernaturals factor in. Rather, it explicitly excludes non-Beasts from being subject to a Hero's powers.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-31T08:00:49-07:00","id":1565066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1479169-have-you-guys-ever-made-a-deviant-the-renegades-character-based-on-magical-girls?p=1565065#post1565065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Magical Girl Heroes, the thing to remember is that Beast is problematic. It has a subtext of apologetics for predators; and part of that subtext is that in the game, anyone who might call the Beasts out get lumped in with &quot;narcissistic low-Integrity Heroes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast does not defend what Beasts do to feed their Hunger and its moral issue with Heroes has always been that the Heroes who serve as antagonists primarily <i>don't care</i> if the Begotten they hunt have done anything to deserve death, with a side order of &quot;it is extremely difficult to feel okay about someone whose primary threat is that they can put a folkloric-nonsense curse on you based on what they think you are that may directly affect your ability to behave normally, which does not go away until you are dead, depressively isolated from your magical nature in a way that requires being near death to recover from, or hungry to the point of dramatic escalation whose most expedient means of resolution is to kill the person who cursed you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the Horror doesn't care if the Beast's victims learn anything, Heroes in the modern era do not have powers that given them extra insight into the larger picture that would make the unconscious biases that steer them have any consistent connection to reality \u2014 Heroic Tracking and the subsequent activity only cares, at root, about whether a Beast's activities (or inactivity) have disturbed the Primordial Dream, and the issues the Begotten encounter with Heroes stem from the fact that the Heroes who are trying to kill them do not recognize this and will often come up with whatever arbitrary justification they can think of to explain why the Beast has to die. They are a warped magical-social immune response attached to the kind of person whose self-image is bad enough to think their ability to perceive the ripples of supernatural trauma makes them the main character of a monster-killing narrative.<br /> <br /> The gameline does not &quot;lump in anyone who might call the Beasts out with Heroes&quot; because it does not concern itself with anyone &quot;calling the Beasts out.&quot; The splat's primary social lubricant is only magical in the sense that it comes from shared magical qualities and goes away with the same things that sour a regular good impression and half the Satiety Conditions and Family Ties revolve their roleplaying considerations around the Beast becoming isolated or cut off from people close to them. <br /> <br /> Beast has no more subtext of apologetics for predators than Vampire does and I'd love if we could stop pretending otherwise ten years into the line's existence just because the Kickstarter draft fumbled major parts of its presentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (This narrow scope would be understandable if not for the fact that Beast is built with crossovers in mind; so it's not like the narrow scope is because the game doesn't consider how other supernaturals factor in. Rather, it explicitly excludes non-Beasts from being subject to a Hero's powers.) </div> </div> </div>It also explicitly presents a Heroic Gift that extends much of the benefits of their abilities as Beast-specific antagonists to characters with Family Ties to a Beast, i.e. supernatural characters for which a Hero is a reasonable antagonist to be involved with without extenuating circumstances that have little to do with Heroes in general. Considering Dark Eras 2's material on Oracles/Heroes from before the signal-to-noise ratio got quite so bad gives their powerset a number of adjustments including having a Virtue and Vice instead of a Life and Legend and effectively giving a modified version of an existing Gift to let them place Anathema in place of their ability to recruit Followers.<br /> <br /> The problem with magical girl Heroes is the same problem as with magical girl Huntsmen or magical girl Strix, i.e. they are designed as antagonists whose powerset exists to specifically make trouble for one type of monster first and their ability to be a threat outside of that context is dramatically more limited \u2014 setting aside conditional bonuses like Vanquisher's Strength, Champion's Endurance, and Warrior's Speed that Kinslayer can extend to conflict with all tagged monsters, Gifts mostly work by shutting down or bypassing the advantages a Beast has from having a Lair or expanding their ability to place Anathema, and the nature of how Heroes get stronger is such that for practical purposes higher-Lair Begotten treat experienced Heroes as insidious threats to their autonomy and an extra escalatory pressure valve for if they fail at operational security for feeding their Hunger rather than as direct threats, just like the Strix and the Huntsmen engender paranoia in their respective targets and the societies they inhabit by being able to shapeshift, steal bodies, make it look like someone else is possessed, skirt the boundaries of magical restrictions on their master's activity, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast notwithstanding, treating &quot;magical girl&quot; as a template to be applied to any playable monster type also sort of runs into the problem of not all gamelines' protagonist kits assuming the same sociopolitical placement as each other \u2014 a mummy and a vampire (and to a lesser extent a werewolf) both occupy a position where they are more likely to be the power source for characters who would be more appropriate to the broad idiom of mahou shoujo like ghouls, Wolf-Blooded, and Inheritors, and the isolation and potential direct fugitive status of Prometheans and the Unchained brings a degree of personal antagonism to the things that are after them that seldom directly gels with the genre's focuses. Given that this thread is still nominally about Deviant, it may be prudent to approach this as though it were one or more universal Lesser Forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Separately, I notice there's a couple unsigned references to capital-S Subroutines in the Demon post and I don't know what that's actually referring to. Is there a homebrew post or STV product that those are from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-31T12:06:01-07:00","id":1565067,"title":"","content":"The thing is, none of these magical girls requires that the underlying supernatural type be modified, per se. So whether you want to use Greater/Lesser Forms or full templates, it doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}